JERUSALEM (Reuters) - The Israeli military said on Wednesday that its warplanes had bombed Syrian army infrastructure overnight in response to missile launches from the country. This is according to the release by the APF news agency on January 31, 2024.
However, no details have been provided on the deaths and injuries caused by the attacks in southern Syria.
During more than a decade of civil war in Syria, Israel has launched hundreds of airstrikes, mainly targeting Iranian-backed forces as well as Syrian army positions. Such attacks have intensified since the start of the war between Israel and the Palestinian Hamas movement on October 7.
The Syrian Observatory for Human Rights says Israeli airstrikes in Syria killed eight people on Monday, including militants loyal to Iran. Violence also erupted along the Israeli-Lebanese border, with almost daily shootings between Israel and Hezbollah, an ally of the Iranian-backed Hamas.
Photo from AFP Leaked letter: Mr. Teav Vannul instructed the elected Commune / Sangkat Councilors to listen only to the candlelight party, not to listen to others, analysts say that this letter shows a direct attack on Mr. Sam Rainsy
(Phnom Penh): On January 31, 2024, a letter from Mr. Teav Vannul, President of the Candlelight Party, was leaked on various social media, in which he introduced the Chairman of the Capital-Provincial Party Executive Committee and members of the group. Commune / Sangkat councilors elected from the Candlelight Party should listen to the instructions of the Candlelight Party only and must not listen to any politician or party.
On social media, analysts saw that Teav Vannul's letter appeared to be a direct attack on Sam Rainsy, a foreign politician who called for the Lantern Party to unite with the Nationalist Party, which is splitting the Lantern Party.
On social media, Mr. Sam Rainsy on January 29, 2024 called on all representatives of the democratic forces in Cambodia to unite and work together to promote democracy, stating that there are currently three political parties representing It is the democratic forces that have supporters from the same source: the Candlelight Party, the National Forces Party and the Khmer Will Party.
Through this message, Mr. Teav Vannul confirmed the following 4 points:
1. The Candlelight Party is the only political party that has the authority to control and protect the 2,198 elected Commune / Sangkat Councilors from the Candlelight Party.
2. No other political party or political figure can come to force or advise the members of the Commune / Sangkat Council elected from the Candlelight Party, even in any regional constituency to vote for any political party. Other than the Khmer Will Party.
3: The Candlelight Party has already decided to select the only Khmer Will Party to register the political party and the list of candidates for the 5th Senate election in 2024.
4: Candlelight Party requires all members to remain loyal to the party and continue to actively implement the party's work in accordance with the party's bylaws, internal regulations, decisions and guidelines.
It should be noted that recently, the Candlelight Party and the National Forces Party, a new opposition political movement, have attacked each other, with the Candlelight Party considering that the National Strength Party has dragged its forces at the grassroots level.
