The following is the message from Samdech Krom Preah Norodom Chakrapong: The Ministry of Economy promotes the modernization and opening of the social protection system in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Pen Sophea, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chair of the Executive Committee of the National Council for Social Protection, on the morning of January 31, 2024, presided over the opening ceremony of the seminar on modernization. Open Social Security Benefit Package in Cambodia at Raffles Royal Hotel Phnom Penh.
The workshop was attended by representatives of relevant ministries and institutions, the National Bank of Cambodia, private banks, and development partners, as well as relevant civil society organizations.
Please be informed that "Government Open Benefit Package 4th Generation or G2P 4.0" is another important step in the digital social protection agenda that the social protection system, especially the social assistance system, is currently operating. Open benefits package through G2P 2.0 protocol, which is enabled between one social protection operator to another payment service provider.
In line with international best practice, building an integrated benefit package delivery system in line with G2P 4.0 protocol can enable all social protection operators to access benefit packages through multiple remittance providers that may Provide more flexibility and convenience to beneficiaries as well as enhance the financial environment in Cambodia.
The study and development of concept documents and roadmaps for the development of integrated integration packages in accordance with the G2P 4.0 approach have been assessed by international experts and the World Bank as an important role in enhancing efficiency. , Environment, and financial accountability, especially the flow of benefits in the provision of benefits in the social assistance system and the social security system in Cambodia.
Please be reminded that in the past, the Royal Government, which has the National Social Protection Council as its staff, has supported the digital social protection agenda by setting out ideas and initiatives in three main stages: Phase 1. Construction of Social Protection Registration Database, Phase 2 Construction of a digital nursery for the provision of social protection services, and the third phase. Building an integrated ecosystem.
Currently, the implementation of the first phase has been remarkably successful through the integration of the pilot joint registration system and is being continuously expanded in line with the strategic plan for digital transformation in a social protection system. Specific.
