(Phnom Penh): Duke Leng Navatra, Chairman of the Board of the Galaxy Navatra Group, urges all students studying at the University of Digital Cambodia to make an effort to focus on English for the first year. To be the basis for "Digital" research.
The Duke says that the English language needs to be standardized in order to educate students on basic knowledge, increase students' ability to speak, listen, read and write as capital for personal communication and to serve the needs of the profession and the field. Other.
Duke said that learning English fluently is important in developing the quality of a long-term digital career, as digital has been evolving rapidly over the years. During the meeting with more than 3,000 students, Duke Leng Navatra also shared his experience with many students as a basis for future life as well as study.
Please be informed that in order to meet the needs of the market and the economy in the digital age, Digital University of Cambodia has launched a special curriculum that focuses on training digital subjects in accordance with the standards of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
(Phnom Penh): General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, this morning, January 30, 2024, in the meeting to review and tighten the road traffic law 2023 and to further guide the traffic police force to continue the campaign. Strict road traffic laws, especially alcohol control on drivers of all types of vehicles to reduce traffic accidents.
Through the recent campaign in Phnom Penh, General Sar Thet claimed that the rate of traffic accidents has decreased compared to the previous period of the campaign to tighten traffic laws and check alcohol on drivers. The general said that the campaign to control alcohol could not be withdrawn.
General Sar Thet said, "In the past few days, due to the direction of the President's order, we have personally ordered His Excellency Chuon Narin to launch a campaign to control alcohol." "As a result, in Phnom Penh there is a reduction in the number of accidents, which means we are on the right track."
According to the General Commissioner of the National Police, the enforcement of traffic laws to control alcohol on the driver is to protect the lives of the people or to eliminate anarchy, disobedience to traffic laws. The general added that in the future, any capital-province that continues to increase the number of traffic accidents will be convened separately for further experiments.
In addition to preventing and preventing traffic accidents, General Sar Thet emphasized that the enforcement of traffic laws, especially at night, led to the prevention of drug offenses, gangsters, criminal offenses, just released from prison. Therefore, this work can not be done for a period of time, that is, it must be carried out continuously without prior notice.
At the same time, General Sar Thet also instructed all police officers when enforcing traffic laws to use behavior, use words and eliminate other inactivity to avoid criticism from the people. However, the law enforcement force must apply strictly and without exception to those who obstruct the authorities.
The Board of Directors of the National Social Assistance Fund is committed to the successful implementation of the Royal Government's Social Assistance Plan.
(Phnom Penh): The Board of Directors of the National Social Assistance Fund has expressed its high commitment to the successful and better implementation of the Royal Government's Social Assistance Plan led by His Excellency Hun Manet.
This commitment was made at the board meeting of the National Social Assistance Fund on Monday, January 29, 2024. The meeting was chaired by Mr. Sunivong Viseth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and Chairman of the Board of the National Social Assistance Foundation.
In the above meeting, Mr. Sunivong Viseth, as well as a member of the Board of Directors of the National Social Assistance Foundation, expressed his high commitment to implement all the tasks related to the National Social Assistance Plan to achieve better results.
This program is designed to officially announce the transformation of the Skills Development Fund Management Pilot Project into a permanent institution (Trust Fund) and to present the achievements and new programs of the Skills Development Fund in order to strengthen and expand development. Skills to meet the needs of the private sector, as well as the signing of memoranda of understanding with strategic partners and award programs for partners who are actively involved in skills development.
It should be noted that the Skills Development Fund was initially initiated and established as a pilot project by the Ministry of Economy and Finance in March 2018 with the aim of testing new and innovative mechanisms to mobilize, manage and allocate resources for the purpose of strengthening And expand skills development to meet the needs of the private sector and national social and economic development.
The Skills Development Fund (SDF) has the vision of becoming the most credible financing center for skills development to meet the needs of the private sector effectively and sustainably to contribute to achieving the Royal Government's 2030 and 2050 vision.
In addition, the SDF has set out a mission to promote a real partnership between the private sector and training institutions to design and implement quality skills training programs that meet the needs of the private sector and socio-economic development. In a proactive spirit to participate in strengthening and expanding skills development and problem solving in the ecosystem, SDF will continue to develop new and more innovative support programs.
In addition, three MoU signing ceremonies were held, including:
Meanwhile, speaking at the closing ceremony, Dr. Phan Phalla called on the private sector, factories, enterprises and training institutions to continue to organize skills training programs that meet specific needs to be submitted to the SDF.
