WASHINGTON (Reuters) - Waiting for US action to retaliate against an enemy drone strike that left three US soldiers dead and 34 wounded on the Syrian-Jordanian border remains unclear. 48 hours have passed. The president of the United States has said he will retaliate. How will revenge attacks be carried out?
Washington faces complex challenges
The United States already has its military options in place at all times. These military options were developed by the US Department of Defense with the inclusion of intelligence from the CIA and the National Security Agency. The military options will be presented to the US National Security Council and policymakers, with the president making the final decision and signing the chosen process.
Option 1: Attacks on Iranian allies and commanders
Option 2: Attack on Iran
* Option 3: Not responding
