UNRWA has 13,000 employees in the Gaza Strip. More than a dozen countries, including major donors, the United States and Germany, have suspended their funding for the agency following reports of its involvement. Photo by Reuters Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth Labor to industry based on skills and continue to develop modern industry
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, said on January 30, 2024 that the Cambodian economy is moving from a labor-intensive industry to a skills-based industry and continues to develop modern industries.
This statement was made on the occasion that Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth presided over the official inauguration of the Skills Development Fund (SDF) under the theme "Skills Development, Business Development, Personal Development" organized by the Ministry of Economy. And Finance on January 30, 2024.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth stated that "the Cambodian economy has been moving from a labor-intensive industry to a skills-based industry and continues to develop modern industries based on technology and knowledge."
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth said that in this context, skills development plays an increasingly important role in enhancing the capacity, competitiveness and living standards of the Cambodian people, as well as meeting the huge needs of the low, medium and high skilled labor force. And the needs of investors in both quality and quantity.
This requires the active and proactive spirit of all stakeholders, both in the supply and demand sectors (especially the private sector), to join forces as a whole, intertwined and complementary. To achieve the strategic goals set by the Royal Government. This is an additional confirmation.
He said that based on the proactive spirit and response to the insistence of relevant partners, especially the private sector and development partners, the Ministry of Economy and Finance has studied and evaluated the situation of supply and demand in the ecosystem with development partners, the private sector. And relevant ministries and institutions based on international and regional trends and norms and including the Cambodian context.
As a result, the Ministry of Economy and Finance initiated, developed and implemented a pilot project to manage this Skills Development Fund management mechanism in March 2018. This is the emphasis of Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth also gave recommendations to ministries, institutions, development partners and the private sector in charge of professional development as follows:
First, request the participation and cooperation of all relevant partners from all relevant institutions, including the Royal Government, the private sector and development partners to be a major driving force in achieving the development of Cambodian human capital with knowledge, skills. , Attitudes, and Professional Ethics in Accordance with the "Pentagon Strategy Phase I" Under the Clever and Talented Leadership of His Majesty Hun Manet.
Second, request the Skills Development Fund to continue to improve the quality of services and efficiency of the management and allocation of the Fund's resources in order to enhance the trust and participation of stakeholders in the development of skills that are the real needs of the private sector.
Third, request the Skills Development Fund to start considering and studying the financing model for the medium and long term in order to ensure the efficiency and sustainability of financing to support the skills development of the people of Cambodia to meet the needs of the private sector. And the needs of socio-economic development.
Fourth, request the Skills Development Fund to continue to organize more new programs to meet the needs of the private sector, as well as support key policies of the Royal Government.
Fifth, request the Skills Development Fund to study the current and future skills needs necessary for economic and social development.
Sixth, request the Digital Development Skills Development Fund to add to its operations to increase efficiency, strengthen quality and ensure transparency and trust in the management and distribution of funds.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mai Hong Sreang, a former member of the Board of Directors of the Candlelight Party, confirmed that the leaders of the Candlelight Party are all immoral, truthful, a group of people hungry for power, dictatorship and partisanship.
May Hong Sreang's remarks came after he saw that the Candlelight Party's politics did not have clear principles, did not have a proper strategy for democracy, but only went beyond the red line of democracy. And made himself a criminal, made himself a prisoner, unable to return home.
Mr. Mai Hong Sreang stated that politicians, both domestic and foreign, do politics for themselves, not for the nation as they have memorized. Conflicts of interest see only the policy of the Candlelight Party, which seems very good, but for the poor implementation of the policy, turned to jealousy, jealousy of each other's power and did not participate in the development of society, especially Always criticizing, tearing up, leading to the disintegration of the society and so on.
Mr. Mai Hong Sreang stated: "Do not say that being with the opposition party is called patriotism, the ruling party is also patriotic, it is patriotism that builds the nation from scratch until today, we have achieved peace. Get development under the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen and continue under the leadership of Samdech President Hun Manet.
Mr. Mai Hong Sreang warned the leaders of the Candlelight Party not to accuse the ruling party, including all the leaders of the Candlelight Party, of internal strife because they did not respect the party's stated principles of morality and truth. By not giving young people the opportunity to become leaders in turn.
