The ambassador will work to promote cooperation between the two countries in the fields of trade, people-to-people contacts, as well as education. This statement was made during a meeting on the morning of January 30, 2024 at the National Assembly.
The National Assembly welcomed Dr. Santo Mosumato's diplomatic mission and stressed that the National Assembly is always ready to cooperate with the Embassy of Indonesia to strengthen and deepen the cooperation relations between the two countries. More.
The National Assembly thanked Indonesia for its continued support of Cambodia in all circumstances, from the recognition of Cambodia's independence, the deployment of peacekeeping forces under the auspices of the United Nations in the pursuit of peace for Cambodia and national development. To date, Samdech has also highlighted Indonesia's important role in ASEAN.
National Assembly President Khuon Sodary and the Indonesian Ambassador jointly agreed on the importance of good relations between the two countries and said that Cambodia and Indonesia have many potentials to further strengthen cooperation in the fields of diplomacy, trade and education. Agriculture, tourism, especially people-to-people contacts that will bring benefits to both countries alike.
In February 2024, Indonesia will hold elections for a new parliament. Following the establishment of the new Indonesian National Assembly, Santos Mosumato said he would work to further boost bilateral relations in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks, as well as gender-based cooperation.
