(Phnom Penh): Ms. Hun Dany, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, recommended that the departments under the Ministry and the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism continue to promote women in the tourism sector, because women play an important role in administrative, service, business and hospitality activities.
Secretary of State Hun Dany highlighted the important role of the two working groups in the informal economy and gender equality, which are the staff of the Ministry of Tourism in implementing the Ministry's policies and plans to promote business, livelihood and livelihood. Life aims to make progress, and these jobs also involve a lot of women.
"In the field of tourism, women have played an important role in administrative, service, business and hospitality activities, so we ask the civil servants of the departments under the Ministry of Tourism, as well as in the 25 capital-provincial tourism departments, to continue," she said. "Pay attention to promote more revitalization, especially female civil servants, we also need to strengthen ourselves."
She said that this is due to the important role of women, the Ministry of Tourism considers women as a potential driving force and indispensable stakeholders who actively contribute to improving the living standards of families, communities and Socio-economic, especially the return of national and international tourism growth in 2023.
The Secretary of State also mentioned that the Royal Government of the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly under the leadership of Samdech Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has paid high attention to employment and employment in the informal economy through the introduction of the "Strategy". National Informal Economic Development 2023-2028 ”which aims to enhance the protection, capacity building, productivity and resilience of the informal economy.
In the above meeting, the Secretary of State also presented the implementation plan for 2024 to the General Departments, Departments and Departments of Capital-Province to strengthen the activities within its framework of responsibility and to seek opportunities. To achieve new progress for the Ministry as well as the Royal Government.
Poor young people expect to have a clear job with a decent income after graduating from the beverage business
(Phnom Penh): Poor young people who are studying vocational and technical skills at the National Institute of Entrepreneurship and Innovation hope to be able to work as staff in a coffee shop and be able to open a small cafe on their own after studying Biology and technical expertise of coffee in the next 4 months.
A young woman from Banteay Meanchey province, Ms. Het Reaksa, who is studying professional business in the beverage business at the National Institute of Entrepreneurship and Innovation, said: "It was my first step and then I wanted to open a small cafe on my own."
She explained that she chose this coffee specialty because in Cambodia today, coffee is a popular beverage for Cambodians, so the coffee job market is good today. Learning this coffee business skill, the young woman hopes that she will be able to have a clear job and a decent income that will make her family life better in the future.
Prum Pich, from a poor family in Phnom Penh who is studying beverage business at the National Institute of Entrepreneurship and Innovation, said: “The desire to make coffee is one of my dreams and I hope "Can open a small cafe for myself in the future."
He added that the vocational and technical training program is the only hope for him to learn a clear skill to find a job with a decent income. The young man expects to be able to save the family life better than now, as the family is poor and his parents are getting older day by day.
He also highlighted that the vocational and technical training program for young people from poor and vulnerable families, which was officially launched on November 14, 2023, has taken another step. On January 15, 2024, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training announced the official opening of the school year nationwide.
