(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia said that due to the slow recovery of some sectors, credit growth in Cambodia slowed to 4.8%, the lowest rate in the last two decades. This is according to the report on macroeconomic progress and the banking sector in 2023 and the outlook for 2024 released by the National Bank on January 29, 2024.
The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) said that with the recovery of the economy, the banking system, which continues to dominate the financial sector, has played an active role in supporting key economic sectors, despite the slowdown in credit growth.
"In this situation, a number of prudent provisions have been favored to provide additional opportunities for banking and financial institutions to support sectors in need of financing to sustain and expand investment," the NBC said.
"The delays in implementing the US dollar reserve requirement and other regulations have enabled banking and financial institutions to have an additional $ 1.2 billion in liquidity to lend to priority sectors," the NBC added.
In addition, the banking system has been contributing to the improvement of the women's financial environment and sustainable financing to strengthen women's participation in economic activities and sustainable economic development.
According to the report of the National Bank of Cambodia, as of the first half of 2023, loans provided by banking and financial institutions in the economic sector amounted to 238.7 trillion riels or 57.8 billion US dollars, an increase of 10. 5% compared to the same period in 2022.
