This afternoon, Samdech Thipdey Hun Manet closed the meeting to review the work of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Tuesday, January 30, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, will close the meeting to review the work in 2023 and raise the work direction. 2024 of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
Agriculture is an important sector for the nation and the people of Cambodia. This sector is also considered by the Royal Government led by the Cambodian People's Party.
In order to promote the effective implementation of its work, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has the same mechanism as other ministries: to hold annual meetings to review the performance in the old year and launch the implementation in the next year. New.
On January 25, 2024, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries also held its annual meeting to review the implementation of work in 2023 and launch work for 2024. The conference will last for four days, January 25, 26, 29 and 30.
The meeting was attended by the leaders of the Ministry, the leaders of the General Department, the leaders of the 25 Departments of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the leaders of the Capital and Provinces, and the leaders of the relevant associations in agriculture, forestry and fisheries.
According to the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, based on the achievements in 2023, the agricultural sector will maintain a positive growth of around 1% with a total value added increase of 28,207 billion riels or 4.84. Percentage compared to last year, although the sector has been affected by natural disasters and global crises.
For animal production, supply up to 98% of domestic meat demand. At the same time, private investment in livestock farms, feed mills and modern slaughterhouses has contributed to increasing animal production and improving hygiene and safety for consumers. The implementation of appropriate legal measures and technical measures, especially animal hygiene inspections and products of animal origin, has been continuously promoted.
Prevention and suppression of forest crime, wildlife and deforestation, as well as demarcation of forest lands, the Ministry continues to pay high attention and strengthen good cooperation with relevant ministries, competent authorities and sub-national administrations. The Ministry has been promoting the timber industry and aims to facilitate the import of wood products to reduce the pressure on demand for timber on forest resources.
In particular, cooperation with development partners, including the private sector, is being strengthened and focused on strategic planning, policy, human resource development, and improving support infrastructure as key factors for the agricultural sector.
In addition, various support services have achieved better results in each sector in accordance with the principles and directions of the Royal Government. At the same time, each specialized unit, which is the staff of the Ministry, will continue to implement the policy direction and strategic plan set out for 2024 with a high sense of responsibility.
