(Phnom Penh): Mao Phea and Mao Phearith are young people living in Boeung Char commune, Sambo district, a remote area in Kratie province. Due to lack of livelihood and lack of livelihood, two young brothers and their father decided to cut down trees in Prey Lang, which is adjacent to their commune.
Phea said that his brother and father started logging in Prey Lang in 2013 and had been doing that for about four years.
Both young men and their father have now resigned from the logging business. According to the task force, he resigned because he had been arrested by environmental officials and now that he now has a job in a plantation owned by Sing Bay Otec.
Sing Bay Otec is a company licensed by the Royal Government and cooperates with the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to plant industrial trees such as oil, wind and teak on the area of Boeung Char Forest Extension and Rehabilitation Station in Kratie Province and Province. Stung Treng.
Currently, about 10,000 hectares are cultivated and some of the wood can be cut to make plywood. Through the company's investment, many jobs have been provided to people living in the area.
In addition to the young brothers, Mao Phea and Mao Phearith, many other people who used to cut down trees in Prey Lang came to work for Sing Bay Otec and stopped logging in the forest.
Mao Phea said he was paid about 900,000 rupees a month. Therefore, two siblings are paid 1,800,000 riels. Through this wage, the family life is better. His father no longer struggled to enter the forest, cut down trees, and saved money to buy a motorbike and buy a cow to raise.
Mao Pheara and Mao Phearith saw that Sing Bay Otec's investment in planting trees contributed to providing employment, income and supporting their families and other people to live a decent life. In addition, the investment in planting trees has contributed to people giving up logging activities in Prey Lang.
The two young men called on people who continue to enter Prey Lang to cut down trees to stop their activities and return to work at Sing Bay Otec. Authorities Enforce Road Traffic Law in Chbar Ampov District and Detain a Vehicle Equipped with Lighting
