(Phnom Penh): Mr. Long Naro, Delegate of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the Director General of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, confirmed that in the dry season of 2024, Phnom Penh will no longer face water shortage, as the Water Supply Authority is currently Work to install water mains along Win-Win Road from the base of Prek Pnov Bridge to National Road 4 to ensure adequate water supply in the area.
Speaking to reporters during his inspection of the pipeline work along the Victory Boulevard, Long Naro said that ensuring an adequate water supply was due to the company's ability to produce clean water. Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority produces a lot of water while the water treatment plant is completed.
According to Mr. Long Naro, from the end of February 2024, the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has the capacity to produce more than 1 million cubic meters of water per day, while the current demand is only about 820,000 cubic meters, but the challenge is the lack Loss of water supply vessels, which is why the Authority is working to speed up the work of installing water pipes to supply water throughout Phnom Penh.
However, he pointed out that in some areas there may be low water pressure due to the increase in population living in that area. However, the PPWSA has been preparing to expand further to increase the pressure. If people notice that there is low water pressure in any area, please provide information to the Water Supply Authority so that the Water Supply Authority can solve it in time.
Currently, the people who use clean water in Phnom Penh are about 470 thousand customers. He hopes that by the end of this year, the number of users of clean water will increase by 35,000 more customers.
