The National Bank of Cambodia is committed to maintaining the stability of the riel in order to protect the purchasing power and income of the people.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Chea Serey, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that maintaining the stability of the riel will continue to be an appropriate political option to contribute to maintaining price stability and protecting the purchasing power and income of the people.
This statement was made on the occasion that Dr. Chea Serey presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work results for 2023 and the work direction for 2024 of the National Bank of Cambodia.
Dr. Chea Serey stated that the National Bank of Cambodia will continue to implement monetary policy based on maintaining the exchange rate under the floating exchange rate regime, managing the supply of money at an appropriate level and intervening as necessary. According to the market situation.
In order to maintain the value of the riel, Dr. Chea Serey calls for more active participation in: * Continuing to implement measures to promote the widespread use of the riel from all walks of life * Development of political instruments, monetary, exchange and interbank markets And * Developing a monetary policy framework by establishing a central bank benchmark interest rate to orient the riel interest rate of banking and financial institutions.
The stability of the riel has contributed significantly to stabilizing the purchasing power of the riel as well as consumer income and maintaining overall macroeconomic stability.
Mr. Sok Sabayna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Function and Chairman of the Sub-Committee on Sports Practice Examination Centers, said that this morning, the Examination Organizing Committee explained to all candidates about the three types of sports, including throwing, Long jump and speed, and after covering the procedure, this afternoon began to practice immediately.
