Vietnam and the Philippines claim their respective shares in the South China Sea, but relations are relatively normal compared to those between the Philippines and China over disputed waters. Photo: Reuters Banking and financial institutions have no transactions related to crypto.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Chea Serey, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, stated that the National Bank of Cambodia does not allow banking and financial institutions to conduct transactions related to crypto to prevent risks to the public who may be vulnerable to fraud and loss. Other.
This announcement was made on the occasion that Ms. Dr. Chea Serey presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work results for 2023 and the work direction for 2024 of the National Bank of Cambodia.
"Crypto assets are digital assets with no clear source and high risk, and the National Bank of Cambodia does not allow banking and financial institutions to conduct crypto-related transactions to hedge the public risk," said Dr. Chea Serey. "Can be vulnerable to fraud and other losses."
"Blockchain is a state-of-the-art technology that we can use to develop more efficient, secure and low-cost payment systems, such as the Bakong system, which has become a payment system for facilitating interbank and financial payments," she said. And cross-border payments as well.
Cambodia's payment system has been seizing opportunities and potentials from the advancement of digital technology, which has made payments more efficient, secure and affordable, as well as contributing significantly to improving the financial environment and boosting the economy. Digital in line with the Royal Government's Pentagon strategy.
The National Bank of Cambodia will continue to promote the interoperability and connectivity of payment systems to contribute to improving the financial environment, efficiency of payment systems and regional and global integration, aimed at promoting trade, investment, tourism and remittance activities. From abroad. This is the additional confirmation of Dr. Chea Serey.
"With the innovation of electronic payment systems, we also need to pay more attention to strengthening security, technology and operational risk management to be more efficient and timely to ensure the smooth operation of digital financial services, strengthen trust," she said. Public trust and contribute to maintaining financial stability.
Crypto assets do not have any value that can be determined by a specific mechanism, but the price of crypto assets fluctuates depending on the mood of the buyer and the investor, the opportunist, or even unsubstantiated information on social media. Therefore, buyers of crypto assets face high risks and may reach a complete loss of money.
Ministry of Environment Officially Launches "Local Community Development Strategic Plan (2024-2028)"
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment on the afternoon of January 29, 2024 officially announced the "Local Community Development Strategic Plan (2024-2028)." This strategic plan is prepared by the General Department of Local Communities of the Ministry of Environment.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, representatives of relevant ministries and institutions, as well as leaders of civil servants of the Ministry of Environment, representatives of the capital-provincial administration, development partners and the private sector.
While Cambodia has achieved excellent economic growth, the Ministry of Environment has better fulfilled its roles and responsibilities in four key areas, including: building a modern administration, and second: biodiversity conservation and natural resource management. , 3: Local community development and 4: Promoting sustainable living.
The Ministry of Environment has established 73 protected areas covering an area of approximately 7,046,863 hectares and 193 protected area communities, with 73,149 participating families, 305,621 members managing forest area. 332,108 hectares for biodiversity conservation, natural resource-cultural management, participation in national economic promotion and sustainable local development.
