The Global Peace Federation has been working with leaders around the world who are willing to work together to bring peace to mankind. The Global Peace Federation is not a political party or political party, but values the role that political leaders play in the complex world of governance and international relations. The Global Peace Federation aims to promote global peace beyond religion, race, nation, culture and politics.
The Global Peace Federation acts as a consultative body with the United Nations Economic and Social Council (ECOSOC) and has representative offices in more than 120 countries, including Cambodia.
The Global Peace Federation has more than 50,000 peace ambassadors, including ambassadors / diplomats, religious leaders, civil society leaders, leaders and former leaders of states and governments around the world. Cambodia officially takes over the chairmanship of 77 countries and China at the United Nations Conference on Trade and Development
