Authorities crack down on flooded forest land in 3 areas of nearly 100 hectares in Peam Chkork commune, Chulkiri district
(Kampong Chhnang): Joint forces of Chulkiri District Administrative Unity Command on January 27, 2024 cooperated in cracking down on the crime of clearing flooded forest land in 3 areas of nearly 100 hectares, which was stolen by some crooks. The law even stole the rice because it was on that land.
The land was stolen and taken away by the perpetrator because the above is located at Prek Sdey Dok Kong Toch, next to Prek Phdol, in Kbal Konlong village, Peam Chkork commune, Chulkiri district.
Choul Kiri district governor Dov Kimsin said that the flooded forest land in the three areas at the above point was looted by criminals during the 2023 river season. At that time, the authorities also called some bulldozers to make a contract to stop the clearing and also did not allow the sowing of rice.
However, during the dry season this year, the police went to inspect the flooded forest land in 3 areas at this point, almost 100 hectares were continued to be cleared, and there were also people who stole rice because it was easy to fraudulently take over Also owned. Therefore, on January 27, 2024, the joint authorities of the Chulkiri District Administrative Unity Command cooperated to crack down on this case by not allowing rice to be sown.
In the above case, when the police arrived, they found that almost 10 perpetrators were acting because when they saw the rice, the police fled and the police confiscated 12 sacks of rice seeds, one in each bag. There is a weight of 40 kg on the land above. In particular, a small amount of land has already been stolen because of rice. In this case, the district administration is continuing to crack down and not allow further farming.
The governor of Chulkiri district confirmed that the case of clearing the flooded forest area 3 at this point is against the policy of the Royal Government, suspecting that there are organizers behind which the authorities are investigating to build a case to be sent to court. Continue.
Residents revealed that some of the burglars in the three areas at the above point are suspected to be government officials and some are residents. In this case, the competent authorities and authorities should search for the perpetrators and send them to court to be punished according to the law, so that the crime of encroaching on the flooded forest land of the state as above will no longer occur.
