In the morning of January 28, 2024, the Governor of the Department of Agriculture and Forestry said that during the meeting with the people who suffered from drought and pumping water to save dry rice in Deum Rus commune, Kandal Stung district, Kandal province, on the morning of January 28, 2024. And Provincial Fisheries, the Department of Water Resources, as well as the Kandal Stung District Authority and all stakeholders must pay attention to pumping enough irrigation water to the people.
He said that it is necessary to study how to restore the Stung O canal, which is located in Kandal Stung district, so that the people have enough water and avoid water shortage in the following years.
Mr. Ouch Sao Voeun, Governor of Kandal Stung District, said that in Kandal Stung District, a total of 3,260 families cultivated dry season rice, equivalent to 2,083 hectares, and currently 1,893 hectares are facing water shortage for irrigation Pump water into the field without damaging the rice yet.
