Mr. Chiv Keng shared his sad memories with his relatives, friends and villagers who lived and worked together for 3 years, 8 months and 20 days during the Khmer Rouge regime. Forced Cambodians across the country, including himself, to build dams and dig canals to dry in the sun, in the rain, to starve every day.
