(Phnom Penh): Today, information technology is playing an important role in promoting economic growth and sustainable business development, through which information technology business owners can develop distribution networks, information management and risk management more effectively. To make their business grow.
Understanding the potential and importance of information technology banking, SMEs in Cambodia have encouraged enterprises in this field by developing and launching "Digital and Modernization Financing Projects" to support research and development enterprises. Information technology, including the provision of management services through information technology systems.
Business owners in the technology sector will receive up to 4 billion riels, or about 1 million US dollars, to be used as working capital or investment capital.
This amount of financing will provide up to 70% of the collateral for the soft title or up to 80% of the value of the collateral for the hard title, providing up to 7 years for working capital or 10 years for investment capital.
The enterprises that will receive the concessional financing are small and medium enterprises engaged in business related to digital modern technology in Cambodia, small and medium enterprises with at least 51% Cambodian shareholders. Small and medium enterprises in priority sectors and registered businesses are encouraged. The collateral is land or building.
