It should also be noted that nearly a month ago, farmers in Taing Kork district, Kampong Thom province, faced a shortage of water to irrigate agricultural land during the dry season, so Mr. Hak Mong Huot, Taing Kork district governor, inspected the land. Practically collect information from farmers directly to farmland to find ways to solve water problems in a timely manner.
In addition to solving the problem of irrigation water for farmers, the Governor of Taing Kork District also thanked the Governor of Nguon Rattanak for always paying attention and providing guidance to lower authorities.
He also civil servants, law enforcement forces, local authorities, villages / communes and all colleagues who have overcome all difficulties to facilitate the search for water sources across communes, districts, provinces to make sure to send water to the rice fields of farmers. .
The people in the rice fields are very happy with the timely intervention of the district authorities, especially under the leadership of the district governor Hak Mong Huot, which helped to re-irrigate their rice fields, save rice and other crops. More on time.
As the district authority, Mr. Hak Mong Huot also thanked the local farmers for sharing, so that this joint solution can solve all the concerns of farmers.
