Ministry of Environment announces death of baby elephant in Mondulkiri province and strict measures to continue protection
(Phnom Penh): On January 26, 2024, the ranger of the Department of Environment of Mondulkiri Province, led by Mr. Chea Dara, Deputy Director of the Department, found a dead 7-month-old baby elephant weighing 200 kg in Chi Klop village, Sok San commune. Koh Nhek District, Mondulkiri Province. The team cooperated with the Koh Nhek District Police Inspectorate to autopsy the bodies of the dead elephants.
According to a press release issued on January 27, 2024, the Ministry of Environment said that the team inspected the sharp wounds in the lower part of the chest, but the police did not find the bullet in the animal. . The team has been continuing to inspect the scene to find more evidence.
The Ministry of Environment strongly regrets the loss of this rare species in Cambodia's protected areas and condemns the perpetrators of the protected area law. The Ministry of Environment calls on the relevant authorities and citizens to search for evidence and arrest the perpetrators and prosecute them in accordance with the law.
