China cuts reserve requirement ratio to boost growth
BEIJING: China has said it will reduce its reserve requirement ratio for banks within two weeks and has announced the introduction of more economic support measures. This is a rare early announcement that shows the growing urgency across the government of President Xi Jinping to strengthen the economy and prevent stock market declines.
Hours after the announcement, Chinese regulators introduced further measures to boost the declining real estate and stock markets. These regulators have expanded the use of commercial real estate loans for developers to help them repay other debts and boosted shares in China and Hong Kong, signaling steps toward deepening financial ties with the company. Hong Kong.
