MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russian President Vladimir Putin said on Friday that a Russian military plane that crashed near the border with Ukraine on Wednesday had been shot down by Ukrainian forces. It is not clear whether the shooting was intentional or by mistake. This was released by Reuters on Saturday, January 27, 2024.
Ukraine did not acknowledge or deny Russia's allegations, but protested Russia's claims about the identity of the occupants and what happened. Kiev acknowledged on Wednesday that a POW exchange was planned, but Russia did not give advance notice that there would be the same airstrikes as previously done, Moscow said. That it informed Ukraine in advance.
In his first comment on the incident, Putin said: "I do not know for sure whether they (Ukraine) did it (shot down) intentionally or by mistake What is clear is that they are the perpetrators. "However, it is a crime, whether by negligence or intentional."
BANGKOK: Thai Prime Minister Setha Thaksin Shinawatra said on Wednesday that he believed the Thai economy was in crisis and that the government would introduce more stimulus measures in addition to cash stimulus programs.
"I confirm that the economy is not doing well and is in crisis," Setha, who is also finance minister, was quoted by the Bangkok newspaper as saying. He added that it would not matter if the Bank of Thailand (BoT) did not agree with his view.
The Thai government this week cut its 2024 growth forecast to 2.8 percent from a previous estimate of 3.2 percent due to lower exports and a drop in foreign tourist arrivals. .
Former real estate tycoon Setha, who became prime minister, told the central bank chief that high rates were hurting businesses and prompted the central bank to cut its one-decade-high interest rate by 2.5 percent. According to the Bangkok Post, car sales in 2024 are expected to grow by around 15% due to demand, while new cars are expected to grow at a faster pace.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Soeun Dara, Executive Director of the Automobile Industry Federation of Cambodia (CAIF), confirmed that the Automobile Industry Federation of Cambodia has forecast that car sales in 2024 will increase by around 15% due to demand. Cars of Cambodians.
Mr. Soeun Dara said that this increase is due to the demand for cars of the people of Cambodia is still high, combined with the strong economic situation and still high momentum, so the Federation of Automotive Industry of Cambodia is forecast to increase. Up in 2024.
In addition, Soeun Dara said that if the global economy improves, car sales growth will exceed expectations. For 2024, the Federation of Automobile Industries of Cambodia predicts that new cars will increase significantly while used cars will increase slightly due to:
* People as well as consumers understand the benefits of a new car after buying a new car and do not worry that the car has a problem and no repair in the first 5 years. * For the price is similar to a used car * and quality guaranteed From the factory, an average of 5 years * with maintenance service as well as repair service from the factory * and now some cars are installed locally and the price is better.
In fact, on the afternoon of January 25, 2024, Dr. Tan Monyvann, President of the Automotive Industry Federation of Cambodia (CAIF) also chaired a monthly meeting with the participation of members of the Federation.
The meeting summarized and reported on the achievements of the past year with the action plan and direction approved by the Board for implementation in 2024 to continue to promote and engage with the government and relevant partners in the development of the automotive sector. In Cambodia to grow like other countries in the region.
The progress in the development of the automotive sector is in line with the strategy of the Royal Government, which has identified the automotive sector as one of the key priority sectors in promoting national economic growth.
According to the Automobile Industry Federation of Cambodia, although the car sales rate in 2023 will fall by more than 20% compared to last year, the momentum of investment in car assembly plants and new car dealers continue to invest and expand. New car dealerships are on the rise and continue to grow.
This is a positive sign of the growing Cambodian automotive industry, which has evolved from a car-importing country to a country capable of assembling domestic cars on its own.
The Cambodian Automobile Industry Federation will also continue to cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions, especially the Royal Government, to continue to promote more automotive investment in Cambodia and ensure fair competition, transparent vehicle imports and taxation. .
In addition, ensure the import of cars in accordance with technical standards or standards to ensure the safety of consumers, incentives for the import of electric vehicles and investment in the network of power stations in Cambodia.
