The competition for the selection of civil servants as teachers specializing in physical education and sports has been announced for the candidates to register for the competition widely and the official application deadline will be on January 3, 2024.
Applicants must be qualified and meet the requirements of the special selection must pass a physical examination by the Department of Health Education of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
The competition to select teachers specializing in physical education and sports will be tested in two disciplines: writing and sports practice.
The writing course will take place on January 28, 2024 at the Royal University of Law and Economics, with three subjects: 1: General Culture for 1 hour and 30 minutes and 2: Biology for 1 hour and English. 1 hour.
All exam subjects will be prepared on the same day, that is, the subjects will be prepared in the morning and the exam will start from 12:30 noon.
Sports practice will start on the afternoon of January 29, 2024 and continue for 8 days at the National Institute of Physical Education and Sports, practicing three sports, including throwing, long jump and sprinting.
Each candidate must practice the throwing event twice in a row and then continue to the long jump event by jumping twice in a row and then to the sprint event once.
Ministry of Labor issues guidelines on strengthening the implementation of fire prevention measures and occupational safety and health measures of workers
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, issued a new guideline on strengthening the implementation of fire prevention measures and occupational safety and health measures of workers in factories.
1. Increase the regular inspection of the power supply network, measure the temperature of the power supply equipment in accordance with the safety standards and maintain the power supply equipment and all electrical equipment that cause the eventual fire. Workplace and daily temperature monitoring installed in the enterprise.
2. Supervise and promote the implementation of the roles and responsibilities of the committee or occupational safety and health team in the enterprise, especially the regular monitoring and update of occupational risk assessments in the workplace.
3: Educate and train workers to understand safety signs, evacuation methods and do proper exercises regularly.
6: Regularly inspect emergency exits that can be evacuated safely, unobstructed, no barriers, no locks and automatic lighting in the event of a power outage.
7. Prepare an emergency response plan by assessing the classification of workplaces with the use of chemicals and pagodas or flammable materials and response measures and keeping those substances separate from work or production buildings.
8 - Regularly inspect and maintain the ventilation system in the building and open for at least 1 hour before allowing workers to work.
9: Open all windows and doors or add a fan to ventilate or ventilate the production building when the weather warms up and arrange materials and raw materials in an orderly and safe manner, not to block the air source.
10: Advise workers to drink a glass of clean and hygienic water every 15-20 minutes and wear appropriate clothing according to the weather.
11. Monitor and take necessary measures to respond to the spread of hazardous substances to workers caused by the use of toxic substances, pesticides from outside the premises of the enterprise.
12: For enterprises and establishments that use steam boilers, regularly inspect the use of steam boilers in accordance with the technical and safety specifications, as well as have a permit and have steam boiler operators who have undergone training from ministries and professional institutions.
The owner or director of an enterprise who fails to comply with this instruction and endangers the life, property, security and public order shall be subject to penalties under the Labor Law and other criminal penalties in accordance with Article 30 of the Law. Fire prevention and extinguishing and other relevant laws.
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training strongly hopes that all owners or directors of enterprises, establishments and workers will strictly implement this guideline in a high sense of responsibility.
