History has shown us that the Khmer people established one of the first kingdoms since the beginning of the Christian era, the ancient Khmer mountain kingdom called Funan, which the Chinese called Funan or Funan. In fact, the people of Cambodia and China have been in contact with each other since before the creation of the mountain kingdom, according to Professor Trung Nga's book on Khmer history.
The book on the history of Cambodia-China relations also states that the Khmer mountain kingdom was a crossroads of trade, sea trade, as well as a culture between Chinese and Indian civilizations, as well as an abundance of resources of all kinds, including the ports of Okeo and Tun Sun. An important international trade port of our Khmer mountain kingdom.
In addition to increasing trade activities with the Phnom Kingdom, the Eastern Uyghur government also sent two envoys, including Kaing Thai and Zhu Ying, to pay official visits to the Phnom Kingdom and other kingdoms. This is the first time that the Chinese side has sent an ambassador to Cambodia as a demonstration of significant political significance. The Mountain Kingdom, which was visited by the Chinese embassy at the time, was called Fàn Xún by the Chinese.
Please be informed that the ambassadors of Tong, Wu, Thai, and Zhu Ying, after returning from the mountain kingdom, wrote works related to the territory, geography, resources, products and traditions of the people of Funan. Through the writing of these books also made the Chinese understand and know more about Cambodia. Both works also provide some content for writing books on the history of Cambodia, especially during the Mountain Kingdom.
