Cambodia will provide technical support, knowledge and expertise to Mongolia on demining work and support the implementation of Ottawa Convention standards.
The bilateral meeting was held on January 26, 2024 in Geneva.
During the meeting, Dr. Ly Thuch praised the cooperation between Cambodia and Mongolia in the past and highly commended Mongolia for its accession to the Ottawa Convention and for its support and participation in its activities. .
Mongolia has been committed to being a party to the Ottawa Convention, but due to a number of factors, including a lack of funding, Mongolia has not been able to join.
Dr. Ly Thuch expressed Cambodia's willingness to mobilize assistance and provide technical assistance, knowledge and skills to support Mongolia, clear mines against human trafficking and support Mongolia to implement the Ottawa Convention.
In response, Ms. Davaasuren Gerelmaa congratulated Cambodia on its election as Chair and Host of the Fifth Review Meeting of the Ottawa Convention and highly commended Cambodia's efforts as Chair and Pledges to continue Cambodia's proposal to the Mongolian government for consideration and to request further talks between Cambodia and some key institutions of Mongolia.
