The Minister of Rural Development instructed the Capital Department of Rural Development to identify model villages in the suburbs based on the criteria of model villages
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, instructed the Capital Department of Rural Development to cooperate with local authorities to identify model villages in the suburbs based on the main potential according to the criteria of model villages.
This introduction was made during the meeting and greetings with the leaders, civil servants and contracted officers of the Department of Rural Development of Phnom Penh, a total of 33 people on January 26, 2024, with the participation of the Permanent Secretary of State, Under Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State. Lead the Ministry of Rural Development and Mr. Im Ron Hassan, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh.
For the new legislature, the Ministry of Rural Development has set an important vision of "building a prosperous, rural, innovative, digital, and resilient rural Cambodia" to ensure an increase in rural household income. Sustainable and well-being through the launch of the National Strategic Development Plan 2024-2028, which translates into five priority programs.
The Minister instructed the leaders and civil servants of the Department of Rural Development of Phnom Penh as follows:
* The Capital Department of Rural Development shall cooperate with local authorities to identify model villages in the suburbs based on the main potential according to the criteria of the model villages.
* Must continue to maintain the achievements and achievements of the past as a basis and strive to increase the achievements and new works to participate in achieving the vision of Cambodia 2030 and 2050.
* Must strive to fulfill its duties and responsibilities responsibly and adhere to professional ethics, as well as consider themselves as officials to serve the people with integrity.
* The department must strive to fulfill its role as a good and honest staff to the Capital administration, have good cooperation with the authorities at all levels, relevant departments, as well as NGOs, development partners with experience and resources to promote better rural development.
