Stung Treng Provincial Election Commission Holds a Dissemination Meeting with Stakeholders on Registration of Political Parties and Candidates
(Stung Treng): The National Election Commission of Stung Treng Province on the afternoon of January 25, 2024 held a meeting with stakeholders on the registration of political parties and candidates for the 5th term of the Senate election. 2024.
The meeting was held on the morning of January 25, 2024 at Stung Treng Provincial Election Secretariat, chaired by Mr. Nhem Sary, Deputy Governor and Mr. Hang Kong, Chairman of Stung Treng Provincial Election Commission and members, Mr. Chairman, Deputy Chairman. Relevant departments and institutions of the three forces and representatives of political parties.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Hong Kong said that the meeting was held to focus on the following points:
* Posting of List of Candidates * The implementation of the election work has gone through 2 main stages (Stage of Voter Registration and Stage of Registration of Political Parties and List of Candidates) * Use and Completion of Forms 1007 (T.007) * Political party election campaign plan * About polling stations and counting ballots.
During the meeting, there were also comments from members of the meeting from representatives of political parties, including: representatives of the Cambodian People's Party, the Khmer Will Party, the Candlelight Party, FUNCINPEC and the National Forces Party.
Mr. Nhem Sary addressed the meeting in a meaningful manner by focusing on the work of organizing the security forces to improve the security around the election of the 5th legislature of 2024, the organization of public order and asked the relevant parties, especially political parties to Cooperate to respect the law and the code of ethics to avoid insecurity in the province around the election.
Mr. Hang Kong also summed up and closed the meeting by instructing the relevant parties, especially the representatives of political parties who attended the meeting to follow the rules and ethical procedures properly to lay the foundation for democracy in Cambodia better.
