(Pursat): Mr. Lay Viseth, Deputy Provincial Governor, on behalf of Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province, on January 26, 2024, called on farmers to participate in understanding, tolerance, stopping more dry farming and saving water. Save for the next 3 months as they exceed the plan.
The Deputy Governor appealed this during the inspection of the plan that has been set out in the past regarding the distribution of water use from the 5th gate to the main canal of Damnak Ampil to intervene to save the dry rice farmers. Water shortage problem.
Mr. Lay Viseth informed that 2023 is the year with the high price of rice and our farmers have produced more than 300% of the dry season plan, so the water shortage is even more scarce for this year and very challenging for Water distribution.
The Deputy Governor also called on all farmers to stop further dry farming due to water shortage after harvest, and then shut down dry farming and save water for sharing and for Use on human life, animals and clean water.
He pointed out that rice is not an aquatic crop like Prolit, Roomchang and Chhouk, but it is a water-resistant crop, so it only needs water to moisten the soil. He asked farmers not to misunderstand that rice crops need abundant water to overflow. And if you have water in the field, please stop pumping to send this water to the rice fields that need water.
