KOICA Holds First Bilateral Meeting in 2024 with Council for the Development of Cambodia on Development Cooperation in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) and the Cambodia Development Cooperation Committee of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDCB / CDC) have held a bilateral meeting to promote development cooperation and partnership. Between the two countries for the first time in 2024.
The bilateral meeting was held on January 25, 2024 yesterday at the meeting hall of the Council for the Development of Cambodia.
The main purpose of the meeting was to discuss plans for 2025, plans for new projects for 2026, and updates on ongoing programs. The two sides also discussed the inauguration of a new building for the National New Business Center of Cambodia (NICC) at the Royal University of Phnom Penh (RUPP).
Senior Minister Chiang Yanara thanked KOICA and the Government and people of the Republic of Korea for their continued support for Cambodia's socio-economic development through the implementation of various projects and programs.
The two sides also discussed cooperation on Official Development Assistance (ODA) between Cambodia and Korea. Both sides also focused on the next step in the work between KOICA-KOICA, the Council for the Development of Cambodia and the relevant ministries of Cambodia to develop new projects for 2026.
