H5N1 bird flu is a flu that is usually transmitted from sick birds to other birds, but can sometimes be transmitted from birds to humans through close contact with sick or dead birds. Avian influenza in humans is a serious disease that requires timely hospitalization. Although it is not easily transmitted from person to person, if it can metabolize it can be as contagious as the seasonal flu.
The Ministry of Health has also suggested measures to prevent the disease, such as washing hands frequently with soap and water before eating and after contact with birds, keeping children away from birds and keeping birds away from the environment. Eat sick or dead birds and all birds made for eating must be cooked well.
