"As credit restructuring was completed in the aftermath of the Kovid 19 crisis and the national, regional and global economies faced high uncertainty, with rising foreign lending rates, credit growth slowed to a record low," she said. 4.8%, the lowest rate in more than two decades. However, credit growth continues to play an important role in boosting manufacturing sectors such as manufacturing and agriculture, which are still double-digit growth.
