The two Southeast Asian nations are vying for the South China Sea, a major waterway for fishing and world trade that China claims almost entirely.
The two countries will sign a memorandum of understanding on coast guard cooperation, the Philippine Coast Guard said on Thursday. It is not clear what the agreement will include, but Coast Guard cooperation is usually important in reducing the risk of collisions between fishing vessels invading foreign waters as a step. That could help ease bilateral territorial disputes.
China has broad claims to the South China Sea and is often skeptical of progress in resolving border disputes among other claimants. After Vietnam and Indonesia recognized the borders of their respective exclusive economic zones in the South China Sea in December 2022, the Chinese Coast Guard repeatedly traveled near those strategic areas, sparking an angry reaction. Jakarta and Hanoi.
