Kampong Leng commune chief, Kampong Leng district, instructs cattle owners who are no longer allowed to eat people's rice, from now on, if the rice owners are caught, they will be fined one million riel per head
(Kampong Chhnang): Residents in Plou Touk commune, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province, who are engaged in dry farming, requested the authorities to help disseminate and take strict action against cattle that are no longer allowed to roam and come to eat. Their rice crops are everywhere.
According to the villagers, most of the cattle that were released from their owners were from Kampong Thom province, which borders Plou Touk commune, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province.
The other herds of cattle came from Chronok commune in Kampong Leng district, which the owners chased away and released, and the owners went fishing or doing other things, leaving the herds to roam forever and enter to eat. On the other hand, some people have just received permission from the Royal Government to farm in three areas for only one season.
Therefore, they asked the local authorities of Plou Touk commune to cooperate with the authorities of Kampong Thom province, which borders Plou Touk commune, to jointly prevent cattle owners from releasing anarchic cattle. People 's rice crop almost every day loses their benefits, some of which have just been approved by the Royal Government to allow them to farm in three areas only this season.
Through this media, the commune chief also requested all cattle owners who have not been allowed to graze in the past to let the people in the commune on the road to take care of their rice crops, please take care of them. Correct, otherwise, from now on, any cattle that eat people's rice, if the owner of the rice is caught, will be fined one million riel per head.
