(Beijing): More than 10 days is the traditional Chinese New Year. The express delivery company website states that "there will be no holidays during the Chinese New Year", that is, the freight center and service station are open as usual, and customer service hotline is open 24 hours a day. Etc. Chinese fast-moving enterprises do not rest on holidays are releasing the heat of economic development.
As a key point in the modern service sector, the size of the express delivery business is an important practical quantity index for observing the Chinese economy. What drives China's fast shipping business to thrive? This is inseparable from the drag on demand, the strength of supply, as well as the strong support from the central network.
On the supply side, whether or not delivery can be delivered quickly depends on the customer experience and level of satisfaction. China is currently the only country in the world to have all the full range of industries in the United Nations. The strong secondary industrial capacity as well as the supply chain excellence have greatly guaranteed the production speed and reactivity of Chinese enterprises.
The manager of a garment and hat factory in Rizhao, Shandong province, said that from receiving foreign customers' designs to producing prototypes, they can control the whole process within 24 hours. The growth of cross-border e-business has led to the rapid popularity of Chinese products abroad.
Nowadays, Chinese express delivery has become a prominent Chinese business card. The size of the business has steadily increased, indicating that the level of consumption has increased and is driving demand. Each package is a vivid interpretation of China's stable and better economy.
