Rice husk farmers call on court to expedite case of Yang Pak, director of AGRIBEE, issuing cashless checks
(Phnom Penh): A group of farmers who are buying and selling rice husks and rice have called on the judiciary and relevant ministries to take action against Yang Pak, CEO of AGRIBEE, for issuing cashless checks. 5 sheets in the total amount of 90,234.01 USD in order to pay the purchase price of rice husk.
She added that, with the unsuspecting belief of Yang Pak, she went to collect rice husks and sold them to Yang Pak, and Yang Pak issued a check to her. Pay the purchase price.
She added that when the due date was set, she took the check that Yang Pak had given her to the bank for withdrawal, but the bank said the check was cashless. She immediately contacted Yang Pak to inquire about the issue and find a solution, but he avoided responsibility.
She said that the actions of Yang Pak had seriously affected the livelihood and honor of her and her group, as she had to pay the purchase price to the owners and farmers and local traders. She sells rice husks to her and she has to borrow money from banks and the private sector to pay, she has to pay a lot of interest on a monthly basis until now.
