(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, on the afternoon of January 24, 2024, visited and brought rice and foodstuffs to support the National Center for the Treatment and Rehabilitation of Drug Addicts. Heart and community based in Keo Phos commune, Stung Hav district, Preah Sihanouk province.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said that for Sihanoukville, if there is a collection of drugs, a collection of drug addicts must be sent to a drug rehabilitation center located in Keo Phos commune, Stung Hav district, Sihanoukville. Healed and reintegrated into the community.
He added that he, as the chairman of the Provincial Unity Command, had to take control at the local level, starting from the implementation when he met and saw that the person was from where the province was and what the situation was. Testing for drugs in the body must be taken to the National Center for Treatment and Rehabilitation of drug addicts.
He said that in Sihanoukville, the Provincial Unity Command carried out simultaneously in all operations, taking measures to control open administration on public roads and in the local area after the implementation of the last three months. More than 200 drug addicts were found and sent to the center for treatment.
He also added that for this campaign, there is no withdrawal, if you have drugs in your community, you can continue to use from one person to another to use with them, causing harm in the community. .
Keo Veasna, director of the center, said that there were currently 670 victims, 36 of them women, who were being treated for drugs.
The National Center for Voluntary and Community-Based Drug Addiction Treatment and Rehabilitation has a rehabilitation and rehabilitation center for vocational training and rehabilitation, including psychology, psychology, physical education, sports, handicrafts, agriculture, life skills training, vocational training workshops. Before integration, you recover to your family and community.
Please be informed that the donations provided to the center include: 30 tons of rice, 200 bags of fish sauce, 200 bags of soy sauce, 200 bags of noodles, 200 bags of pure water, 10 million Riels, a gift from Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and 3,000 donations. Dollars as well.
