Former opposition member Long Kimkhorn, alias "So Samyuth", has been appointed Secretary of State at the Ministry of Justice.
The appointment was made in response to a request from the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Hun Sen.
On January 3, Mr. Long Kimkhon, a former member of the Board of Directors of the former National Rescue Party, sent a letter of respect to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, requesting to join the political life of the Cambodian People's Party.
He said that having joined the political life with the Cambodian People's Party so that he has the opportunity to contribute to the service of the motherland and the people of Cambodia to move forward. Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith Instructs Court Officials to Resolve More Than 6,000 Birth Certificate Complaints By the End of March
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, instructed all judges in the courts to resolve more than 6,000 cases of civil status (birth certificates) by the end of March 2024. And must not be involved in absolute interests.
Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith said: "We have collected more than 6,000 civil registration cases nationwide, which is equivalent to 90% of civil cases when filed and must be resolved quickly. I have requested as soon as possible. By the end of March, 6,000 cases will have to be settled.
In this case, the Minister of Justice instructed the justice officials to resolve the issue as soon as possible, adhering to the correct principles, promptly and without interest.
Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith also stated that in order to expedite the process of resolving the civil registration complaint, it is not necessary to take the opportunity to decide on any illegal documents. This means that any civil status that the law allows to be amended must be corrected in accordance with the law, while any point that the law prohibits the amendment must not be corrected.
At this point, the Minister of Justice added that if there is any problem, it is necessary to clarify the problem, especially please do not appear at all about issues of interest, even if it is small.
Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith also called on judges, prosecutors and all judicial officials to work together for a positive change for the image of the judiciary. In this case, no one can do it alone, and not a single judge has already done this work. What a pity! Endangered frog found in Sambo district, Kratie province
(Kratie): A female frog-headed tortoise weighing 26 kg and with eggs in its abdomen was found dead on Koh Andeng Khchey, Vathana commune, Sambo district, Kratie province on the 23rd. January 2024.
According to a report from the Kratie Fisheries District, an autopsy by the Kratie Fisheries Administration and WCS concluded that the frog-headed tortoise had died after being caught on a hook with hooks attached to its legs.
WCS also stated that in general, unhooked hooks are more likely to catch frog-headed tortoises because they are soft and the tortoise-headed tortoise is classified as vulnerable by Sub-Decree 123. Arrest and trafficking are illegal.
The Fisheries Administration and WCS call on fishermen and local people to take care of this species and avoid illegal catch and trafficking, which will be punished according to the law.
Minister of Information Presents and Shares Experiences on the Effectiveness of Information and Public Speech
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, participated as a speaker in the seminar on "Effectiveness of Information and Public Speech" organized by the Ministry of Justice on the afternoon of January 24, 2024 at Moradok Techo.
The Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia is located on Victory Blvd, Prek Taroth Village, Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh, with the participation of Mr. Seng Dina, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice.
Workshop on "Effectiveness of Information and Public Speech" for Spokespersons and Information Officers of the Ministry of Justice and the Tribunal at All Levels Awareness Raising Awareness Public opinion aims to contribute to increasing the efficiency of work in accordance with the direction of the Pentagon strategy and key measures of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra raised the question of whether you have ever asked yourself if your organization has done a lot of work and achieved a lot, but why the public does not seem to receive information from their institution and sometimes Misunderstanding and people are more likely to believe more slanderous information?
Therefore, communication with the media for dissemination is necessary and it is important to remember that in order not to lead to false information, we need to have a quick explanation through the media. If we do a lot and do not broadcast, it is zero.
The Minister highlighted the key points of public relations:
1: Communication with the community and the public 2: Communication with the media and journalists, and communication is in order to strengthen and expand mutual understanding, reduce misunderstandings and increase cooperation between Institutions and external environment.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra mentioned the important role of the spokesperson is to collect information related to his institution to disseminate to the public and manage public opinion for his institution. Spokespersons work closely with institutional leaders and public relations officials to release information through press releases and statements to ensure that the public receives comprehensive and timely information.
Answering the question of whether spokespersons need to be neutral? The Minister emphasized that for the institutions of the legislature, the executive branch, companies or other entities, the spokesperson acts as the sole bodyguard. For the judiciary, the spokesperson should balance the neutral position of the parties in the case, because the court has many parties and responds to the principle of equality before the law.
Speaking at the opening of the seminar on the morning of January 24, 2024, Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, stated that spokespersons at tribunals across the country have been established since 2016. To date, there have been no capacity building seminars or training sessions for spokespersons at the tribunal.
The spokesperson was created in order to increase the efficiency of the work of informing the public, both nationally and internationally, about the work as an achievement, as well as the objectives and policies of its institution and organization. In particular, individuals who can become spokespersons require knowledge and skills related to public relations work.
For spokespersons at the Trial Chamber, additional features are required to be in the middle between two interrelated tasks, including:
Firstly, confidentiality related to court affairs and secondly, the right to information, which requires the spokesperson to be extremely careful about this matter.
Due to the confidentiality of matters relating to the judiciary, it is imperative for the spokesperson of the Trial Chamber to carefully weigh what types of information should or should not be disseminated in order to avoid compromise. Processes and decisions of the courts as independent institutions.
This workshop will bring knowledge sharing as well as important experiences related to information work, speeches and public opinion from key dignitaries of the Royal Government who have a lot of skills and experience.
