(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, on Wednesday, January 24, 2024, accompanied by the technical officers of the Ministry and the Department, inspected the progress of the Irrigation and Flood Reduction Development Project (IDFMP). Banteay Meanchey Province, receiving concessional financing from the Eximbank of the Republic of Korea.
According to the construction company report, the implementation of the Banteay Meanchey Irrigation and Flood Reduction Development Project has so far achieved 20% of the 15% plan.
After listening to the progress report on the implementation of the project, the Minister together with the leaders, technical officers and the Director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Banteay Meanchey Province inspected the construction work at the main sites of the project, including Canal No. 2, Pong Ang Reservoir. O'Khaidon, Veang Heng Reservoir and Canal No. 1-1 and Canal No. 1-2 in Banteay Meanchey Province.
It should be noted that through the cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of Korea under the concessional financing from the Korean Bank Eximbank and with the close cooperation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance of Cambodia, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has been implementing a number of projects. Three are:
* First: the multi-purpose project of Daun Try Stung Mong Russey Dam, Battambang Province is under construction, which is scheduled to be completed in 2025 * Second: Irrigation and Flood Reduction Development Project in Banteay Meanchey Province is under construction, which is scheduled to be completed in 2026 * and Third: Flood mitigation and development project of Bavel Irrigation System, Battambang Province.
Minister of Justice urges speeding of traffic accident proceedings so that victims' families do not suffer injustice due to delayed proceedings
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, instructed judges, prosecutors and judicial officials to expedite traffic accident proceedings to ensure that the relatives of the victims do not suffer injustice due to the delay. No court proceedings.
Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith made this instruction on the morning of January 24, 2024, when he chaired a seminar on "Effectiveness of Speech, Information and Public Opinion for Spokespersons and Officials." Information from the Ministry of Justice and the Tribunal ”at the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith instructed all judges, prosecutors and judicial officials not to leave the case of the traffic accident that caused the death of the victim and the relatives became victims due to the delay of court proceedings. So push these things to help reach the victims.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith said: "In the case of traffic accidents, the most important priority is for the victims to receive compensation, but when they receive compensation, they must not let the person who hit the victim die and pay Money is free. "Not to have this situation, it will create class anger in society, it creates a blasphemy before the law because the power of money we can not get."
The Minister of Justice added that when the person who caused the accident caused the death of the victim but showed a willingness to take responsibility by coming in to settle the compensation, it means that the perpetrator can be released legally, but at this point, the court can Consider easing the sentence for the perpetrator because the victim withdrew the complaint. But the law must take strict action against the perpetrator who hit the victim, causing death and fleeing to deal with.
