(Phnom Penh): A group of young people from poor and vulnerable families said that the vocational and technical training program of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate will turn them into individuals who can change their lives in the family. The future, through a clear skill, has a decent job.
Tech Srey Leap, a trainee from Stung Meanchey commune, Phnom Penh, said: “I hope that after studying this professional skill, I will have a clear skill, have a job and earn a decent income. "I think that through this I will be able to support my family and earn a living."
She explained that due to lack of livelihood, she could not continue her high school education. Loving his studies, he applied for the Royal Government's professional and technical skills to ensure that he continued his education and had a clear skill in life.
"Study without running out of money and even get a stipend, especially after studying for only four months, we can get a clear skill for life in the future," she said. I just heard this news, I immediately applied to study at the Institute of Industrial Technology.
She added that the government's vocational and technical training is a good opportunity for young people from poor families like her to acquire specific skills for their lives.
Chhoeung Sokunthea, another young man from a poor family in Battambang province, said he could not continue his education without a vocational and technical training program. The Royal Government provides a unique opportunity for poor young people like them to learn short-term skills and have a stipend.
She thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, for its efforts in making this free training program a reality, enabling poor young people to learn skills and knowledge. Have a decent job to support your family in the future.
The national training program on vocational and technical training of 1.5 million young people from poor and vulnerable families, which officially opened in November 2023, has taken another step. On January 15, 2024, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training officially announced the opening of the first vocational training school.
