(Phnom Penh): In northern Laos, there is a province called Luang Prabang, which has a World Heritage Site and is also the former capital of the King of Laos, including a gold statue. The locals call it Preah Bang.
This is a short history of King Fang Ngum, a Lao king who came to seek asylum with the Khmers and helped the Khmers liberate Angkor from Siam, which is related to the history of our subject.
According to documents from the Mekong Institute of Thailand, in 1778, Thaksin's Siamese army invaded the kingdom of Luang Prabang, and the statue was taken from Luang Prabang to Vientiane. The Siamese army blocked the road and captured Thonburi, the capital of Siam at that time. In 1782, the Thonburi Royal Palace also sent the statue back to Laos due to a story in which King Thaksin broke free.
