(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, has instructed judges, prosecutors and justice officials to strictly enforce drug traffickers, not to sit around blowing smoke, but to put out the fire.
This confirmation was made by Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith on the morning of January 24, 2024, when he chaired a seminar on "Effectiveness of Information and Public Speech for Spokespersons and Information Officers of Ministry of Justice and the Trial Chamber ”at the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith stated: "Three measures to be taken in our field of justice that need to be operated on. The first step is to deal with drug cases." "Drugs are the fourth key measure of Samdech Hun Manet for our justice sector to be clear together, we do not sit around blowing smoke, we just put out the fire in the justice sector."
Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith added: "If the drug case is related to the interests of any drug lord, I apologize and let the information come to me, if I do not take action, I will walk away, not joking. "This has already been confirmed with the unit, because this is not a problem of anyone, it is a problem of the whole nation, it is an order of the head of the Royal Government."
The Minister introduced four points to the judges, prosecutors and judicial officials, namely: 1: Transparency, 2: Strictness, 3: Fairness in the implementation of the law, and 4: Ask the judges in the field of justice to be accepted. Be accountable to the Cambodian people as the drug situation is dangerous for our people.
Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith said that for the current drug case, it represents 60 percent of all criminal cases, more than 50 percent of which are incarcerated. Therefore, crime in Cambodia is covered by drugs because more than 50 percent. Security is a complex issue, but the second major issue is how many Cambodian human resources are lost due to drugs.
At this point, the Deputy Prime Minister emphasized that based on this challenge, as a justice official, it is the responsibility of the judiciary. This responsibility, based on the approach proposed by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, former Minister of Interior, is "3, 1 and 1 report".
The first report is to report to the authorities about drug storage, drug processing, etc. Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith emphasized: "Do not tolerate the drug master must be taken seriously, do not relax. "We must be transparent so that no one can accuse us of justice."
