Samdech Hun Sen Manet: The development of the Ream Naval Port is to strengthen the national defense capacity, not to threaten or invade any country (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Once again, Samdech Hun This morning, January 24, 2024, the development of Ream Naval Port and other types of troops is to strengthen Cambodia's defense capabilities and has no intention to threaten or create war with anyone.
On the occasion of presiding over the celebration of the 25th anniversary of the founding of the Army Command, Samdech Hun Sen also claimed that the Ream Naval Base, which is under development, will not allow any foreign military bases to set up positions. That said, separately and generally speaking, on Cambodian territory there are no foreign military bases.
According to Hun Manet, Article 53 of the Constitution clearly states that Cambodia does not allow foreign military bases on its territory, and that Cambodian troops are not based on other countries' territories, except under United Nations umbrella.
Samdech Hun Sen, General Hun Manet, said, "I would like to reiterate that this work is often mentioned in the newspaper, often the story of the Ream Sea." Cambodia Article 53 of our Constitution makes it clear that Cambodia does not allow foreign military bases on its territory and that Cambodian troops have no base on any territory except under the auspices of the United Nations.
I have already confirmed this case at the United Nations, Samdech Techo Samdech Pichey Sena, our national leaders have also confirmed it regularly, and I would like to reaffirm the capacity building of the Cambodian Navy, Air Force. "Only to defend Cambodia, not to make war on anyone."
The Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia also affirmed that there is no law in the world that prohibits the modernization of each country's defense, that is, strengthening the capacity of the army is to participate in maintaining peace and stability in the framework. Cambodia directly and the regional framework. If a situation arises such as terrorism or terrorism and Cambodia needs to participate, Cambodia will join immediately.
Samdech Hun Manet added that the Cambodian forces sent to work under the umbrella of the United Nations, if not increase capacity, can not integrate with other countries, so only have the ability to join. Other countries.
This statement was made during the celebration of the 25th anniversary of the establishment of the Army Command (January 24, 1999 - January 24, 2024) at the Army Headquarters on the morning of January 24, 2024.
On that occasion, the President said that the new government has introduced a number of reforms to strengthen the capacity of the army. The reform of the Cambodian Armed Forces into a modern force is capable of ensuring sovereignty in defending the sovereignty, peace, national independence and national development.
He said that the reform of the army must be based on the spirit of nationalism, national defense, religion, the king and the maintenance of peace and stability for the nation and the people. This is the spirit that we must adhere to at all stages, not to be divided.
He added that in addition to strengthening the spirit, it is necessary to strengthen the capacity of the national army to ensure the success of all tasks for the motherland, all the specialties of our army, which means to strengthen the independence, sovereignty in all areas of the army is reform. Based on the spirit of nationalism.
On the other hand, the Armed Forces must enhance cooperation with the Armed Forces of the bilateral and multilateral friendly countries on the basis of mutual respect in order to enhance the prestige of the Armed Forces on the international stage.
The ceremony was held at the Army Headquarters in a grand manner, with demonstrations of troops and tactics from various units under the Army Command.
Speaking on that occasion, Samdech Hun Sen issued five recommendations to all units of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces as follows:
First, the Cambodian Army must be a highly professional army that is absolutely loyal to the nation, the motherland and the people, and must strictly abide by all regulations, directives, statutes of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, legal norms, and adhere to the tradition. The dignity of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, and become a real force to defend the motherland and the people.
Second, all units must pay high attention to the use of force, resources and assets of the unit to be stable and effective, that is, to use force in accordance with the needs of skills and to manage and maintain all kinds of weapons, military equipment. Well, as well as food, etc. properly and sustainably.
Third, all units must strengthen the training, learning and building human resources, both quantitatively and qualitatively, to serve the national defense effectively, especially to strengthen the skills of the soldiers in accordance with their respective duties and roles. Body.
Fourth, please advise all units to pay attention to prepare all forces, means, and materials to help rescue people in the event of an accident, with a proactive spirit and good cooperation in a proactive spirit with Local authorities and relevant ministries and institutions.
Fifth, encourage all units to promote on-site economic development, such as crop production and animal husbandry, to contribute to improving the lives of soldiers and families, ensuring comfort, well-being, and productivity in carrying out their missions.
Samdech Hun Sen also highly commended the leaders, commanders at all levels, officers, deputies and soldiers throughout the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces for their heroic hard work and sacrifice in carrying out their duties. Protect the territorial integrity, maintain peace, security and better order for our people and society.
The reaffirmation of Samdech President Hun Manet was made on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the celebration of the 25th anniversary of the establishment of the Army Command (January 24, 1999 - January 24, 2024). The ceremony was held at the Army Headquarters in a grand manner, with demonstrations of troops and tactics from various units under the Army Command.
