Senior officials of the Ministry of Interior chaired a meeting to review and promote the implementation of the "Safe Villages, Communes and Sangkats" policy in Pursat province
(Pursat): Mr. Dr. Kiet Chantharith, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, represented by Mr. Abhisit Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, on the afternoon of January 23, 2024, chaired a meeting to review and promote implementation. The policy of "safe villages, communes and sangkats" falls under the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Interior in Pursat province.
The meeting was held at the Provincial Council Hall with the participation of Mr. Pov Piseth, Deputy Governor, Representative of Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat, representatives of the Provincial Court, leaders of various departments around the province, the Armed Forces. 3. The mayor / district governor, commune / sangkat councils, chiefs of the 49 commune / sangkat administrative police stations and some other relevant officials.
Brigadier General Heang Sitha, Deputy Commissioner of Pursat Provincial Police, read out the decision on the composition of the working group to monitor and promote the implementation of the "Safe Villages, Communes and Sangkats" policy under the Ministry of Interior at the sub-national level: Mr. Kirt Chantharith, Secretary of State, Chairman of the 17th Task Force in Pursat Province, Mr. Phang Pov, Undersecretary of State, and Mr. Hem Theng, Undersecretary of State.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Santi Dr. Kirt Chantharith also praised the results obtained by the Pursat Provincial Administration in the efforts of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command, which cooperated well in implementing the policy of "Village Communes are safe ”and congratulations to the communes that received good grades in the competition to implement the above policy.
The Secretary of State continued that the implementation of the policy of "safe villages, communes, sangkats" of the Municipal, District, Commune / Sangkat Administrative Unity Command enables the provincial administration to prevent local crimes such as drug offenses, theft, gambling, traffic accidents, trafficking. People, control of foreigners, immigration, economic crimes, border crimes are cracked down on in a timely manner and there are regular educational measures.
At the same time, we must work together to ensure order, safety, and order for the people living in the local area in accordance with the policy of "safe villages, communes, sangkats" that the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out and continue to disseminate traffic laws. And standard letters to local people and educational institutions on a regular basis through the police and the community.
Dr. Kirt Chantharith also requested the provincial administration as well as all relevant authorities to continue to work hard to implement the policy of "safe villages, communes, sangkats" and achieve the vision strategy. Of the Royal Government, which has been set out to ensure public safety, security and order to all local people in Cambodia, as well as in Pursat province.
