This morning, Samdech Thipdey Hun Manet Celebrates the 25th Anniversary of the Establishment of the Army Command
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Wednesday, January 24, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Hun Manet presided over the celebration of the 25th anniversary of the founding of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Army Command (January 24, 1999 - January 24, 2024). The ceremony was held at the Army Headquarters in a grand manner, with demonstrations of troops and tactics from various units under the Army Command.
According to a chronicle compiled by the Army Command, the Army has a long history dating back to the first century (AD 50), when the first monarchs reigned in Khmer territory, from the time of the Phnom Kingdom to the present, and the army has evolved many times according to each era and stage.
Under the leadership of His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, demanded full independence on November 9, 1953 The Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) was fully established, establishing the General Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (Army), Royal Cambodian Air Force, and Royal Navy.
After the 1970 coup, Cambodia plunged into a political crisis and civil war erupted until the motherland of Cambodia continued to fall into the Pol Pot genocidal disaster of April 17, 1975, which devastated society, economics, and freedom. And the structure of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces of the First Kingdom of Cambodia was completely destroyed.
On September 6, 2018, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet was trusted by the Head of the Royal Government and the King to be appointed Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander-in-Chief of the Army and the Ministry of National Defense. It was also decided to reorganize the divisions and brigades from under the command of the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to under the direct command of the Army Command.
The achievements of the Army depend on tireless hard work, sacrifice in all respects, integrity, loyalty, solidarity, internal unity and intelligence in leading the unit and fulfilling its responsibilities responsibly. The leaders, officers, deputies and all the soldiers who have made progress in the army in all fields should be very proud.
