Sihamoni Raja Buddhist University organizes entrance exam for students to study for a master's degree (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Preah Sihamoni Raja Buddhist University organizes a recruitment exam for students to study for a master's degree for training purposes Human Resources.
The ceremony was presided over by Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Bour Kri, Rector, Mr. Meas Samnang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Cults and Religions, Representative of Dr. Chay Borin, Minister of Cults and Religions, Mr. Nguon Sdech Pheakdey, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Cults and Religions and Vice Chancellor, including Preah Somethavong, Dr. Sok Bunthoeun, President of the Department of Buddhist Higher Education.
The entrance exam focuses on three specialties, including: 17th generation of public administration, 3rd generation of private law and 5th generation of general management, with 275 candidates and candidates, divided into 8 examination rooms: 1: Administration 4 public rooms, 2: private law, 2 rooms and 3: general management, 2 rooms.
Tan Sokhom, Vice Chancellor of Sihamoni Raja Buddhist University, said that in 2024, there will be an increase in the number of students participating in the exam, only in the 17th generation of public administration, up to 175 students who took the exam. The third generation of private law exam and the fifth generation of general management. In total, there are about 275 students in these three subjects, which is an increase from last year, when there were only 100 students.
He hopes that the students who come to this exam are they believe in the Buddhist University of Sihamoni Raja. He would also like to express his gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia and other philanthropists. It is 9 stories high and was inaugurated last year.
He confirmed that the study here, the teaching has been reformed to suit the job market, and therefore many students come to study here.
He also committed to continue to train students here effectively and successfully so that they can continue to reach the next level, because it is a generation of success that the first generation of students study at the level. 194 such people are seen as the pride of Sihamoni Raja Buddhist University, especially in public administration and private law.
Professor Chan Hoeun, who teaches a Master's degree at Sihamoni Reach Buddhist University, said he considered Sihamoni Raja Buddhist University to be a state-owned Buddhist university, the first Buddhist university to offer doctoral degrees, especially Buddhism. At this university, Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Bour Kri, the Rector, focused on the quality of education.
In addition to focusing on education, the Buddhist University also offers some possibilities to students or ordinary students who wish to receive various scholarships, they can choose this university is: first, quality, Second, students who are in need can receive additional accommodation incentives, this is a benefit for those who are in need.
Professor Mong Monisophea, a law teacher, similarly said that he was very satisfied and happy because the Sihamoni Raja Buddhist University, he helped a lot in teaching and was very strong because the people In particular, the students here are the children of the able-bodied, and for him to have a heart and sympathy, seeing him try to come to study is motivated to teach.
