BANGKOK, Jan. 7 (Xinhua) - Thailand's economy is expected to grow 2.8 percent this year, a sharp drop from the economy, the finance ministry said in a statement on Tuesday. An earlier forecast of 3.2 percent growth. According to a report by Reuters.
Reuters reports that gross domestic product (GDP) growth in 2023 is expected to reach 1.8 percent, down from a previous estimate of 2.7 percent.
Foreign tourist arrivals in 2024 are projected at 33.5 million, down from the previous forecast of 34.5 million, while exports are expected to increase by four. , 2% this year, compared with the previous estimate of 4.4%. Exports in 2023 are projected to decline by 1.5 percent.
