The following is a statement from Dr. Sar Sokha: Cambodia requests UN-ESCAP to mobilize countries in the Asia-Pacific region that have not yet become parties to the Ottawa Convention. Hosts 2024
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mine Action Authority and Chairman of the National Committee for Mine Action, and on behalf of Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Action Authority, requested UN-ESCAP to assist in mobilizing countries in the Asia-Pacific region that have not yet Become a State Party to the Ottawa Convention while Cambodia is chairing and hosting the 2024 Summit.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch made the request during a working meeting with Dr. Amida Saliyah Alice Jabana, Deputy Secretary-General of the United Nations and Chair of the United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific (UN-ESCAP). ) On January 22, 2024.
During the meeting, Dr. Ly Thuch extended a warm welcome to Dr. Amida Saliyah Alice Jabana and the delegation who paid an official visit to Cambodia and thanked UN-ESCAP for its continued support. Strive to leave the status of a less developed country and achieve the goals of sustainable development.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch spoke about the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to clear mines and explosive remnants of war for more than 30 years and to become one of the countries in the world that has cleared more landmines and landmines in the world. Among the 30 countries that are clearing mines like Cambodia.
The Senior Minister continued that 2025 is the common goal of the governments, development partners and all stakeholders to support the work of demining in Cambodia and to make Cambodia a landmine-free country.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Ly Thuch informed Lok Chumteav Bandit about Cambodia's success in receiving the support of the States Parties to the Convention on the Prohibition of the Use of Anti-Personnel Mines (the Convention) as the chair and host of the review meeting. 5 of the Convention, which will take place on November 25-29, 2024.
At the same time, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, on behalf of Samdech Hun Manet, Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Authority, requested the support of UN-ESCAP in the globalization of the Ottawa Convention, supporting Cambodia in mobilizing countries in Asia and the Pacific to participate and participate. States Parties to the Ottawa Convention.
In response, Dr. Amida Saliyah Alice Jabana expressed her deep gratitude to Dr. Ly Thuch for his cooperation with the UN-ESCAP delegation, and she expressed her gratitude and pleasure for the warm welcome to her and All delegates on an official visit to Cambodia.
Dr. Amida Saliyah Alice Jabana congratulated Cambodia on its support for chairing and hosting the 5th Review Meeting of the 2024 Ottawa Convention. In addition, Ms. Bandith is also committed to continuing cooperation with the Royal Government of Cambodia and supporting Cambodia.
