Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Dimitri Medvedev Agree to Strengthen Multilateralism
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, and Dmitry Medvedev, President of the United Russia Party, have agreed to strengthen the multilateral system, which is an important element in strengthening the international legal system and maintaining world order.
The agreement to strengthen the multilateral system between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Dmitry Medvedev was made in a video meeting on the afternoon of January 22, 2024.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen's social media post, during the 20-minute meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Dimitri Medvedev announced their mutual support for international cooperation within the framework of the dual forum. The parties, the multilateral forum and the regional forum, are in-depth discussions in unification, working to safeguard the interests of their respective regions, especially the proper strengthening of multilateralism in the region and in the world.
The two leaders saw that multilateral cooperation will create an atmosphere of mutual understanding and mutual assistance as necessary in accordance with the rules respected by the United Nations.
The announcement comes as the world is seen to be torn between the allies of liberal democracies and socialist or communist regimes. The rift prompted the two regimes to put in place countermeasures.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Dmitry Medvedev Pledge to Work Close, Strengthen Cooperation, Cooperation and Respond to Global Issues (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Dmitry Medvedev, President of the United Russia Party, agreed to work more closely to strengthen bilateral relations and cooperation, as well as to respond to global issues.
On the afternoon of January 22, 2024, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Dmitry Medvedev met to discuss work by video for about 20 minutes. According to the results posted on Samdech Techo's social media, the two party leaders praised the bilateral meeting in a happy atmosphere and greeted each other for the new year.
The leaders of the two parties saw the need for mutual cooperation in the fight against the color revolution, which is a point to think together. The two leaders see interference in internal affairs as a threat to their respective national security, so the two countries must unite to avoid interfering in each other's internal affairs and help each other. And share experiences as needed.
The leaders of both parties felt that the cooperation between the younger generation of leaders, especially Russia, also supported the leadership of Samdech Hun Sen and celebrated when the CPP decided to elect Hun Sen as President. Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party, which is to prepare an appropriate successor.
Mr. Medvedev praised the wise decision of Samdech Techo, President of the Cambodian People's Party, as well as the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party, who chose a young successor to continue the long-term cooperation.
The leaders of the two parties also provided support for cooperation and discussions on major forums of Russian initiative, as well as other friends in the BRICS community, the Eurasian community, as well as in the Russian community. The Mekong is also a point where both sides are satisfied with the changes in practical cooperation, and the governments of each country will work together to examine the feasibility of practical cooperation.
During the meeting, the leaders of the two parties agreed to review any work that can be done on the old agreement and make new agreements as far as possible, and other agreements can be reviewed and reconsidered.
