Iranian foreign minister to visit Pakistan next week after missile strike
(Islamabad): Pakistani authorities said on Monday that the Iranian foreign minister will visit Pakistan next week. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on January 22, 2024.
The visit is a sign of efforts to rebuild ties after the two neighbors launched a missile attack last week on what they said was aimed at militants.
The Pakistani Foreign Ministry said in a statement that the ambassadors of the two countries were also asked to return to duty on January 26.
Last week, Pakistan recalled its ambassador to Tehran and barred the Iranian ambassador from returning to Islamabad and canceled all high-level diplomatic and trade ties. All the more.
