Leaders and technical officers of Tonle Sap Authority inspected the clearing site of flooded forest land in 3 areas of Kampong Thom province
(Kampong Thom): Under the guidance of Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology and Chairman of the Tonle Sap Authority, on 22 January 2024, the technical staff of the Tonle Sap Authority led by Mr. Hel Tony, Deputy Chief of Staff and Mr. Sar Kimsan, Secretary General of the Tonle Sap Authority, inspected the site of the clearing of flooded forest land in three areas in Kampong Kor commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province.
During the inspection, the leaders and technical officers of the Tonle Sap Authority, in cooperation with the provincial authorities and local authorities of the relevant districts and communes, found that the area in the three areas was cleared by the conspirators. Expand the area of dry rice or rice chasing water, even though this area has been cleared by the Royal Government in the past.
After an actual inspection of the area affected by the encroachment, the leaders and technical officers of the Tonle Sap Authority prepared a report and asked the relevant provincial, district and commune authorities to recognize and promise to prevent this encroachment. Cultivation on the encroached land, otherwise it will be responsible before the law in force and must continue to search for individuals who have committed crimes to deal with the legal process.
On that occasion, the leaders of the Tonle Sap Authority also instructed all officials to continue to cooperate and implement the spirit of roles and responsibilities as defined in Sub-Decree No. 197 dated August 29, 2011.
Please note that the Tonle Sap Authority is an institution that is responsible for the Royal Government in the mandate to coordinate the management, conservation and development of the Tonle Sap area. In particular, in the spirit of Article 4, Sub-Decree No. 197, the Tonle Sap Authority states that the Tonle Sap Authority has the duty to inspect the activities of flooded and flooded forests and report to the Prime Minister for action.
