Research has found that there are five countries with the longest rail network in the world, including:
* United States
With the third largest population after China and India, the United States needed to build 226,427 kilometers of railways.
* Russian Federation
Russia is the largest country in the world, although the population is not as large as other large countries, but this giant country desperately needs railways to travel and transport goods. The country's railway network is 87,157 kilometers long.
* People's Republic of China
This Asian giant has the largest population in the world as the economy is growing rapidly, so the need for rail to boost its economy is also essential. Greater China has a total railway network of 77,834 km.
* Republic of India
Greater India has a large population of Indians and is still in high numbers, so railways play an important role for people to travel. The giant has just woken up with a total railway network of 63,327 kilometers.
The geography of this country is mostly covered with ice, just like Russia. Canada has a total rail network of 46,688 km.
