Analysis: Choosing the Chinese market is not a risk but an opportunity
BEIJING, Jan. 17 (Xinhua) - China's economy has been strengthening and improving, according to the 2023 National Economic Data released by the Chinese government on January 17.
Looking back at exports and imports, global demand is now declining and in some countries trade protectionism has re-emerged. The report of the United Nations Conference on Trade and Development predicts that by 2023, global trade volume will decline by 7.5 percent. China's exports and imports were generally stable, which is expected to maintain its position as the world's largest global commodity trader for the seventh consecutive year.
