(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, emphasized that the Ministry will strive to manage information security well so that people do not poison the false information that causes confusion.
This statement was made by the Minister on the morning of January 22, 2024 at the opening ceremony of the meeting to summarize the work results of 2023 and the work direction for 2024 of the Ministry of Information on the morning of January 22, 2024 at the Ministry.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra emphasized: "Within this framework, the Ministry of Information has strengthened the information security, which is different from information security (in terms of information related to traffic accidents), but information security is the same as food security, energy security. ...! ”
The Minister also highlighted the information security that the Ministry has focused on three points: 1: access to information of the people, 2: quality information (quality of journalists) and 3: media security, which refers to information that Set up, release, publish is accurate information, non-toxic.
Minister Neth Pheaktra added: "If the people are poisoned by the media, it will be difficult, and as a ministry where both the state and the media take legal action, it is necessary to fully control information security."
The minister added that information security is part of helping to strengthen security for the nation, order and stability for the country.
He added: "In the future, the Ministry will introduce a national policy from broadcasting information from analog to digital, which is more relevant, including the import of audio-visual equipment into the country whether we need. Allow the import of analog audio equipment? "That's why we need a national policy on the transition from analog to digital, with a lot of work to be done."
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that as the Ministry of the Royal Government, we can not walk behind, we must strengthen to do so to walk first. In the digital context, true and false information are mixed together. At this point, what can we do to provide real information to the people?
He said that in 2024, the Ministry will check the status of three officials: first: officials who are assets, second: debt officials and third: senior officials. "In this situation, we need to re-analyze the functions and train those officers to work in different areas without leaving a trace."
At the same time, the Minister also mentioned that the Ministry has identified five main designers, including:
