(Siem Reap): The Angkor Writing Program, which lasted for one day in front of the Angkor Wat temples, was successfully completed unexpectedly due to the large number of participants and such good results, but what was behind it? Organizing this important program?
After the Angkor Writing Program, which ended on the evening of January 21, 2024, Mr. Lim Bunhok, the initiator of the Angkor Writing Program, described the struggles behind the organization of the program, including the location of the casting. Hundreds of shirts are not very rich, the prize money to encourage the candidates is not much, especially the lack of funds to spend on the program itself.
However, all stakeholders have been actively involved in providing financial assistance, physical and mental support in various ways to achieve this important way, especially with the participation of a large number of monks, candidates and candidates. There are still people participating outside the program and from many distant homes, which shows the strong love of national literature of the Cambodian people. This is according to Mr. Lim Bunhok.
Through the experience of this first organization, Mr. Lim Bunhok will strive to better organize the next program and also called for more participation from the public of all ages and nationalities to participate in the literary cause. Khmer nation.
