Listen to Mr. Puy Kea: 20 years of establishment of the Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center, focusing on three main activities for the development of Cambodia, human resources and strengthening Cambodian-Japanese diplomatic relations
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center of the Royal University of Phnom Penh was established in 2004 under the auspices of the Royal Government of Cambodia, represented by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, and the Government of Japan, represented by the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA). JICA), a technical and financial assistance agency.
Construction of the center building began in June 2004 and was completed and handed over to the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on November 25, 2005 at a total cost of approximately US $ 4,455 billion. The building was officially inaugurated on February 21, 2006 under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In general, the Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center focuses on three main activities: first, the entrepreneurship and business management training program, second: Japanese language courses for career development, and third: cultural exchange and education programs.
In 2024, the Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center is 20 years old and is continuing its project in the fifth phase, which started in April 2022 and will end in March 2025. After the fifth phase, the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) is expected to continue the sixth phase for another three to five years from 2026.
First, through entrepreneurship and business management training programs
* CJCC has contributed to the training of approximately 30,500 people who are business owners, managers and employees in government institutions and private companies in Phnom Penh and other provinces. Business training programs include Entrepreneurship, Advanced Japanese Management, Business Acceleration, Business Management for Company Leaders, Training at the request of clients, and more.
* After training in the country, some trainees are given the opportunity to visit Japan to gain more knowledge as well as exchange experiences with the management of the company in Japan.
* In addition, participants have the opportunity to meet with investors and financing institutions to obtain financing for further development of their business.
* In addition to the training program, the Center established the Cambodia-Japan Trade and Investment Association (CJBI) in March 2016, which acts as a platform for networking and business matching between Cambodian-Cambodian and Cambodian-Japanese companies for the purpose of establishing Opportunity to catch business partners together.
At the same time, to help companies (especially Japanese companies in Cambodia in the country) to recruit staff and provide opportunities for job seekers, CJCC organizes job fairs twice a year since 2012.
Second: Through Japanese language courses for career development
* Following the Japanese Foundation for Japanese Language Education (CJCC) standard, CJCC has trained approximately 12,000 Japanese language students, many of whom have completed courses in Cambodian and Japanese companies in both Cambodia and Japan. .
* To help promote the study of Japanese language, CJCC organizes Japanese speech competition with the cooperation of relevant institutions in Cambodia.
* In response to the needs of Japanese language learners in Cambodia, the Center has been authorized to organize the JLPT Japanese Language Proficiency Test since 2006 with a total of 31,045 candidates.
Third: Cultural Exchange and Education Program
* In addition, with the support of JICA Study Center in Japan to provide opportunities for those who want to continue their studies in Japan. Each year, the Fair is attended by more than 1,000 participants.
* In addition to organizing study fairs, CJCC has developed a website and collaborated with the Okayama University Study Information Office in Japan to promote the study of Japanese studies more effectively.
The Center has been highly praised by the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) for its innovative and diverse activities for sustainability. Especially in 2018, the center received a letter of commendation from the Japanese Ministry of Foreign Affairs for its role in contributing to friendly relations and cultural exchanges between the two countries.
