Young women from Pursat land strive to learn as a bridge from poverty to near the goal of being killed by a drunk car
(Phnom Penh): Nget Srey Mao, a poor farmer from Prey Rong village, Talor commune, Talor Senchey district, Pursat province, was hit by a drunk car when she stopped at a traffic light under the Russey Keo flyover along National Road 5, Sangkat Russey Keo, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, on the night of January 20, 2024.
Srey Mao, a child from a poor family, worked hard to study. After bankruptcy in 2020, he continued to study architecture at the Royal University of Fine Arts. By the third year, the dream is to become a support for the family for a better life, close to the goal of the goal, and then die on the streets caused by drunkenness to destroy.
Srey Mao's death has shattered the hopes of the family, the loss of young women full of resilience, the loss of Cambodia's good resources.
The accident killed four people, three women, one man and seriously injured four people.
Road accidents kill people every day. Social observers see that penalties for dangerous drivers should be considered more severe and enforced to raise awareness among drivers, especially under the influence of alcohol.
