(Siem Reap): The Cambodian Tourism Association (CATA) distributed certificates of completion of tourism skills training to 90 participants for 3 months, including theoretical and practical training from September 25 to December 25. 2023 in Siem Reap province.
There are 30 food and beverage service staff, 30 front office staff and 30 room and housekeeping staff.
The ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Yun Linne, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap, Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of the Cambodian Tourism Association CATA, Mr. Eng Kunthea, President of the Cambodia Tourism Association, Siem Reap Branch, and representatives of relevant sectors and many participants in the afternoon. January 20, 2024 at the Star Angkor Hotel, Siem Reap.
Mr. Eng Kunthea said that the Cambodian Tourism Association (CATA) has partnered with a research and arithmetic consulting firm approved by the Rural Sustainability Support for Farmers Market and Agricultural Trade in Cambodia (SAAMBAT) project under the Ministry of Economy. Provide skills training for young people from remote and poor areas to receive education in tourism and hospitality.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin said that due to the peace factor, we have increased the number of tourism services, if we do not have peace for tourists, we have to choose the safest area, and now we can bring in tourists. Going deep into the forest to see the rich landscape and natural resources of Cambodia proves the peace of Cambodia as a whole.
She said that the trainees who graduated today are all pillars and successors in applying the skills to tourism that have been learned, although this course is only 3 months, but we Keep rehearsing it until you can say it with conviction and confidence that you're going to be an expert in the future.
She added that all tourism professionals must adhere to a polite and friendly attitude, not to discriminate on the basis of race, color or country. We have a lot of good resources like Angkor Wat, but if we, the tourism service providers use quality, then tourists love Angkor Wat, but they do not love the waiters in the tourism sector.
In addition, Mr. Yun Linne thanked the Cambodian Tourism Association (CATA) for helping to train all participants to strengthen tourism in Cambodia, especially in Siem Reap.
He also urged all participants to take the knowledge learned and self-research to apply properly to develop themselves to grow and attract more tourists to Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha announces the composition of the Royal Government's working group in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha, Minister of National Defense and Chairman of the Royal Government of Siem Reap Province, on the afternoon of January 21, 2024, presided over the announcement of the composition of the Royal Government of Siem Reap Provincial Working Group.
Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha paid a courtesy call on Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet and the Royal Government's efforts to implement the party's policies and the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy, as well as the establishment of a grassroots working group. To serve the interests of the people and contribute to the national economy.
On that occasion, the composition of the National Field Team in Siem Reap Province was also announced, with members assisting at the municipal and district levels.
Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha also instructed the working group to prepare additional components to visit the districts and to adjust the composition in the districts as the Deputy Chairman of the working group throughout Siem Reap, in accordance with the indication from the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha explained the roles and responsibilities of the field teams at the national and sub-national levels, working methods and working mechanisms for effective and efficient implementation.
Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha continued that the grassroots team must work together to be good, willing, responsible and authoritative, and that it is necessary to go to the grassroots to listen to the needs of the real challenges. Sure of the people to think together to solve for the people most effectively in accordance with the priority policy of the Royal Government.
The Deputy Prime Minister said that the task of the grassroots team is to help in the spirit of providing innovative ideas, and the team did not complete any work on behalf of the specialized unit.
(Kampot): Police from Kampot Provincial Anti-Drug Office cooperated with Takeo Provincial Police to launch a search operation and arrest 5 drug distribution and use ringleaders and confiscate some exhibits.
Authorities immediately launched an operation to crack down on one case of illegal drug trafficking (incitement measures) and arrested one suspect.
The suspect is Sem Saroeun, alias Chap, male, 29 years old, living in Sovan Sakor Village, Sangkat Kampong Kandal, Kampot City, Kampot Province. Seize 1 package of drugs, 1 motorcycle and 1 mobile phone
After interrogating the suspect, Sem Saroeun, on January 20, 2024, at 1:30 AM, the police continued to detain the suspect, who was a drug trafficker in Prey Thnong village, Prey Thnong commune, Teuk Chhou district, Kampot province. One more suspect, Uy Sokheng, male, 32 years old, living in Trapeang Kampleng village, Ang Phnom Touch commune, Angkor Chey district, Kampot province. Seize 1 motorcycle and 2 mobile phones.
After interrogating the suspect, Uy Sok Heng, on January 20, 2024, at 5:30 AM, the police continued to detain the suspect, who was a drug trafficker in Boeung Nimol village, Boeung Nimol commune, Chhuk district. Kampot arrested one more suspect, Dong Chanon, male, 23 years old, living in Smaong Village, Smaong Commune, Traing District, Takeo Province. Captured exhibits: 3 packs of drugs, 1 motorcycle and 1 mobile phone.
After interrogating the suspects, Nget Raksmey alias Koei and Dong Chanon, on January 20, 2024, at 5:30 PM, the police continued to detain the suspects who were part of the group calling to buy drugs in the village. Sisla commune, Thla Prachum commune, Koh Andet district, Kampot province, arrested one more suspect, Khim Tola, male, 32 years old, living in Po village, Phnom Kong commune, Angkor Chey district, Kampot province. Capture evidence: 1 motorcycle and 1 mobile phone.
According to the report, through the evidence and confessions of the members of the Kampot Provincial Anti-Drug Office, they continued to cooperate with the Takeo Provincial Police until they proceeded to crack down on the mastermind of trafficking in Sisla Village, Thlay Prachum Commune, Koh Andet District, Takeo Province. Total weight 2851.37 grams. A total of 5 suspects.
Currently, the suspect and exhibits were brought to the Anti-Drug Office to file a case according to legal procedures. Preah Vihear Provincial Armed Forces confiscated more than 1 ton of drugs that the suspect dumped in a car in Chey Sen district.
(Preah Vihear): A vehicle loaded with 33 packs of drugs, equivalent to 1,020 packages weighing 1,020 kg, which the suspects dumped in front of Chey Sen High School in Chey Sen District, Preah Vihear Province, was taken by the Preah Vihear Provincial Gendarmerie. Come and save to deal with according to the law.
After receiving a report from the Commander of the Chey Sen District Gendarmerie, Brigadier General Kang Sao Kun, Commander of the Preah Vihear Provincial Gendarmerie, reported to Mr. Ty Sovinthal, Prosecutor of the Preah Vihear Provincial Prosecutor's Office. Mr. Sreng Vuthea, Deputy Provincial Prosecutor, coordinated the implementation of the procedure and sent the evidence to the Preah Vihear Provincial Gendarmerie Command to inspect the actual evidence.
After the inspection, it was found that there were 33 bags of drugs equal to 1,020 packs (one pack equals 1,000 grams) weighing 1,020 kg. The fugitive suspects are being investigated by special forces.
