Minister of Rural Development: The Ministry is working to improve the living standards of rural people in terms of economy, society and culture.
(Oddar Meanchey): The Ministry of Rural Development has been actively pursuing its mission to achieve its vision of improving the quality and value of life of people in rural areas, both economically, socially and culturally. .
These were confirmed by Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, during a meeting with leaders and civil servants of the Department of Rural Development of Oddar Meanchey and Preah Vihear Provinces with a total of 40 officials on January 20, 2024. Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey, Mr. Kong Kannarith, Deputy Governor of Oddar Meanchey, Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear.
After listening to the 2023 annual report and 2024 work direction of the directors of the two provincial rural development departments, the Minister praised and appreciated the efforts of all leaders and civil servants of the department until the results. Should be proud.
The Minister said that the new Royal Government has set out a pentagonal strategy to achieve the vision of 2050, Cambodia is a high-income country.
"In order to contribute to the support of the Royal Government's policies, the Ministry is actively pursuing its mission to achieve its vision of improving the quality and quality of life of people in rural areas," he said. "Economic, social and cultural environment."
He said that the Royal Government, like the Ministry of Rural Development, has been continuously upgrading 50,000 km of rural roads to paved and concrete roads and promoting rural water supply and sanitation to improve livelihoods. Of the people in the countryside.
The Minister also informed about the priority strategies of the Ministry of Rural Development, including: the development of physical and transport infrastructure, the improvement of living conditions of rural communities through the supply of clean water and household toilets, the diversification of rural economic activities, and Strengthening administrative support services and general affairs.
With this, the Minister instructed the leaders and civil servants of the two provincial rural development departments as follows:
1. Continue to maintain the achievements and achievements of the past as a basis and strive to increase new achievements in order to contribute to achieving the vision of Cambodia to make people with high middle income in 2030 and high income. In 2050.
2. As civil servants, we must serve the people with ethics and professionalism as public servants in order to turn Cambodia into a prosperous country.
3. The department must strive to fulfill its role as a good and honest staff to the provincial administration and must have good cooperation with relevant departments as well as authorities at all levels, NGOs, development partners with experience and resources to promote better rural development. Even better.
4. The Department shall increase the dissemination and establish a group of spokespersons of the Department to communicate and provide information to each other in order to participate in disseminating the achievements and achievements of the Royal Government as well as the achievements of the Ministry of Rural Development from the beginning of the mandate. More widely to the masses through social media.
5. The leaders of the department must take care of the well-being of civil servants and be encouraged by promoting their positions, ranks, medals or other means.
6. There must be good internal unity, do not take sides, take care of civil servants who are disabled, civil servants who are pregnant or have small children.
