(Phnom Penh): After traveling for about 17 hours from Paris, France, Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia and HE Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet led a delegation to arrive in Cambodia safely at 3 pm, Saturday, January 20, 2024.
Samdech President Hun Manet and Lok Chumteav Bandith led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to pay a one-week visit to France and Switzerland from January 13 to 19, 2024.
Samdech Manet's one-week mission to Europe in early 2024 is a fruitful visit, both political and economic. Political views Samdech Manet met with the top three leaders of France, including the President of the Senate, the President of the National Assembly and the President.
In addition to expressing his gratitude and appreciation to the Government for helping to preserve the temple as well as the development of Cambodia, Samdech Mani also announced his firm position to continue to improve relations and cooperation with France.
Samdech Hun Sen also expressed his hope that through his visit, the relationship and cooperation between Cambodia and France will be better. The Prime Minister also wants to see the cooperation between the private sector of the two countries more lively to become the lifeblood of Cambodian-French relations.
During the meeting, Samdech President Hun Manet disseminated the Royal Government's policy on environmental issues and policies related to investment in Cambodia. Samdech Hun Sen also sought the support of these international organizations for development as well as investment in Cambodia.
From the economic point of view, Samdech Hun Sen met directly with the management of nearly 20 companies and indirectly through the business forum of about 80 more companies. Up to six memorandums of understanding have been signed between Cambodian and French companies. The MoU signed includes:
During his current mission in Europe, Samdech Hun Sen also met with Cambodians living and studying in various European countries. During the meeting, in addition to visiting and expressing condolences, the Prime Minister also highlighted the policies of the new Royal Government and the achievements of the new Royal Government over the past four months.
Please note that the private companies that President Hun Manet met during his mission in Europe include:
Alstom is a French company with global operations in the railways, high-speed rail, subways and other infrastructure services, from electric trains to state-of-the-art technology. Alstom operates in 63 countries worldwide and employs approximately 80,000 people of about 175 nationalities.
Blue Circle has been developing, financing and operating renewable energy projects in Southeast Asia since 2013. Blue Circle opened its first office in Phnom Penh in 2015, choosing Mondulkiri to implement the company's first project on wind power conversion, which is scheduled to open in 2026.
HawkEye 360 is a radio frequency data analysis company established in 2015. The company has developed aerial network and radio frequency solutions to monitor air, land and water transport.
The company has served the maritime, defense and telecommunications industries, traveling through satellites to search, identify and locate a wide range of radio frequency bands to help consumers around the world.
The company has advanced agricultural technology from cultivation, processing, packaging, supply and distribution, with the main products of the company are: coconut oil, cereal oil, flour and sugar.
Lippo Group is based in Indonesia and specializes in real estate, retail, hospitality, healthcare, education, journalism, digital telecommunications and finance.
The company focuses on food security and safety by evolving state-of-the-art technology in food processing, packaging and distribution. In addition, Bühler is a leader in automotive optical technology, printing, packaging and glass technology.
