An electrician was electrocuted in Chulkiri district
(Kampong Chhnang): An electrician was electrocuted after being taken to hospital as the victim climbed a pole and removed the pole to move the pole on January 19, 2024 at Prek Lvea. Located in Tamol Leu village, Koh Thkov commune, Chulkiri district.
Sources from witnesses at the scene said that before the incident, the victim climbed on a light pole to remove the power line to move the pole so as not to obstruct the traffic of people driving through there every day while people The victim went up to the light pole above and touched the electric wire, causing the victim to faint on the pole.
Seeing this, the electric team came to pick up the victim on the truck and took him to the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital immediately.
According to the Koh Thkov Administration Post, the victim was Sok Teng, 36, a member of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Electricity Technical Working Group, residing in Toek Laak Village, Kraing Leav Commune, Rolea Bier District. The above incident happened at around 10:10 am on January 19, 2024 at Prek Lvea point in Tamal Leu village, Koh Thkov commune, Chulkiri district.
