UN experts say Israeli invasion of Gaza violates international law
MADRID (Reuters) - Israel's "merciless" bombing of the Gaza Strip that destroyed cities and killed thousands of Palestinians is a violation of the law, a UN human rights expert said on Thursday. International. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on January 19, 2024.
The comments by Francesca Albanese, an Italian lawyer and UN special rapporteur on the Palestinian territories, come at a time when Israel is facing a South African case at the International Court of Justice. United Nations on charges of genocide.
Albanese told a news conference in Madrid that while Israel has the right to defend itself, international humanitarian law must also be respected "to protect innocent people who do not take part in the fighting."
She added that this means that Israel must differentiate between fighters and civilians and ensure that military strikes are proportionate to avoid excessive harm to civilians.
Fighting has devastated Palestinian territory since Hamas launched an offensive in southern Israel, killing at least 1,140 people, mostly civilians, according to AFP. Based on official Israeli figures.
