The President and Mr. Makrong also discussed the implementation of other projects aimed at the protection and promotion of Cambodia's heritage, including the renovation and expansion of the National Museum in Phnom Penh. In this regard, both sides welcome the signing of a letter of intent on cooperation in the field of museums and heritage.
During the meeting, both sides stressed the importance of political pluralism and the full protection of fundamental rights to ensure the strength of democracy. The two sides agreed to strengthen cooperation in these areas, both within the framework of bilateral relations and multilateral frameworks. The important role of civil society in finding solutions to global problems is also recognized.
