Ukraine claims new attack on Russian oil depot
Ukraine says it was behind a drone strike that triggered a massive fire at an oil depot in western Russia on Friday (January 19). The latest round of cross-border attacks is on the rise. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on January 19, 2024.
It is the second attack on a Russian oil depot in recent days and is part of what Kiev describes as Moscow's retaliation for an attack on Ukraine's energy infrastructure.
A Ukrainian security source confirmed to AFP that the operation was carried out by the intelligence department of the Ukrainian Ministry of Defense, without giving further details.
The video clip shows a large missile penetrating the depot's fuel tank as black smoke billows across the city, which has a population of about 60,000.
However, he had previously announced that no one was killed or injured as 13 fire trucks were deployed to put out the blaze. Toyota Cambodia on ALPHARD Vehicles and Parts in Cambodia
