(Phnom Penh): On January 18, 2024, at the Office of the Mine Authority, on behalf of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Authority, Dr. Ly Thuch, Senior Minister and First Vice President of the Mine Authority, met with Mr. MA Shengkun. Deputy Director of the Arms Control Department of the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs on Strengthening Cooperation and Humanitarian Mine Action Assistance in Cambodia.
Mr. MA Shengkun stated that prior to the meeting with HE Senior Minister Ly Thuch, he and the delegation visited to learn about demining activities in the field organized by the Cambodian Mine Action Center and Mr. MA clearly understood the need. And Cambodia's challenges in clearing mines and explosive remnants of war.
Mr. MA highly appreciated Cambodia's achievements, experience and expertise in the field of mine action and thanked the Mine Authority for its excellent cooperation during the visit.
On behalf of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Ministry of Defense of the People's Republic of China, MA is committed to continuing to support mine action cooperation, which is a priority of the Royal Government of Cambodia, until Cambodia achieves its goals.
He praised the mission of MA Shengkun and his delegation in Cambodia to strengthen cooperation in humanitarian mine action, and affirmed that the Chinese government and people have made significant contributions to the reduction of casualties. Reduce poverty in Cambodia by clearing mines and providing safe land for cultivation.
On behalf of Samdech Hun Manet, Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mines Authority, he thanked the Chinese government and people for their continued partnership and support for humanitarian mine action in Cambodia, including funding, grants, materials and capacity building in Cambodia. .
