NEC Presents the Outcome of the Meeting to Review and Decide on the Comments of Stakeholders on the Draft Regulations and Procedures for the 4th Mandate Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Council Elections
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the National Election Committee (NEC), held a meeting on the morning of January 18, 2024 to review and decide on the opinions of stakeholders on the draft regulations and Procedures for Capital Council Election, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council, Khan Council, 4th Mandate 2024.
Mr. Tep Nytha, Secretary General of the NEC, reported to the NEC meeting that the NEC had submitted the draft regulations and procedures for the Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and District Council elections. Khan Council of the fourth mandate 2024 to 86 stakeholders on December 18, 2023 to provide advice.
These parties include the General Secretariat of the Constitutional Council, the legislature, the Royal Government, which is involved in the election, 26 political parties, non-governmental organizations and a total of 26 associations. Thirty-two institutions commented, revised and agreed, and submitted the draft regulations and procedures for the election to the NEC by December 20, 2023.
After listening to the report of the Secretary General of the NEC, the NEC meeting reviewed and discussed in detail the contents of the recommendations point by point, then the NEC meeting decided to approve the regulations. And Procedures for the Election of Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council, Khan Council, 4th Mandate 2024, which have 2 chapters, 13 sections and 7 annexes.
According to the calendar of the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council, Khan Council, the fourth mandate will be held on Sunday, May 26, 2024.
