(Kampong Speu): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, on January 18, 2024, chaired an inter-ministerial committee consisting of the Ministry of Rural Development, the Ministry of Economy and Finance and with the participation of Major General Rin Rith, Deputy Director of the Department of Engineering, Ministry of Defense. The nation inspected the results of the reconstruction of two lines in Udong and Samrong Tong districts, Kampong Speu province.
A 5,050-meter-long, 6-meter-wide gravel road, a 15-meter-long, 9-meter-wide concrete bridge and a double-sided drainage bridge were damaged by floods in 2021. The road and the above construction are located from Trapeang Chrov village to Tuol village, Prey Krasaing commune, Oudong district, Kampong Speu province, implemented by the Department of Engineering, Ministry of National Defense.
The event was attended by Mr. Tum Pen Virakvitou, Chairman of the Reporting Team for the Author of the Double Prince and Mr. Ieng Pisey, Researcher of the book "Hun Sen Kampuchea" and Mr. Lat Phirun, Deputy Governor of Prey Veng Province, representing Mr. Suon Somalin, Provincial Governor. Invitation from various departments and units around the 13 provinces, municipalities, districts, a large number of students.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Ieng Pisey, a researcher and author of the book "Hun Sen Cambodia", said that this book is a reflection of the heroic heroism of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister of Cambodia, who took his life as a capital to Motherland and for the full rights and freedoms of the people, especially to seek peace for the motherland.
Mr. Tum Pen Virakvitou said that the preparation of this lecture is very important to promote the priceless heroic example of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and many other important figures in the fight. The struggle to overthrow the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, which brutally massacred the Cambodian people themselves from 1975 to 1979, lasted for 3 years, 8 months and 20 days.
Deputy Governor of Prey Veng Province added that, of course, the book "Hun Sen Cambodia" highlights the meaning of the life and political history of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the unification, reconciliation, national development from the rubble of the war to save the country. The ashes of building a country from scratch to achieve peace, political stability and development in all areas and have everything as it is today.
(Phnom Penh): A senior civil aviation official said that the construction project of Koh Rong International Airport (Class 4C) worth $ 300 million invested by Royal Group Koh Rong Development Company of Duke Kith Meng has started gradually. Currently, the company has been clearing the land.
Sin Chanserivutha, Undersecretary of State and Spokesman for the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, told Fresh News on January 18, 2024 that the Royal Group Koh Rong is currently clearing land after the company resolved the issue. Social impact with the people in the area.
It should be informed that on January 18, 2023, the Secretariat of Civil Aviation and the Royal Group Koh Rong Development Company of Oknha Kith Meng signed an agreement and approved the master plan for the construction of Koh Rong International Airport on Koh Rong Development Zone, Koh Rong City, Preah Province. Sihanouk.
Earlier, Duke Kith Meng reaffirmed his commitment to build the $ 300 million Koh Rong International Airport (4C) on Koh Rong Development Zone, Koh Rong City, Preah Sihanouk Province, in accordance with the master plan signed at January 18, 2023, the airport will take 5 years to build.
Koh Rong International Airport is the fourth new international airport to be invested with the participation of the private sector after Darasakor International Airport, Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport and Techo International Airport.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha said that the construction of this airport to facilitate the travel of tourists, and according to research, any tourist area with an airport is more developed than any tourist area without an airport.
