71-year-old grandmother in charge of raising 7 orphans received a gift from the head of the working group to help Sraem commune, Choam Ksan district
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Duong Samneang, Deputy Chief of Choam Ksan District Field Team and Chairman of Sraem Commune Field Team, on the morning of January 18, 2024, led the team to visit and deliver some gifts. Mrs. Soeur Ya, 71 years old, lives in Thomacheat village, Sra Em commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province, who has a poor life and raises seven orphaned grandsons and daughters.
Seeing the difficulty of the grandmother's family in defecating without proper toilets, Mr. Duong Samneang and his wife and his team built a new toilet, 1.5 meters by 2 meters, with a galvanized roof. At a cost of 1,686,500 Riel, handed over to him at this time.
