Rotary Club, Santosasa Singapore and Cambodian Community Dreams Provide Computers, School Supplies, Bicycles and Shoes to Banteay Srei Students
(Siem Reap): On the afternoon of January 17, 2024, Rotary Club, Santosa Club, Singapore and Cambodian Community Dreams brought 15 computers, 50 bicycles, sports equipment and shoes to needy students in Phnom Penh. Khun Ream Secondary School, Khun Ream Commune, Banteay Srey District, Siem Reap Province.
The event was held in the presence of Mr. Pich Sophatra, Deputy Director of the Secondary Education Office of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Siem Reap Province, and Ms. Jenny Lipa, President of the Cambodian Community Dreams Organization, and Mr. Jack Lin, President of the Rotary Club of Santosa Singapore, as well as colleagues and local authorities, teachers. Students as well as parents are involved.
Ms. Soeun Soksen, Principal of Khun Ream Secondary School, said that this is the second time that Rotary Club Santosa Singapore has provided to Khun Ream Secondary School and also built 4 toilets for the school and provided equipment. Learn more too.
She requested Rotary Club, Santosa, Singapore and Cambodian Community Dream to help build a building to meet the needs of students in the coming year.
Mr. Pich Sophatra thanked Rotary Club, Santosa Singapore and Community Dreams Cambodia for their continued support of students in key rural areas in Banteay Srei District.
He said that these bicycles are also a vehicle for you to travel to study and provide benefits to you to build your future to the happiness of the family and you will be a strong pillar of human resources. In the future development of the society.
Mr. Pich Sophatra also expressed his generosity of the organization, which always pays attention to the Royal Government of Cambodia in training human resources at the local level by providing transportation and study materials, clothing to poor students who lack access. Traveling to school is important, providing computers to the school to train students.
He urged the organization to continue the tradition of supporting the education sector in Cambodia, as well as in Siem Reap, where schools are in short supply. He also instructed teachers, students, as well as parents and the school management committee to take care of the school property equipped by the organization to use long-term food.
Ms. Jenny Lipa and Mr. Abi Jacobs, Rotary Club of Santosa Singapore, expressed their pleasure to meet with the students in a warm and friendly welcome, which made the delegates unforgettable memories of Khun Ream Secondary School students under the roof of peace. .
They said that the donations to poor students in Cambodia are not different from the intention of Rotary Club Santosa Singapore, which has joined the Royal Government of Cambodia in training human resources in remote areas.
He also gave some good advice to students to adhere to ethics, to respect the advice of teachers, parents and seniors so that we become an important resource of the country, especially everyone must work hard to learn. It is a fixed property that does not go away.
He stressed that in order to become a good student, all students must have patience, diligence, study, understand all the work according to the curriculum and listen to the explanations of teachers and have the courage to study.
In addition, the Director General of Rotary Club, Santosa Singapore, also said that Rotary continues to help poor students in Cambodia as much as possible. The organization also signed a memorandum of understanding (MoU) in partnership between Rotary Club, Santosa Singapore and the Cambodian Community Dream Organization.
