BEIJING: China's economy grew 5.2 percent in the fourth quarter of 2023 from the same period in 2022, slightly below analysts' expectations, official data showed on Wednesday. Respond to the direction of Beijing. According to Reuters.
Contrary to many analysts' expectations, the world's second-largest economy has struggled to recover to a strong and sustainable recovery following the crisis-hit Kovid-19 outbreak. Real estate lengthened consumer confidence and business declines, rising regional government debt and slowing global economic growth.
For the full year 2023, Reuters reported, citing data released by the National Bureau of Statistics (NBS), that the superpower's economy grew by 5.2 percent, in part due to lower base influence last year. Acne mainly affects people in the western hemisphere. Analysts forecast full-year economic growth of 5.2 percent.
Compared with the third quarter of 2023, China's economy grew by only 1 percent during the October-December 2023 period, while in the third quarter it grew by 1.5 percent.
