Minister Sok Soken presented the current status and vision for the development of tourism in Cambodia in the future, including the joint strategic initiative of the Ministry of Tourism to turn Cambodia into a vibrant tourism destination, sustainable competition and environment. Focusing on five strategic pillars called "Build 5-Build" as well as three supporting components called "Development 3-3Ds".
The Ambassador of Iran expressed his sincere appreciation for the strategic and visionary development of Cambodia's tourism sector and the high level of attention paid by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The ambassador also praised Cambodia for having a good policy for Muslims with more halal restaurants.
"We will help promote Cambodia as a major destination for the people of Iran and will work to promote direct flights between Tehran and Phnom Penh in the future," the ambassador said.
