Former Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra will be eligible for bail next month
Former Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra will be released on bail next month, officials at the Thai Ministry of Corrections said on Wednesday. His age and health. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on January 17, 2024.
Thaksin, 74, was hospitalized with high blood pressure and chest tightness just hours after returning to Thailand in August after 15 years in exile.
Thaksin was sentenced to eight years in prison for abuse of power, but his sentence was commuted to one year after receiving a royal pardon.
Last week, the prison administration extended his stay at the police hospital, citing the need to monitor his health.
Thaksin was ousted in a military coup in 2006 and is at the heart of Thailand's 17-year unrest that has influenced the politics of his deportation.
