(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has issued guidelines for radio and television stations to sell or rent airtime to political parties to promote their political programs while campaigning for the party's election. Politics for the 5th Senate Election 2024.
The senior NEC official said that the sale or lease of airtime to political parties to promote the policies of political parties must be based on the principle of equality, equal value and in order of precedence. The owners of the radio and television stations are not responsible for the content of the policies of the political parties. Political parties are responsible for the content of their campaigns.
Radio and television station owners must abide by the law on the election of senators and the rules and procedures for elections, and these principles to disseminate policies during the election campaign.
In addition, in the event that the NEC finds that the content of the campaign violates the Law on the Election of Senators and the Rules and Procedures for the Election of Senators, the NEC has the right to request that political parties If the NEC still refuses to correct, the NEC has the right to revoke or stop the radio and television station from broadcasting the entire election campaign content and taking legal action.
In particular, national and international associations and non-governmental organizations and the media who wish to organize a Q&A session or discussion can consult with the Voter Education Coordinating Committee and disseminate political party policy programs before launching the program. Here are some issues such as:
* Technical characteristics to be prepared * Topics or questions to be submitted to political parties * Coordination of meeting place, security and safety.
He stressed that the program manager, Q&A or discussion on party policies must be neutral and impartial.
According to the NEC calendar, the political parties' election campaign for the 5th legislative election for the 2024 Senate will take place from 10 to 23 February. The four candidates for the by-elections are: the Cambodian People's Party, the Khmer Will Party, the National Forces Party, and FUNCINPEC.
It should be noted that for the upcoming Senate election on February 25, there are 125 MPs in the current position, including 17 women and 11,622 Commune / Sangkat Councilors, including 2 women. , 568 people.
Snail truck crashes into Chinese truck, injuring six in Kandal province
(Central): At least six Cambodians and a Chinese man were seriously and lightly injured in a traffic accident caused by a snail truck driven by a young man who crashed into an Alpha truck carrying Chinese people. Immediately after the incident, all the victims were sent to the emergency room overnight at the hospital in Phnom Penh.
This incident happened on January 16, 2024 at 20:20 on National Road 21 in Prek Pang village, Koh Khel commune, Saang district, Kandal province.
The same source said that after the incident, the competent authorities of the Saang District Police Inspectorate inspected and measured the scene and took the relevant evidence to be kept at the Saang District Police Inspectorate to build a case according to the procedure. The families of the six injured were taken to Phnom Penh Hospital for treatment.
