On the first day of a working mission in Switzerland, Samdech Hun Sen met with 6 world-class companies
(Davos, Switzerland): During the first day of a working mission in Davos, Switzerland, on Tuesday, January 16, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Hun Sen, allowed six world-class companies to meet. Be polite and discuss work.
The six companies are from various countries invited to the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland. Some companies are investing in Cambodia as well. In the meeting with these six companies, Samdech Hun Sen presented policies and incentives related to investment and encouraged them to invest in Cambodia or expand their investment. 1: Meeting with the CEO of HawkEye 360 Inc
HawkEye 360 is a radio frequency data analysis company established in 2015. The company has developed aerial network and radio frequency solutions to monitor air, land and water transport.
The company serves the maritime, defense and telecommunications industries, traveling through satellites to search, identify and locate a wide range of radio frequency bands to help consumers around the world.
Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet welcomed the meeting with the CEO. He expressed his pleasure at the company's intention to co-invest with local partners, encouraging the company to continue to study the feasibility of investing in geospatial information technology.
She also confirmed the company's intention to continue to cooperate with partners in Cambodia to bring more tourists to visit Cambodia, a beautiful country and a very attractive tourist destination.
The Prime Minister welcomed the Company's intention to expand its investment activities in Cambodia, especially through cooperation with local partners, while the Royal Government of the seventh mandate has been setting out the necessary policies and mechanisms to promote The growth of tourism in the aftermath of the Kovid-19 crisis.
Hun Manet welcomed the company's intention to invest in Cambodia, especially the production of solar power equipment, and encouraged partnerships with local Cambodian companies interested in the model. This new type of business.
The Prime Minister thanked Grab for investing in Cambodia in the transportation sector. He said that Grab's business model has made a significant contribution to attracting and mobilizing informal operators, especially in the transportation sector, to Grab's growing digital nursery.
He supported Grab's commitment to encourage businesses to use the Grab digital nursery as a model for respecting traffic laws, providing safety and comfort to its customers on a regular basis.
Mr. Jared Cohen also informed the President about the intention to expand its investment opportunities to Cambodia and expressed confidence that under the honorary leadership of the Prime Minister of Cambodia will continue to develop with confidence and macro stability. Complete economy and peace.
Hun Manet expressed his pleasure and welcome to the company's intention to invest in Cambodia and encouraged the company to cooperate with all stakeholders in Cambodia to study and understand the potential of Cambodia and the possibility of real investment.
