(Phnom Penh): At least 56 foreigners were successfully rescued by Cambodian police from the same kidnapping incident, while two Bangladeshi ringleaders were also arrested by the Cambodian police. That operation, too. This is according to the release by the General Department of Immigration on the morning of January 17, 2024.
Pursuant to the complaint of intervention and rescue of Bangladeshis on December 14, 2023, the Investigation and Enforcement Department of the General Department of Immigration conducted an investigation until January 11, 2024 and arrested 58 foreigners. Two locations in Daun Penh district, Phnom Penh, in which 56 foreigners were victims and 2 Bangladeshi foreigners were suspected of being the masterminds involved in the case of illegal immigration.
The 56 victims were of three nationalities (51 Bangladeshis, 4 Indians and 1 Sri Lankan) and were dragged to Cambodia to find separate jobs for non-English speakers and computers. Thailand and Malaysia.
Currently, the 56 foreign victims, with the coordination of the Ministry of Social Affairs, have been handed over to Caritas Cambodia-Kandal. Two Bangladeshis suspected of being masterminds in connection with a case of smuggling with the aim of building a case to be sent to court and continue to search for four other foreign suspects who escaped to take Follow the procedure.
Mr. Yim Viseth said that the Ministry of Mines and Energy recently introduced a policy called "Principles for Permitting the Use of Solar Energy on Roofs in Cambodia" with the vision of improving management. Allow the use of solar energy on the roof in Cambodia clearly, efficiently, transparently, equally, accountably and equitably.
Based on the content of the principles for permitting the use of solar energy on the roof in Cambodia, defined roles, duties and responsibilities of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, Electricity Authority of Cambodia, Electricite du Cambodge (EDC), electricity suppliers, system installation service providers Sunlight on the roof and consumers.
The contents of the draft regulations on the installation and use of solar roof systems in Cambodia, which are ready to be discussed and collected, are limited to the main principles and conditions, such as:
First, the principles for permitting the use of solar energy on the roof in Cambodia
Second: Announcement of quota for installation of solar roof system on an annual basis
Third, the procedure for applying for a permit to install and use a solar system on the roof and the issuance of a permit by the Electricity Authority of Cambodia
Fourth: Procedures for installation of solar power system on the roof and registration of system installation by the Electricity Authority of Cambodia
Fifth, the conditions and procedures for the users of the solar system on the roof type 1, which is planned to be connected to the national grid system
Sixth: Procedures for resizing existing solar systems
Seventh: Requirements for the installation of solar power systems on the roofs of large-scale consumers, medium-voltage users and bulk consumers-existing high-voltage consumers and already authorized within the framework of regulations On the general conditions for connecting the power source from the solar power system to the power supply system or with the power system located in the power supply system of the national grid
8th: Procedures for changing ownership
9th: Procedures for dismantling the system
10th: Calculation of electricity tariffs for consumers who install solar energy systems connected to the national grid. Civil servants and their dependents
