(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Rath Sovannarak, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, on January 16, 2024, attended the handing over ceremony and inauguration ceremony of Teuk Laok Peace Community Kindergarten, located in Toek Laok Village, Sep Commune, Kampong Tralach District, Kampong Chhnang Province. .
Education is an important core for Cambodia's sustainable growth. Pre-school education not only provides children with a place to study, but also gives them the opportunity to expand and express their creativity. The construction of Teuk Laok Peace Community Kindergarten is an initiative of the National Bank of Cambodia and Teuk Laok Village Community and is sponsored by KREDIT BURO (Cambodia) Co., Ltd.
Mr. Rath Sovannarak, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, said, "Pre-primary education before entering primary school will help establish reading habits and help children to be disciplined, moral and behave appropriately from an early age. "Relieving the burden on people with small children can have time to earn a living."
Oeur Sothearoth, Chief Executive Officer of KREDIT Bureau Roe Cambodia, said: “Participating in social work is one of our commitments to contribute to development, especially in the field of education. In addition, this year, under the initiative of the National Bank of Cambodia, we have supported the construction and establishment of this Peaceful Water Community Kindergarten to allow all children in the community to have easy access to everyone.
In addition, Mr. Oeur Sothearoth added: “CBC strongly hopes that community kindergartens will be the starting point for children in the community and an important training ground to connect them to the next level of education at public schools. Continuing. Children are the main bamboo shoots for our society. "CBC will continue to be committed to contributing to society, education and finance."
The inauguration ceremony was also attended by advisors from the National and International Festival Committee of Kampong Tralach District Administration, Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Education of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, CEOs and associates of KREDIT Buroro Cambodia, as well as 40 children, elders and relevant authorities. Also in the community with a total of 150 participants.
