Cambodia, Hong Kong hold second meeting of Joint Commission on Economic Cooperation
The purpose of this meeting is to monitor the progress of the work and to promote better cooperation in the fields of economy, trade, investment and other priority areas in accordance with the content of the Agreement on Economic Cooperation between Cambodia and Hungary, which was signed. Signed on June 13, 2019 during Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia for the 6th term, paid an official visit to Hungary.
As a result of the meeting, the two sides noted the progress of cooperation in all fields, especially the increase in bilateral trade volume in 2022 by 84% compared to 2021, which shows a significant positive step. Identified and agreed to further strengthen cooperation in priority areas, such as:
In the economic and trade sectors, the two sides expressed their willingness to continue to increase the bilateral trade volume to its potential level and encouraged businesses and investors to seek additional business opportunities, especially in key sectors such as: products. And agricultural technology, manufacturing, environment, health and information and communication technology (ICT).
At the same time, the two sides also discussed cooperation and support for Cambodia's future exit process from the Least Developed Countries (LDCs).
The two sides also agreed to continue discussing cooperation on credit projects, especially in the fields of agriculture, food security and water resources management, and pledged to continue international development cooperation.
The two sides signed the joint minutes of the meeting in a friendly and cordial atmosphere and agreed to prepare for the third meeting at an appropriate date.
Cambodia exports major commodities to the Hungarian market, including grain, tobacco, electrical appliances, clothing, mechanical equipment, steel and footwear. Goods imported from Hungary include medicines, machinery and mechanical equipment, toys, dairy products.
