The wife of the national badminton player who was hit by a Jeep in Tuol Kork district and the family who complained to the perpetrator's mother will come to clarify the summons of the prosecutor's office on the 24th of January
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Kruy Chhin Liang, the wife of the national badminton player who was hit by a Jeep in Tuol Kork district, claimed that she and her relatives who were sued by the mother of the perpetrator will testify at the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on January 24, 2024, according to the deadline of the prosecutor's office, although he has not yet received civil damages.
"Now, less than 100 days after my husband's death, I have gone from being a victim to being a suspect in another case, even though my husband's case has not been resolved," she said. As for the court summons, I am not afraid to comment in this case, because I and all family members stand on justice and ask for justice for my husband.
As for civil compensation, Ms. Kruy Chhin Liang, as the plaintiff, will also testify on January 29, 2024.
Please be informed that the case of a Jeep car that hit a national team player and died in Tuol Kork district recently, leaving his wife and baby orphaned, now a new picture has been leaked and has been widely distributed. According to social media, the mother of the perpetrator filed a lawsuit against the victim's wife and four relatives of the victim for "public defamation" until the prosecutor's office issued a summons.
Deputy Prosecutor Seng Meng Srun has ordered the four defendants to testify at the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on the morning of January 24, 2024, going to the second floor of Room "P" Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
Regarding this case, especially at the same time as the summons issued following the complaint of the perpetrator's mother, many criticisms on social media continued to fall, with social media users all expressing outrage and some saying that they had just seen This is the first time that the perpetrators have killed others and sued them, even though the 100-day funeral has not yet taken place.
Social media users recalled a phrase that was allegedly uttered by the perpetrator's family as the perpetrator was fleeing after the provocation, "If the lawsuit is filed, the future will be ruined." The word was heard when a representative of the perpetrator brought $ 1,000 to the victim's funeral and ordered the victim not to file a complaint.
In particular, for the perpetrator, when the provocation caused the death of others, he refused to take responsibility before the law, that is, tried to escape until this story surprised the special leadership, Mr. Keut Rith, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Justice. Ordered the representative of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to issue an order for the perpetrator to be held accountable before the law, while the Phnom Penh Municipal Police investigated carefully to find the arrest.
