Letters from readers! Status of Opposition Political Parties in the 5th Senate Election in Cambodia
Sunday, February 25, 2024 is the date of the 5th Senate election. This election shall be conducted in accordance with the proportional system and the distribution of seats by constituency shall follow the highest average formula as defined in Article 135 of the Law on the Election of the National Assembly.
Voters and constituencies are the members of the National Assembly elected in 2023, with a total of 125 members, and 11,622 members of the Commune / Sangkat Council elected in 2022.
For the 5th Senate election, there are 4 parties participating in the election, including: the Cambodian People's Party in the first place, the Khmer Will Party in the second place, which is an alliance of the Candlelight Party because the Candlelight Party does not have Just enough documents, there are more than 2,000 voters, FUNCINPEC in third place and National Forces in fourth place, the new opposition party on the official list of the National Election Commission.
Please be reminded that in 2023, four parties, including the Candlelight Party, the Khmer Will Party, the Local Democrat Party and the Cambodian Reform Party, which are not yet a party in the National Assembly, have formed an alliance. . The formation of the alliance comes as the Candlelight Party, an opposition party, is unable to contest any elections due to the lack of original documents of its party registration at the Ministry of Interior.
In a joint statement issued after the announcement of the political alliance, the leaders of the four parties said: "The alliance towards the future will be a new driving force for motivation and encouragement, as well as the choice of "Cambodian people to participate in building a democratic society, social justice, equitable and sustainable development, as well as harmony for the entire Cambodian nation in the future."
In the national election on July 23, 2023, the Candlelight Party failed to stand for election due to lack of original documents confirming the registration of political parties at the Ministry of Interior. The Cambodian Reform Party has boycotted the election.
On December 11, 2023, the National Election Committee (NEC) simultaneously decided for the Khmer Will Party and the National Forces Party to participate in the 5th legislative election for the 2024 Senate. Both opposition parties have stepped up their campaign to attract more than 2,000 members of the Candlelight Party's commune council, while the Khmer Will Party has gained the right to replace the Candlelight Party.
Separately, the National Forces Party, whose leader split from the Candlelight Party and ran for office, is also expected to draw more or less voters from the Candlelight Party and hope to win seats in the by-elections. The new Senate.
Chea Mony, spokesman for the National Forces Party, expects the commune councils of the Phleung Tien party to support the party, as the leaders of the split National Party have worked together in the past. Go. This is according to the broadcast of Radio Free Asia.
As for the advisor of the National Forces Party, Mr. Rong Chhun, he announced to find a solution with the Candlelight Party to participate in the Senate election so as not to split the vote. The National Forces Party gives the option to the Candlelight Party to divide the region to stand for the Senate election in February.
Son Chhay wants to see the National Forces Party should consider the 2027 and 2028 election plans better.
According to Radio Free Asia, the executive director of the Cambodian election watchdog Nicfec, Sam Kuntheamy, said the two parties were vying for the same vote, thus reducing the number of votes and could put both parties at risk. Loss of seats in the Senate. He said that although the constituencies of the two parties are from the Candlelight Party, it is not certain that all constituencies will vote for the same Khmer Will Party.
Pursuant to the Law on the Amendment of the Law on Political Parties, the new Article 18 clearly states: "A person who is a convicted felon must be imprisoned for a felony or misdemeanor without parole."
On the other hand, according to the reply letter of the Minister of Justice to Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the Election Commission in May 2023, it is stated that Mr. Rong Chhun has not yet fully rehabilitated according to the law. Within 5 years from the date of execution, there are not enough conditions to apply for rehabilitation in court in accordance with Articles 534 and 535 of the Code of Criminal Procedure.
In the judgment of the Court of Appeal, the Supreme Court upheld the Criminal Judgment No. 110 and sentenced Mr. Rong Chhun to 2 years imprisonment, which was changed to 1 year 3 months 11 days imprisonment. The remaining sentence is suspended for a period of three years.
