The Court of Appeal and the Prosecutor General of Tbong Khmum Court of Appeal held a meeting to review the work in 2023 and raise the direction for 2024
(Tbong Khmum): Tbong Khmum Court of Appeal and the Attorney General of Tbong Khmum Court of Appeal on January 15, 2024 held a meeting to review the work of 2023 and work direction for implementation in 2024 under the chairmanship of Mr. Mong Monichakriya Tbong Khmum Appeal and Mr. Huot Vuthy, Attorney General of Tbong Khmum Appeal Court at Tbong Khmum Appeal Court Hall, 2nd floor, located in Nikom Leu Village, Sralop Commune, Tbong Khmum District, Tbong Khmum Province.
The meeting was held with the participation of the Chief Prosecutor of the Court of First Instance and the Prosecutor of the 8 Provincial Courts under the jurisdiction of the Judge, Prosecutor, Clerk, Secretary General, Deputy Secretary General, Director of the Department, Director of the Secretariat and relevant officials. Many.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Huot Vuthy said that this year, as well as last year, the Tbong Khmum Court of Appeal and the Attorney General of Tbong Khmum Court of Appeal held a meeting to review the work and set the direction for the next year to review the technical and administrative work and what? The main purpose of the conference is to ask you to raise the challenges that have arisen in the past with the relevant institutions.
The Prosecutor General also commended the judges, prosecutors, clerks, officials of the General Secretariat and relevant units for their responsible cooperation since the establishment of the Tbong Khmum Appeal Court and the Tbong Khmum Court of Appeal. In the cause to serve the justice sector to the people.
Mr. Tum Sophoan, Secretary General, also read the report on 2022 implemented in the past, with the discussion of the summary report and the coordination between the President and the Prosecutor General by sharing experiences on measures to address the issue. Clogging the case with discussions on challenges under the theme "Providing justice quickly, accurately, fairly and without corruption" is an important entry point for the judiciary.
During the meeting to review the work results of 2023 and the work direction for implementation in 2024, Mr. Mong Monichakriya said that the efforts of the Court of Appeal and the Attorney General of the Court of Appeal this year have achieved good results. Appreciate and appreciate the achievements throughout the year.
Mr. Mong Monichakriya requested all clerks in the Court of Appeal and the Prosecutor General to continue their efforts with high commitment to actively participate in the performance of their duties and expressed their appreciation to all officials. In the institution of the Court of Appeal and the Attorney General of the Court of Appeal, who have worked hard to fulfill their roles and responsibilities to achieve more new results and achievements.
At the end of the meeting to review the work of 2023 and the direction of work in 2024, Mr. Mong Monichakriya, President of Tbong Khmum Appeal Court and Mr. Huot Vuthy, Chief Prosecutor of Tbong Khmum Appeal Court presented certificates of appreciation to outstanding officials. Complete the past with a happy atmosphere and a smile. River bank collapse affects more than 40 families in Stung Trang district, the provincial governor inspected to intervene
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on the morning of January 16, 2024, led a group of relevant officials to inspect the situation of river bank collapse, which affected the homes of about 40 families living along The Mekong River from Prek Kak commune to Khpob Ta Nuon commune in Stung Trang district and affect some concrete roads and asphalt roads.
Mr. Un Chanda said that the riverbank situation in some communes in Stung Trang district collapsed after the river receded, affecting the homes of about 40 families and affecting concrete roads and Some paved roads as well.
According to the provincial governor, the communes affected by the river bank collapse are: Prek Kak commune, Peam Koh Sna commune, Preah Andong commune and Khpob Ta Nuon commune, with a total length of more than 1,000 meters. Severe damage is in Prek Kak commune, which may face the cutting of concrete roads, making it impossible for villagers to travel.
Separately, in Preah Andong commune, it was severely affected, about 100 meters long, and Khpob Taoun commune, more than 100 meters long, which could affect people's houses and concrete roads.
According to the provincial governor, the working group that inspected the riverbank situation had the provincial authority and the technical director general representing the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology to study the matter with the Ministry of Economy and Finance to ask for guidelines. The Minister of Water Resources examines the possibility of repairing the broken bank immediately.
