TOKYO (Reuters) - US military helicopters in Japan are set to deploy to the quake-hit Noto Peninsula off the west coast to help rescue efforts in disrupted communities. This is according to the release by Reuters on Tuesday, January 16, 2024.
The quake destroyed roads and evacuated people by sea, meaning some vulnerable people could only be evacuated by air. Details of the rescue mission will be officially announced on Tuesday.
More than 220 people have been confirmed dead in the Jan. 1 quake, which destroyed thousands of homes, vital infrastructure and cut off electricity in remote areas. Rescue efforts were also hampered by more earthquakes, which put the risk of landslides and added damage to already damaged infrastructure.
