Cambodian Red Cross welcomes the exchange visit of the Red Cross Youth Delegation of the Republic of Korea Usan Branch (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, Acting Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross welcomes the second exchange visit of the delegation. The 45-member delegation of the Red Cross Youth of the Republic of Korea, Usan Branch, led by Ms. LEE MINSEON, presided over the meeting, which took place at the headquarters of the Cambodian Red Cross.
On January 15, 2024, the Acting Secretary-General expressed her pleasure and warm welcome to the eight-day exchange visit from January 14 to 21, 2024. Red Cross Youth Delegation of the Republic of Korea, Usan Branch with the Cambodian Red Cross.
The Acting Secretary General gave a presentation on the history of the Cambodian Red Cross, which was established on 18 February 1955 and has Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Queen Mother of Cambodia, as its Honorary President since 1994. Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen was elected President of the Cambodian Red Cross by the General Assembly from the second mandate from 1998 to the current seventh mandate.
In addition, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak highlighted the recent important activities that the Cambodian Red Cross hosted (Round 3) of the 20th Leaders' Meeting and the 2nd Youth Forum of the National Red Cross and Red Crescent Society. The Red Crescent, the Southeast Asian region, as well as activities to promote the environment, prevent climate change through tree planting and campaigns to reduce the use of plastic bags.
Ms. LEE MINSEON, Head of Youth Delegation of the Red Cross of the Republic of Korea, Usan Branch, expressed her deep gratitude for the presentation of the Cambodian Red Cross, which reflects the humanitarian activities similar to the work of the Red Cross of the Republic of Korea. She thanked the Cambodian Red Cross team for their warm hospitality during their stay in Cambodia, as well as for facilitating the exchange visit.
At the same time, she emphasized that the Red Cross of the Republic of Korea and the Cambodian Red Cross have always had good cooperation in the past, therefore, this second exchange of experiences will bring the two national associations closer. Long-term unity and friendship. Svay Rieng Provincial Authority Calls on Business Owners to Strengthen Prevention and Cooperate with Authorities to Secure Their Locations from Drug Cases
