Mr. Neth Pheaktra allowed Mr. Chhay Sophal to pay a courtesy call and present 100 copies of the book entitled "37 Prime Ministers of Cambodia - Political and Social Turns in the Fire of War and Peace"
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, on the morning of January 15, 2024, allowed Dr. Chhay Sophal, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Information and Author of the book, to pay a courtesy call and present a book entitled "Prime Minister 37". Images of Cambodia - Political and Social Turn in the Flames of War and Peace "100 copies to the Minister and the General Department under the Ministry of Information.
Dr. Chhay Sophal, currently Secretary of State at the Ministry of Information, this week released his new book, "37 Prime Ministers of Cambodia - Political and Social Turns in the Fire, War and Peace", featuring the Prime Minister's biography. Thirty-seven Cambodians and political, economic and social twists in each phase as the country fell into the flames of a bloody war until the country achieved complete peace.
According to the author, since 1945, the year the world ended World War II, Cambodia has had 37 prime ministers, including eight dynasties (Sen Norodom). 3 members and 5 Sisowath members) and 29 members.
Dr. Chhay Sophal stated that of the 37 Cambodian Prime Ministers, most were in office, but did not have much power and influence, as power rested with the King, the Head of State, and the pro-imperialists. After the coup, only four prime ministers have the power and influence of the world, including:
* First: His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King, who reigned as both King, Head of State and Prime Minister. He officially declared independence from the French colony in 1953 and built the Independence Monument to represent Cambodia's independence and developed a prominent country in Asia before the country fell into the flames of war on State Day. March 18, 1970
* Second: Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, the son of a farmer, risked his life and sacrificed his own happiness for the nation and the motherland, including:
Tear life with tears from a six-month-pregnant wife to rescue millions of people waiting to die from the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime and restore the country from scratch with other elites. And until the country has developed to the present for the successor.
* Raindrops are the shadow and reliance of farmers, laborers and workers, both inside and outside the economic framework, as well as people across the country.
* The first Cambodian elite to bring the highest level of Khmer Rouge genocidal leaders to justice for national and human history, as well as the world, without wanting such a brutal regime to recur in Cambodia.
* The first Cambodian elite to strive for a peaceful end to the border dispute with the three neighboring countries, including Vietnam, Thailand and Laos, to have a clear and precise border post according to the map that Cambodia has deposited at the United Nations. Before 1970, in order to prevent the next generation of Cambodians from continuing to suffer because the borders of the territory were not clear and were constantly being violated and moved, leading to further loss.
The youngest Prime Minister among the leaders of the other 10 member countries of ASEAN, Samdech Hun Manet, despite saying that "the job of Prime Minister is equivalent to the weight of 10 big planes pressing on me." However, he is committed to maintaining the old achievements and continue to innovate in the sense of conservation and development for the nation and the motherland.
The book "37 Prime Ministers of Cambodia - Political and Social Turns in the Fire, War and Peace" is 1,400 pages in A4 size and according to Dr. Chhay Sophal, this book will be distributed to the National Library, University Library and at In some bookstores.
Dr. Chhay Sophal stated that the publication of this book also intends to celebrate the happy day of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit on January 5 and to celebrate the 7th of January Victory Day and the coming Peace Day. From the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as well. DPM Hun Manet Receives President of French VINCI Company
