The United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA) says more than 14.6 million people, or 40 percent of Ukraine's population, will need humanitarian assistance in 2024 due to Russia's war of aggression. According to the OCHA, about 3.3 million of those in need are living in communities near the front lines in eastern and southern Ukraine, including territories under Russian control.
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on January 15, 2024, led a group of relevant officials to directly inspect the cultivation of farmers and solve the problem of water shortage in more than 1 area. , 000 hectares for farmers in Cheung Prey and Batheay districts.
Mr. Un Chanda said that during the inspection of farmers' cultivation, it was found that in Tang Krasaing commune, Batheay district, people planted rice on more than 500 hectares of land and experienced water shortage.
The provincial governor said that the rice crop is the third crop in a year of our farmers. But the problem of lack of irrigation water has already been solved for them.
The provincial governor continued that after working to solve the problem of water shortage for farmers in Batheay district, the team continued to inspect the Thmar Da reservoir area to urge local authorities to drain the water to save our farmers' dry rice in Cheung Prey district. There are 8 villages in Sampong Chey and Pring Chrum communes on an area of more than 900 hectares that face water shortage.
The provincial governor confirmed that after urging the Prey Chhor district authorities and the Thmor Da reservoir community to cooperate with officials from the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Kampong Cham province to help dig more canals in two to three days, the water will fall to Pring Chrum commune. In Sompong Chey commune, there is enough water for farmers to use.
Three drug traffickers sentenced to 30 years in prison, one to life in prison and one acquitted
(Phnom Penh): The Trial Chamber of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, chaired by Mr. Hok Pov and Mr. Kim Manera and Mr. Sar Samnang, on the morning of January 15, 2024, held a hearing on the verdict in the drug trafficking case. In one case, two defendants were sentenced to life imprisonment, one for life and the other for 30 years, while the other was acquitted.
Please be reminded that the specialized force of the Anti-Drug Department cracked down on 2 drug trafficking cases, arrested 4 suspects and confiscated nearly 4 kg of drugs.
The crackdown was carried out on the orders of General Santebandit Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, and General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General of the Anti-Drug Crime Plan, under the direct command of General Kheng Sarath, Director of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes. Coordinated by Mr. Vong Savath, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
