(Phnom Penh): Residents of Ta Prohm Village, Sangkat Prek Eang, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh continued to urge the Chbar Ampov District Authority to close and dismantle an unlicensed rooster farm that still causes noise and stench to residents. Following the decision of the authorities after 30 days from November 21, 2023 to dismantle, but the owner of the farm did not comply.
The people's representative told Fresh News on January 15, 2024 that after the people filed a complaint and inspected the farm location of the authorities, on November 21, 2023, the authorities decided to set a time. 30 days for the owner of this illegal rooster farm to completely dismantle it. In case of exceeding this limit, the district administration will take action to dismantle without any loss or damage.
However, until January 15, 2024, which is almost 60 days ago, the owner of the unlicensed rooster farm still refused to dismantle, still disturbing the people. Therefore, the people strongly urge the authorities to take action against this illegal cockfighting site so as not to affect the daily lives of the people.
