The succession became official when Queen Margrethe II signed his declaration of abdication during a state council meeting, the palace said. Denmark is one of the oldest kingdoms in the world and has no accession to the throne.
Under the freezing temperatures, tens of thousands of people from all over Denmark gathered in the capital to witness events marking the huge popularity of the monarchy in the country of nearly six million people.
The Queen of Denmark, Margrethe II, became the longest reigning monarch in Europe after the death of Britain's Queen Elizabeth II in September 2022, and in July of the same year. Became the longest reigning king in the history of Denmark.
