Tomorrow, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training will open a nationwide training program for young people from poor families.
(Phnom Penh): As planned, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training will open a nationwide office tomorrow, January 15, to train vocational skills for young people from poor and vulnerable families, a program launched by Samdech. His Excellency Hun Manet.
The opening ceremony will be held at the National Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia (NPIC) in Phnom Penh under the chairmanship of Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, with a total of more than 3,700 participants.
Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, confirmed that 15,000 young people, equivalent to 550 classes, will study in 10 different disciplines across the country, which is the first training course.
It should be noted that the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovarithip Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, on November 14, 2023, launched a national program on technical and vocational training for young people from poor families. And vulnerable to get specific skills by studying for 4 months and receive a stipend of 280,000 riel per month.
