Outbreaks of deadly swine fever in Kampong Ror district
(Svay Rieng): There have been a series of outbreaks of deadly swine fever, causing great concern because pig owners, when there are dead pigs, refuse to bury them, so they cut the meat for sale in the village, causing your pigs Other villages died in succession. This case happened on January 13, 2024 in Kandal village, Khseth commune, Kampong Ror district.
Pig farmers in Kandal village, Khseth commune, have requested professional officials, especially the Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, to help provide vaccines against swine diseases and pigs. Outbreaks appear to be exacerbated during pregnancy and in children.
According to the district veterinary officer, the preliminary analysis is: First, suspected swine fever and second, suspected African swine fever, the most deadly disease caused by the currently unvaccinated virus. Prevent and treat no.
The source added that after the preliminary examination and saw such suspicious specimens, the commune veterinary officer disseminated information to the pig farmers to make them aware: Disinfect pesticides in and around the cage every 7 days or every 14 days according to the practical possibilities. Third, clean up regularly.
Veterinarians say the challenge is that when pigs get sick and die, they refuse to bury them. When pigs became ill, some pig farmers treated themselves and refused to report information to commune veterinary officials.
Veterinarians have confirmed that they are still waiting for samples to be taken to a lab in Phnom Penh to find out what the exact disease is. Raise pigs. Air Chief Marshal tells troops to be loyal to the nation and to oppose any color revolution that destroys the nation
