Details: In one day, the fire engulfed the factory and two different shooting range in Phnom Penh in Meanchey and Por Sen Chey districts, the police used 90 vehicles to fully control
(Phnom Penh): The fire engulfed two different factories and shooting fields, causing a surprise to the people and the authorities called fire trucks to intervene and spray water.
Colonel Prohm Yorn, Director of the Fire Prevention and Rescue Police Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, told Fresh News that the two fire cases were as follows:
Case 1: At 9:40 am on January 14, 2024, at the point of the garment factory on Concrete Road, Damnak Thom 2 Village, Sangkat Stung Meanchey III, Khan Meanchey, the fire caused a small amount of damage to the fabric. The fire spread to the neighbors' houses.
The fire was extinguished at 10:10 a.m. on the same day, using four Phnom Penh office vehicles and three trucks, equivalent to 12 cubic meters of water.
Case 2: At 11:00 am, located at Phnom Penh Shooting Range in Khvay Village, Sangkat Trapeang Krasaing, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, caused fire damage to the rear of the shooting range (14m x 23m) and The fire did not spread to the neighbor's house.
The fire was extinguished at 1:00 pm on the same day, in which 13 Phnom Penh office vehicles used 52 trucks, equivalent to 208 cubic meters, and 2 auxiliary vehicles from the Ministry of Interior. 4 water trucks equal to 16 cubic meters, 3 special army command vehicles, 30 water trucks equal to 120 cubic meters and 1 Cambodian beer truck, 1 truck equals 06 cubic meters.
Colonel Prohm Yorn also confirmed that the fire was caused by an electric shock that caused the fire, and no one was injured and did not affect the lives of the people.
