(Svay Rieng): Vietnamese traders come to collect trees along the Cambodian border every day without any restraint from local authorities as well as border authorities.
This case happened at 2:00 pm on January 13, 2024 at the point of the canal on the border ring road in Vealamom village, Thmey commune, Kampong Ror district.
According to the villagers in Vealamom village, Thmey commune, Vietnamese people brought big boats to the border canal and parked at the port next to the border ring road to collect trees along the border ring with the border police. Facilitate Vietnamese groups to cut down trees along the border, including smash trees, acacia trees, pig ears and mixed wood, 3 to 4 meters in diameter, and transport them to Vietnam by boat.
The source added that the trees along the border, including natural trees, smach trees and mixed trees growing along the mouth of the creek and acacia trees, wind oil, if people cut down to use or make firewood is prohibited by the authorities. When the Vietnamese people need the authorities to facilitate the logging and loading of boats to Vietnam.
