(Kampong Cham): Mr. Ma Chhoeun, Member of Parliament for Kampong Cham Constituency, presented the four main meanings of the January 7 Victory Day to the people of Kampong Cham Province, which are the achievements of the Cambodian People's Party, outstanding dignitaries as well as all Cambodians.
This statement was made during the inauguration ceremony of a 168-meter-long concrete road in Tang Kraing village, Cheala commune, Batheay district, Kampong Cham province on the morning of January 14, 2023.
After Mr. Pheng Sophal, Governor of Batheay District, read out the report on the construction of the road, Mr. Ma Chhoeun brought a greeting and a statement of thanks from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Chairman of the King's Personal Advisory Council and Chairman. The Cambodian People's Party to all the people who have supported the CPP in the past.
Dr. presented the four main meanings of the January 7 Victory Day to the people in the ceremony, including:
* Meaning 1: Victory Day January 7 is the day of victory of the Cambodian People's Party, which overthrew the genocidal regime. No party, international organization, or civil society came to help the Cambodian people, only the Cambodian People's Party and the Vietnamese Volunteer Army came to liberate the Cambodian people from the Khmer Rouge massacre. Succeeded on January 7, 1979, these are historical truths that no one has come to distort or recognize.
* Meaning 2: Victory Day January 7 is a day when people are free from the genocidal regime, the regime has no rights, no freedom, no food, only threats, brutal torture and slaughter every day. Since January 7, 1979, more than 3 million people have been freed from slaughter and resumed with all the freedoms that were lost during the genocide.
Meaning 3: January 7 is the time to open a new era, a time of peace, stability, unity, development, roads, bridges, schools, hospitals, democracy, free elections, people can make a living in tourism abroad. . All of this was non-existent during the Khmer Rouge era.
