Heng Sour Calls on Garment Manufacturers Association to Participate in "One Enterprise, One Peace Community" Competition
(Phnom Penh): Speaking at the 16th General Assembly of the Association of Textile, Garment and Travel Products in Cambodia, Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, on Saturday morning, January 13, 2024, called on all factory owners. Participate in the national competition program "One enterprise is a peaceful community", which is the recommendation of His Majesty the King Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, launched at the beginning of his term.
"Factories in the garment sector are the subject of an enterprise competition as a safe community," he said. Through the winner of Level A (A), the factory will receive incentives such as one year inspection exemption, etc., but if the winner of Level A (3) for 3 consecutive years, will also receive the inspection exemption for 3 years. One year or five years in a row.
The Minister stressed that only the establishment of a culture of compliance, a culture of voluntary compliance by all parties, can enable employers and employees to live in peace, which is the desire of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
According to the Minister, the first step in the competition for an enterprise as a safe community will apply to factories in the garment, textile, garment and travel products industries, while factories in other sectors can enter through volunteering.
Please note that this national competition program for enterprises as a safe community is the sixth recommendation of His Majesty Hun Manet, which has been submitted to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to harmonize industrial relations in Cambodia.
