BEIJING: Bilateral trade between China and Russia reached 20 billion US dollars in 2023, setting a new record as the two countries boosted economic ties, Chinese customs data showed on Friday. Close despite the outbreak of war in Ukraine.
China, one of the world's largest oil consumers, has become a key economic lifeline for Russia, a major energy exporter currently under sanctions, the Reuters news agency reported. Sink. Moscow has also increased Chinese purchases, ranging from cars to smartphones, as European and US brands leave the Russian market.
The dollar trade between China and Russia will reach 240.1 billion US dollars by 2023, up 26.3 percent from a year earlier, according to data from the Chinese Customs Administration.
