Samdech Hun Sen and Lok Chumteav Dr. lead a delegation to fly to France safely
In particular, at the hotel of the President and Lok Chumteav Dr. in Paris before traveling to Davos, Switzerland, a large number of Cambodians living in France and other European countries came to welcome the trip. Of Samdech Thipadei and Lok Chumteav Bandith with the deepest feelings of respect, love and remembrance.
Arriving in Paris, France, President Hun Manet will have a number of events, such as meetings with Cambodians living in France and from other European countries, to chair the Euro-Cambodia Business Forum organized by the French Business Association, Meet with Louise Musikivabo, Secretary-General of the International Organization of Francophonie and leaders of several major French companies.
It should be noted that at 8:00 AM on Saturday, January 13, 2024, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet led a delegation. The Royal Government of Cambodia is carrying out two important missions in Europe from 13 to 19 January.
At the beginning of the new year, President Hun Manet will attend the 54th Annual Meeting of the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland.
The 54th Annual Meeting of this year's World Economic Forum is held under the theme "Rebuilding Confidence", focusing on fundamental principles that promote trust, including transparency, consistency and accountability.
After concluding his invitation to the World Economic Forum, Samdech Manet will pay an official visit to Paris, France. The visit comes at the invitation of French President Emmanuel Macron.
The visit of Samdech Hun Manet to France is an important visit to improve Cambodia-France relations. The French President stressed that the first visit of the President will allow to move forward in many important areas that are the foundation of the relationship between our two countries, including economics, military development, heritage and Francophonie.
The President expressed his wish that the President's visit would enable the deepening and diversification of cooperation between Cambodia and France to jointly address the global issues we are facing, especially in the field of energy transition.
The President also expected that the visit of the Prime Minister of Cambodia will examine the means by which Cambodia and France can jointly strengthen law and order in order to ensure the full sovereignty and independence of all states.
In a recent letter to the French President, Hun Manet stated that the visit aims to further deepen cooperation in key areas, focusing on current environmental challenges. In particular, energy transitions and climate change, as well as the promotion of world peace.
He stressed that strengthening economic ties, sharing sustainable development strategies, cooperation in the field of defense, promoting the cultural heritage of the two countries and promoting Francophone are pillars of bilateral relations.
He expressed confidence that the talks between him and the French President would contribute to a deeper understanding and bring together joint initiatives that would benefit both countries. He reaffirmed that Cambodia is committed to continuing to participate in this effort, recognizing the importance of the Cambodian-French partnership for the people of both countries and for the international community.
It should be noted that the Prime Minister and Lok Chumteav Bandit, who are currently on a working mission in Europe, include Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and Mrs. Cham. Nimm, Minister of Commerce, as well as senior government officials and business leaders of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
