Kratie Armed Forces Crack Down on Illegal Timber Truck and Detain 3 Suspects in Chhlong District
(Kratie): The Armed Forces under the command of Brigadier General San Bunthan, Commander of the Kratie Provincial Gendarmerie, in cooperation with the Chhlong Forestry Administration Sangkat, cracked down on an illegal timber truck and arrested three suspects.
This operation took place on January 13, 2024 in Prohot village, Damrey Phong commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province.
According to the Kratie Provincial Armed Forces, the vehicle was a red-headed McVeigh with a blue cage, red stripes, no license plate, carrying firewood, natural wood, diameter from 1 cm to 3 cm, length 0.5 m to 1 M.
Mr. Long Yeung, Deputy Commander of Kratie Provincial Armed Forces, confirmed that the vehicle was stopped by the armed forces on the night of January 12, 2024. At that time, the suspect, the owner of the car, dropped the wood at the potato weighing scale. On the morning of January 13, the military stopped the car and arrested three suspects for obstructing law enforcement.
The three suspects are currently being held at the Kratie Provincial Military Command for further investigation. The vehicle and the above wood were handed over to the Chhlong Forestry Administration Sangkat to handle the procedure.
