General Knowledge: The Role of Khmer Elephant Warriors
(Phnom Penh): War elephants are like tanks for pre-modern armies. Khmer history from the founding of the state to the present day is always associated with elephants. Ancestors used elephants as military vehicles to expand territory, defend territories as vehicles for civil service, as a means of promoting military prestige, and so on.
At the end of the Angkorian period, elephants were added to another important role, trading with artillery from China during the Yuan Dynasty to strengthen the protection of the kingdom. Despite the availability of artillery at that time, elephants still played an important role in the military, as did the modern tanks.
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Chea Van Chan, Deputy Governor and Chairman of the Committee of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Kampong Thom Province, led the youth and volunteers to build a house measuring 4 meters by 6 meters for the homeless poor family and provided a land Lot size 7 meters by 20 meters in Sangvat village, Kraya commune, Prasat Balong district, Kampong Thom province, on January 12, 2024.
