The 5th Committee of the National Assembly in collaboration with the Asian Vision Institute (AVI) organizes a seminar on "Cambodia-EU relations in regional connectivity and peace"
(Phnom Penh): The Foreign Affairs, Cooperation and Information Committee of the National Assembly of Cambodia (Fifth Committee) in collaboration with the Asian Vision Institute (AVI) has organized a workshop on "Cambodia-Europe Relations in Regional Connection and Peace". The workshop was held on the morning of January 12, 2024 at the National Assembly.
The workshop was chaired by Mr. Jan Zahradil, Member of the European Parliament and First Vice President of the International Trade Committee. Facilitated by Dr. Chheng Kimlong, President of the Asian Vision Institute.
The purpose of this workshop is to share information on the achievements, challenges and opportunities of the relationship between Cambodia and the EU, both within the framework of the State and Parliament, in order to further strengthen and expand the cooperation between Cambodia and the EU to respond to the situation. Complex of geopolitical, regional and global politics.
On that occasion, Mr. Sous Yara mentioned that the potential of the EU-Cambodia partnership in recent years has greatly evolved beyond the traditional diplomatic relations based on the principles of mutual respect and understanding. And a joint commitment to promoting regional and global connectivity and peace, in which Cambodia can play a more active and deep role as an economically and culturally connected state.
Jan Zahradil praised the competent bodies and functions of the EU Expert Committees, including the Commission on Trade with ASEAN Countries and the EU Indo-Pacific Strategy.
He also outlined the policy of foreign relations, the benefits of a free trade agreement between the EU and countries in the region, respect for international labor conventions and non-interference in the internal politics of partner countries, and the challenges that must be met. Also consider trading in a digital context and supply chain.
In addition, the workshop discussed the benefits of the Indo-Pacific strategy, climate change, connectivity, free trade and foreign policy based on the spirit of peace and mutual benefit. The workshop concluded with a number of recommendations, especially on business connectivity, human resource cooperation, digital technology skills training and research institutional cooperation.
On that occasion, the Fifth Committee of the National Assembly also thanked for the good cooperation of the European Union and ASEAN countries. The National Assembly Committee also requested that such a sharing forum continue to promote better relations between Cambodia and the European Union.
