WASHINGTON, Jan. 11 (Xinhua) - The United States and the United Kingdom, backed by Australia, Bahrain, Canada and the Netherlands, on Thursday led airstrikes targeting several Houthi-controlled areas in Yemen. Iran is the backbone.
This is the first air strike on a Houthi base in Yemen since the armed movement launched more than 27 attacks on cargo ships in the Red Sea on November 19. The White House and its allies last week warned Houthis of the consequences if they do not stop their attacks in the Red Sea.
Thursday's US airstrikes were the largest against Houthis in nearly 10 years. In 2016, the United States launched a Tomahawk cruise missile attack on three Houthi bases after the group attacked US warships and merchant ships. At that time, Houthi stopped the attack after the US retaliation.
