(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly President of Cambodia, Khuon Sodary, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, said that the National Assembly of Cambodia welcomes all European Parliament delegations in strengthening parliamentary cooperation for peace and sustainable development for the people.
The President of the National Assembly, Khuon Sodary, made this remark while allowing Mr. Jan Zahradil, Member of the European Parliament and First Vice President of the International Trade Committee, to pay a courtesy call and discuss work on Friday morning, 12 January 2024. At the National Assembly.
On that occasion, Mr. Zanzaradil thanked the National Assembly President for taking the time to meet with him and his colleagues on this occasion.
He informed the National Assembly President about the purpose of his visit to Cambodia at the invitation of the Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation and Information Committee of the National Assembly and the Asian Vision Institute to participate in the exchange of views and dialogues with Cambodian MPs and officials. Expertise of the General Secretariat of the National Assembly on "Cambodia-EU Cooperation".
Please be informed that Mr. Zan Zaradil was born in the Czech Republic and that His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, the highest revered person, has been in school from primary to higher education. .
The President of the National Assembly stressed that the National Assembly of Cambodia always welcomes the European Parliament delegation to visit to strengthen and expand good relations and cooperation with each other in order to ensure peace, social stability, respect for human rights, democracy and sustainable development. Sustainably, taking the people as the core.
The National Assembly underlined that the friendship and cooperation between Cambodia and the European Union began in 1994, and the two sides signed an agreement in 1997. Europe is a key humanitarian and trade partner of Cambodia.
During the fight against Kovid-19, the European Union provided financial assistance to Cambodia to fight Kovid-19 and to reduce socio-economic impacts twice, with a total amount of 499 million euros.
The National Assembly Presidents Khuon Sodary and Zan Zaradil emphasized that this is an important time for Cambodia and the European Union to further strengthen their friendship and cooperation based on the interests of the people. Cambodia has just successfully held elections and the European Parliament will hold elections in June.
