(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Deputy Prime Minister in charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, on the morning of January 11, 2024, presided over a seminar on "Climate Resilience and Energy Transition: Suffering for Cambodia" co-organized. By the UN Economic, Social and Cultural Council and the United Nations Sustainable Development Solutions Institution at the Friendship Palace, Office of the Council of Ministers.
The seminar was hosted by Professor Jeffrey Sachs, a world-renowned economist who is currently chair of the Center for Sustainable Development at Columbia University and Head of the United Nations Sustainable Development Division. There were more than 500 participants from the Economic, Social and Cultural Council of the Ministry, national and international institutions and development partners.
Permanent Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth praised Dr. Chhem Keat Rithy, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Missions and Chairman of the Economic, Social and Cultural Council, for cooperating with the United Nations Sustainable Development Solution Organization to organize the workshop. This importance.
Meanwhile, the Permanent Deputy Prime Minister noted that some developed countries have begun to shift their resources to fossil fuels rather than renewable energy sources, which will hinder the progress of the fight against global climate change.
Professor Jeffrey Sachs also shared his views and experiences on sustainable development and energy transition, emphasizing the importance of all countries' commitment to peace, global governance, and global cooperation. The United Nations is a key force for financial innovation and technology transfer.
He stressed that superpowers and developed economies have a vital role to play in ensuring peace and sustainable development for the whole world, without having to support and spend heavily on the causes of war and military conflict. Financing global public goods such as climate change, poverty reduction and peace, etc.
