(Oddar Meanchey): Under the guidance and guidance of General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, and with procedural coordination from Mr. Touch Sopheakdey, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court, Major General Huot Sothy, Oddar Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, led the force. On December 31, 2023, at the corner of Kandek Bridge, Kandek Village, Sangkat Samrong, Samrong City, two suspects were successfully arrested.
Lt. Gen. Huot Sothy said that in the above operation, using the monitoring skills for more than 10 days, the specialized forces were able to identify and arrest two suspects, including First: 16-year-old John Kimchen, residing in Borey Administration Village, Sangkat Samrong, Samrong City, and second: 20-year-old Sambour Meng Hay, residing in Aphivath Village, Sangkat O Smach, Samrong City.
Later, when the specialized force interrogated the two suspects and admitted that they both actually ambushed the victim, causing serious injuries.
It should be noted that on the night of December 31, 2023, at the corner of Kandek Bridge in Kandek Village, Sangkat Samrong, Samrong City, Oddar Meanchey Province, there was a case of intentional violence on the victim, causing serious injuries caused by the suspect. Identified and intercepted the victim, 16-year-old Mon Rin, residing in Champa Sok Village, Kon Kreal Commune, Samrong City, Oddar Meanchey Province.
Currently, the two suspects have been arrested and brought to the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Police to prepare a case file to be sent to the provincial court for legal action.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Meas Sok Sen San, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has not created a new tax, but only postponed and granted preferential treatment on certain types of taxes.
Mr. Meas Sok Sen San stated that "the Kingdom of Cambodia does not have a new tax, only a delay or favor, which favors the state to lose some revenue."
At the same time, Mr. Meas Sok Sen San said that tax collection or tax collection efforts are the duty of tax collectors or the duty of the Royal Government within the framework of reform.
Please watch Mr. Meas Sok Sen San's statement below:
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Meas Sok Sen San, Secretary of State and Spokesman for the Ministry of Economy and Finance, said that tax revenue is now higher than customs revenue, which shows that the Cambodian economy is mature, with a lot of domestic investment.
Mr. Meas Soksen San stated, "Cambodia's revenue, if you look at tax revenue, now reaches a point where tax revenue is higher than customs revenue, which indicates a mature economy, because customs revenue is higher than tax revenue, which means we depend "On the external economy a lot."
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Meas Sok Sen San, spokesman for the Ministry of Economy and Finance, explained that tax collection is the obligation of the Royal Government to give back to the people in various forms, such as infrastructure development and public services.
Speaking at the FRESH BUSINESS program, he explained that the taxes that the Royal Government collects from the people, the state spends on public works such as construction of infrastructure, schools, roads, bridges, salaries for civil servants to serve and provide services. The public returns to the people.
However, he said that due to the limited tax collection in the past and Cambodia has just started to collect taxes at a better level, so it is not yet possible to reach the construction of infrastructure as well as developed countries.
At the same time, despite the Royal Government's efforts to collect taxes, the Royal Government has also considered and given preference to tax collection to investors and business people, especially during the economic crisis.
Hun Sen to Attend World Economic Forum in Switzerland
(Phnom Penh): At the invitation of Professor Clas, former Founder and Executive Chairman of the World Economic Forum, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, will lead a high-level delegation to attend the 54th Annual Meeting of the World Economic Forum. He was born on January 16-17, 2024 in Davos-Clouster, Switzerland. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, which was received by Fresh News.
Under the theme "Rebuilding Confidence", the meeting will focus on basic principles that promote trust, including transparency, consistency and accountability. World leaders and CEOs of major companies, as well as presidents of major international organizations, civil society leaders, youth representatives, social entrepreneurs and media outlets will attend.
Accompanying the President and Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet, including Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia and Mrs. Cham Nimmol, Minister of Commerce, as well as senior government officials and business leaders of the Chamber of Commerce. Cambodian work.
(Kampong Chhnang): Monks, authorities and residents of Banh Chkol village, Chrey Bak commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province have requested the leaders of philanthropists as well as relevant ministries to support the construction of a bridge across the river (Prey Kraing Bridge), which is located. In the above commune villages for the benefit of traveling and transporting agricultural products of farmers in many villages.
The Chief Inspector of Wat Mongkul Panha, also known as Wat Bachkol, in Chrey Bak commune, Rolea Bier district, named Sun Yim, insisted that due to the difficulties of traveling in many villages in two communes of Rolea Bier district, people gathered today. Opinion on the construction of a wooden bridge across the river with a length of 20 meters made of cement, according to the actual possibilities that they have gradually.
It is estimated that this bridge will cost up to 30,000 dollars. On behalf of the Buddhists, I would like to appeal to all local and foreign philanthropists to donate money or materials to help build this bridge for the benefit of the people. Travel and transport agricultural products according to your generosity.
Mr. Sam Samnang, Banh Chkol village chief, Chrek Bak commune, Rolea Bier district, confirmed that the project to build a bridge is 20 meters long, 4.10 meters wide and 6 meters high, crossing the Chrey Bak river, which is planned to cost nearly 30,000 dollars.
On behalf of the people, I would like to appeal to the people who are generous, as well as the leaders and relevant ministries and departments to support the construction of this bridge to be completed as soon as possible. People travel because, according to the possibility that construction has started now, only $ 1,500.
He added that originally, this bridge was a wooden bridge that the villagers built since 1980, when the bridge collapsed, it was gradually repaired until it collapsed in January 2023. People harvested rice with a large amount of water falling off the bridge.
He confirmed that after making a series of appeals, there are also some philanthropists to support. Mr. Seng Vichet, Governor of Rolea Bier District, donated one ton of cement and Lt. Gen. Teap Horn also donated two tons of cement. Asia-Pacific Leaders Respond to HIV / AIDS and Development in Cambodia
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Chairman of Kampong Thom Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, participated in the program of His Excellency Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, National Outstanding Leader of the Asia-Pacific Leadership Forum on HIV / AIDS and Development. In Cambodia, the HIV / AIDS Education Campaign under the theme "One Community Leads to the End of AIDS". The ceremony took place in Stong district on January 12, 2024.
Mr. Say Kimlam, Chairman of Stong District Sub-Branch, reported that the sub-branch has made efforts to visit the grassroots and raise awareness among the people about the catastrophic effects of wind, force and fire, and the sub-branch has carried out humanitarian activities to help A total of 412 people were affected by disasters and crises.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak would like to encourage all Cambodian Red Cross youth in Stong district. One day, more and more good young people will get rid of gangsters, younger brothers, older brothers, drug addicts, alcoholics, gamblers, and bad guys, which cause a bad phenomenon to society.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak continued that through the training of the children, I believe that some important lessons are: the history of the international movement, the Red Cross, the Red Crescent, first aid, the roles and responsibilities of the Red Cross youth, and some other important content.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak urged the trainers to be diligent in presenting to the children, to contribute to the promotion of the spirit of awakening, volunteerism, as a powerful driving force, intellectuals and a strong pillar of the society to participate in the Red Cross youth movement. With a humane heart, with compassion, love for each other, contribute to the great interests of the nation, community and family.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Dith Eang Sophalleth, Minister of the Environment, expressed 100% confidence that by 2050, Cambodia will become a carbon neutral country with a beautiful carbon and forest cover up to 60% or more.
The Minister of Environment expressed this belief in accordance with the law, the campaign to plant 1 million seedlings per year to increase forest cover, along with the current trend that people, especially students, young people and more and more. Understand the importance of trees.
At the same time, Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, supported and approved the implementation of Article 6 of the Paris Agreement on Climate Change, which encourages and encourages Cambodia to conduct carbon exploration in a transparent, accountable and standard manner. International.
In addition, the Minister stated that if young people want to be clean, this is a trend not only for this generation, but for all generations to come. This means that this generation will stop using plastic bags, the next generation will stop using the same plastic bags.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth added that by participating in the promotion and love of the tree, they and their descendants will not cut down the tree.
"So I am 100 percent convinced that our movement is not just for the short term, it is for the long term and it is a potential movement that is the driving force behind it." This is an additional statement of the Minister of Environment.
It should be noted that Cambodia currently has more than 7 million hectares of protected land, or about 41 percent of the country's total land area. In the past, Cambodia has sold carbon on a voluntary market basis at Tatai Wildlife Sanctuary and Cardamom Mountain National Park in Koh Kong Province and Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary in Mondulkiri Province. Proceeds from the sale of carbon will be used to develop communities and conserve various protected areas.
Ministry of Interior finds some associations and non-governmental organizations not fulfilling their legal obligations and notifies them to fulfill their obligations in force
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Interior has found that some associations and non-governmental organizations have not fulfilled their obligations under the Law on Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations, while the Royal Government of Cambodia has always adhered to the promotion of freedom of association. And the activities of associations and non-governmental organizations.
Seeing this, the Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, Dr. Sar Sokha, issued a notification on the fulfillment of obligations as prescribed by the Law on Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations so that non-compliant institutions must comply. In accordance with the law in force.
In the announcement received by Fresh News on January 12, 2024, Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha said that at present, there are 6,279 local associations and non-governmental organizations, including associations. There are 2,747 and 3,532 non-governmental organizations registered with the Ministry of Interior and able to operate freely in accordance with the laws and regulations in force of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
