Handing over ceremony of the hospital building renovation project and the donation of medical equipment as a charitable donation to the Health Department of Phnom Penh Capital Administration, totaling more than 1.7 million USD
(Phnom Penh): The Department of Health of the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration held a handover ceremony of medical equipment donated by the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints to the Department of Health of the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration under the presidency of Mr. Im Ron Hassan. Deputy Governor of the Board of Governors of Phnom Penh.
The ceremony took place on January 11, 2024 at the Cambodia-China Sen Sok Friendship Referral Hospital with the participation of Dr. Ngy Mean Heng, Director of the Health Department of Phnom Penh Capital Administration, Mr. Rath Chansophea, Director of the Church of God Association. Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints in Cambodia and representatives of many other associations.
On that occasion, Dr. Ngy Mean Heng stated that from 2022 until now, the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints Association has been implementing a project to renovate the hospital building, provide medical equipment and facilities. Other doctors to 8 referral hospitals and 1 health center under the health department of Phnom Penh Capital Administration, a total of 14 projects with a budget of 1,785,286.27 US dollars.
He continued, "This noble humanitarian project has been contributing to the improvement of health services and well-being to the people in Phnom Penh better and as part of improving the quality of health services in the eight referral hospitals. The Royal Government of the seventh mandate under the most wise leadership of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Improving the physical infrastructure and the provision of additional medical equipment in accordance with the necessary needs are continuously implemented in referral hospitals and health centers. The source of funding for this improvement comes from the budget of the Royal Government and development partners, as well as humanitarian organizations.
He added that the achievements and progress in the health sector achieved are inseparable from the efforts to overcome all obstacles of health workers at all levels in the health system in fulfilling their duties as officials. The public serves the health of the people, especially the staff of health centers and referral hospitals who have been working to provide services in Phnom Penh.
Dr. Ngy Mean Heng stated that the Department of Health of Phnom Penh Capital Hall considers the support and cooperation from relevant institutions at all levels, the active participation of associations and partnerships with the private sector, financial and technical support from development partners. National and international NGOs remain indispensable, and development progress from other sectors has also contributed significantly to progress in the health sector.
