The meeting was held at the CRC headquarters on the afternoon of January 11, 2024, with the participation of the Honorary President of the Youth Club, Youth Advisors and CRC Youth Representatives of 24 higher education institutions in Phnom Penh and Lead - A total of 96 head office staff.
Mr. Pit Chamnan emphasized the importance of the meeting and conveyed the greetings and congratulations from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to the Rector, Vice Rector, Youth and Youth Advisor at According to 24 higher education institutions in Phnom Penh, which have been implementing activities in their respective youth clubs on a regular basis in the past.
On that occasion, Mr. Mean Chanyada also highlighted the three main objectives of this meeting after receiving the high recommendation of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, that the Central Committee and the leadership of the General Secretariat. Note the following:
1: Review and discuss the proposals of higher education institutions in the short, medium and long term to strengthen the youth movement of the Cambodian Red Cross.
2. Examine and agree on the important and outstanding priorities that the CRC youth should do in higher education institutions in Phnom Penh, both public and private, which are specific activities with good results and high efficiency.
3. Mechanism to strengthen the youth of the Cambodian Red Cross based on two principles: quantity and quality.
At the same time, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak also emphasized the attention from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to the work of youth in the leadership of potential youth and the strengthening of peace by focusing on youth in accordance with The pentagon strategy of the Royal Government.
In addition, she highlighted the priority work of the Cambodian Red Cross in 2024 and the University's proposal regarding the activities of the Cambodian Red Cross Youth, which was raised at the 7th General Assembly of the Cambodian Red Cross on 15 December. 2023, as well as the request of the youth, which was issued in the statement of the second youth forum of the National Association of Red Cross and Red Crescent Southeast Asia in September 2023.
After receiving comments, challenges and suggestions from a number of higher education institutions, Mr. Pit Chamnan summarized and recommended the meeting, especially for the presentation to the Rector in all higher education institutions, including:
