Banteay Meanchey Military sends two Thais to drug court
(Banteay Meanchey): In the morning of January 12, 2024, the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie sent two Thai suspects along with exhibits to the Provincial Court for legal action in connection with the case of storage, distribution and use. Of illegal drugs.
On January 9, 2024, the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie, led by Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro, the Commander of the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie, launched an operation to crack down on illegal possession, distribution and use of drugs by detaining Thais. Two men and women in front of an apartment building in Kbal Spean 2 village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province, and seized some exhibits.
Colonel Nuon Ninaro said that the two victims were:
* First: Bun Yasata Poramet, 27 years old, Thai national, currently living in Samaki Meanchey Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
* Second: Usita Chanthachinda (Phim), 25 years old, Thai national, currently living in Samaki Meanchey Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Colonel Nuon Ninaro confirmed that before the crackdown, the Poipet City Gendarmerie received information from security that there were cases of illegal storage, distribution and use of drugs. He immediately led the force to the scene and arrested the two suspects along with drug exhibits and brought them to the Poipet City Military Police Base for questioning and processing.
After being detained and interrogated, the suspects confessed that they had indeed stored, distributed and used illegal drugs. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the Municipal Gendarmerie has prepared a case file and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Colonel Chea Dara, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of anti-drug work, said that the crackdown was ordered by Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie and coordinated the procedure from him. Born Vannareth, a prosecutor with the provincial court.
