Former UNTAC Chief Praises Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Decision to Arrange a Succession of New Leaders with Strong and Wise Leadership
The former UNTAC chief paid tribute when Samdech Techo Hun Sen allowed him to pay a courtesy call and discuss work at the New Otani Hotel on the morning of January 11, 2024 during Samdech Techo's visit to Japan from January 9 to 12, 2024.
On that occasion, Mr. Akassi was very excited to meet Samdech Techo again and thanked Samdech Techo for giving him the opportunity to meet politely during Samdech's busy time. He said that a year and a half in Cambodia from 1992 to 1993 as the head of UNTAC provided the best memories of his life that will never be forgotten.
He still remembers Samdech Techo's good cooperation and gentle but firm flexibility, which is the key to achieving good results in UNTAC meetings. Everything will not be successful without the cooperation of Samdech Techo.
In addition, he has a direct interest is to love the natural landscape in Cambodia, both forests and beaches and cultural heritage, especially Angkor Wat and Khmer ancient art, which should be more widely disseminated to the world.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo was also happy to meet with Mr. Akassi again and thanked him for reminding him of the time when Cambodia was in a difficult situation. Samdech Techo stated that due to the joint cooperation between UNTAC and the relevant countries at that time and the direct efforts of Cambodia, Cambodia can have a situation like today with full peace and rapid development.
Samdech Techo also emphasized that what is true in front of him is that Cambodia has transformed from a war-torn country to a peaceful one, from a battlefield to a development zone, from a lack of clean water and electricity to a state of adequate access from Phnom Penh. With an area of just over 400 square kilometers to more than 700 square kilometers, from the GDP per capita per year only 100 US dollars then more than 2,000 US dollars today.
In the end, the two dignitaries expressed optimism with the leadership of the new generation of leaders in taking the national economic development to a new level and were confident that at the same time, the bilateral relations between Cambodia and Japan would grow. And more depth in the future. South African Supreme Court hearing accuses Israel of committing genocide in Gaza
The Hague on Thursday accused Israel of committing genocide against Palestine and asked the UN Supreme Court to order an immediate halt to the military campaign. Israel's atrocities in Gaza This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on January 11, 2024.
On the first day of a two-day trial at the International Court of Justice (ICJ), South Africa said Israel's air and ground strikes were aimed at "purging the population" in Palestine.
Israel has denied the genocide allegations, saying it is baseless and has accused Pretoria of acting as a "monster advocate" for Hamas, an armed Palestinian Islamic group against Israel. The war in Gaza.
Israel has begun a full-scale war following cross-border attacks by Hamas militants on October 7, which Israeli officials say killed 1,200 people and took 240 hostages to Gaza. The South has condemned an ongoing Israeli indiscriminate bombing campaign in the Gaza Strip that has killed more than 23,000 people, mostly women and children.
It should also be noted that the 1948 Genocide Convention, adopted after the massacre of Jews in the Nazi dictatorship, defined genocide as "an act committed with intent to destroy, in whole or in part, to a group of people." "Any race or religion."
