His Excellency Hun Manet said this on the afternoon of January 11, 2024, on the occasion of the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of the old year 2023 and the direction of the new year 2024 of the Ministry of Women's Affairs at Sokha Hotel. Phnom Penh.
"The Ministry of Women's Affairs and relevant ministries and institutions must continue to implement programs and measures to enhance the leadership of women and girls at all levels and in all sectors to ensure that all people," she said. "Both men and women have the full right and opportunity to have the choice and representation to contribute to the economic and social development of the environment and sustainability."
His Excellency Hun Manet added that in order to maintain harmony in the family and work efficiency, we request the Ministry of Interior to examine the possibility of appointing women as Deputy Governors of the Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Governments by providing opportunities to serve. Basic work close to his family as well.
Samdech Hun Sen also requested the Ministry of Women's Affairs to continue to lead, coordinate and cooperate with relevant ministries, institutions and partners in integrating these priorities into the development process and national policy on gender equality, the Rattanak Women's Strategic Plan and the policy framework and program. In line with the Royal Government's agenda, which considers the promotion of gender equality as a priority approach and also inter-sectoral.
This statement was made at the closing ceremony of the 2023 work review meeting and the 2024 work direction of the Ministry of Women's Affairs on the afternoon of January 11, 2024 at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
On that occasion, the President encouraged the Ministry of Women's Affairs and relevant ministries to work together to protect women and children and increase prevention of negative points affecting women, children and victims of violence, trafficking and so on.
In addition, attention must be paid to promoting social morality, women's values, especially to educate young men and women when they do something that affects social values or degrades national honor. At this point, the competent officials are not going to persecute them, but to educate them so that they do not deviate from social morality.
At the same time, Samdech Hun Sen called on the people that if they do something, there must be a limit of responsibility and let's respect the law for social order, respect for national cultural traditions.
"I call on the people, both men and women, to do whatever they want, there must be boundaries of responsibility, rights and freedoms exist, but there must be boundaries. "Ours."
He continued that the Cambodian people have had a culture for thousands of years, so the Cambodian people should continue to preserve and practice the national culture, language and language to be consistent, especially to preserve the national identity to survive for future generations. Later generations.
Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, also said that recently, the Ministry of Women's Affairs, through the National Committee for the Promotion of Morality, Social Values, Women and Cambodian Families, recently took action against some groups that committed immoral acts and posted videos. On social media, as well as women who released a video of eating shoes, eating tires, because the video ads affect social values.
Meeting to review the work results of 2023 of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration, Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth provided 6 additional points and focused on the quality of education and health services
(Kampong Chhnang): On January 10, 2024, Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Deputy Prime Minister in charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers and Chairman of the National Working Group for Kampong Chhnang Province, presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the results. 2023 and raise the work direction for 2024 of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration.
The Permanent Deputy Prime Minister considered this meeting as an important annual event where all stakeholders came together to evaluate the achievements in all areas that Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration has achieved in the past, especially in 2023, and to examine the challenges. Identify solutions and seize opportunities to continue to promote socio-economic development in Kampong Chhnang province, especially to improve the living standards of the people.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the efforts of the leaders of the provinces, cities, districts, communes and sangkats at all levels, including all civil servants and the armed forces who have worked together in solidarity. One well, by using physical and mental strength in fulfilling its roles and responsibilities responsibly, leading to the achievement of many achievements for the people throughout Kampong Chhnang province.
In the next 25 years, the need for development will change, with one side maintaining the legacy of the previous generation of leaders and the other continuing to hit the foundations of nation-building to achieve equitable and equitable development. Sustainability to ensure social stability and long-term development.
In this spirit, the Permanent Deputy Prime Minister provided guidelines on some important priorities for provincial, municipal, district and commune administrations to increase their attention and contribute to effective implementation, including the following: To:
* First: the protection of peace and political stability, * Second: ensuring social security and safety, * Third: the promotion of public services and local problem solving, * Fourth: strengthening the implementation of the revised program Forms of decentralization and deconcentration, * 5th: Socio-economic development in the province and * 6th: Participation in the implementation of various policy programs of the Royal Government.
In addition, he urged the Provincial Unity Command on behalf of the Provincial State Land Management Committee to continue to use total force as necessary, with the cooperation of the Natural Resources Crime Suppression Committee and relevant authorities to enforce the law on those who Committing natural resource crimes to strengthen the effective management of land in the flooded forest area of the Tonle Sap region.
Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet urges relevant ministries, institutions and the private sector to continue to strengthen and expand measures to support women entrepreneurs (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The relevant ministries, institutions and the private sector should continue to cooperate to strengthen and expand measures to support women entrepreneurs to promote better gender equality.
This promotion was made on the occasion of Samdech closing the meeting to review the work of the old year 2023 and the work direction of the new year 2024 of the Ministry of Women's Affairs at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
The Prime Minister said, "Relevant ministries, institutions and the private sector continue to work together to strengthen and expand support measures for women entrepreneurs leading small and medium enterprises, improve the financial environment for women and promote women's participation in All economic and social activities.
At the same time, Samdech stated that the Royal Government will strengthen citizenship in a highly civilized society with morality, equity and an environment in which women are the core by providing more opportunities for greater women's participation. And broad in determining the fate of the nation.
He added that the Royal Government has set gender equality and empowerment of women and girls in all areas as a priority in the policy agenda in the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy, which was announced on August 24, 2023. And the national policy on gender equality, which will be implemented soon.
According to research data from 2012 to date, there are more than 500,000 entrepreneurs in Cambodia, of which women are the owners of more than 300,000 entrepreneurs, or 60% of the total number of entrepreneurs. .
Samdech Mani President Hun Manet warns women to sell some products online not to lose the value and dignity of Khmer women (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Moha Bovathi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia This sends a reminder message to women who are engaged in the business of selling or promoting some products online, not to lose the value and dignity of Cambodian women.
Remembrance of Samdech Hun Sen Manet on the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the meeting to summarize the work results of 2023 and raise the direction for 2024 of the Ministry of Women's Affairs and after Samdech saw an inappropriate mistake of the seller Products online today.
According to the Prime Minister, in the past, some women online advertisers have been arrested after excessive advertising on social media, which affected the value of Cambodian women.
His Excellency Hun Manet said, "How many nephews have been arrested in connection with the excessive publicity on social media about the sale of excessive products." "Of course, the rights and freedoms of the people, including the rights of women, are upheld, but we must also have an obligation to uphold and protect social, cultural and traditional values, and especially the values of Cambodian women."
The Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia stressed that no matter how developed Cambodia is, identity must not be eradicated. Free market policies, the practice of some democracies, but in a world where there are no standards that apply to all countries, the basic values must be respected.
Samdech Mani Hun Manet also sent a message that as the technology system is more advanced and the means to promote the product more rich, especially through social media by creating a lot of different content, but what makes the buyer interested. It is not necessary to create pornographic content, so avoid excessive advertising.
At the same time, Samdech Hun Sen also instructed the Ministry of Women's Affairs to monitor the activities of some women that affect the cultural and moral values of Cambodian women. In this sense, the prince explained that this monitoring is not a closure of the rights and freedoms of individuals, nor is it a touch of hands, feet, or feet, just an orientation so as not to cross the red line of freedom.
In today's age of technology, online businesses such as selling food, consumer goods and cleaning products are becoming more and more popular, and most of the sellers are women. There is a lot of different content being created to get the attention of the masses, but some of the content seems to be excessive, like polluting society.
But in the past, the authorities have also summoned a number of individuals, both men and women, for education and counseling, and in some cases to use legal measures to arrest and send to court. With the guidance and reminder of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, it is now expected that the misconduct of some online product sellers on social media will also be eliminated.
