The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, made this recommendation on the occasion of closing the meeting to review the work of the old year 2023 and the work direction of the new year 2024 of the Ministry of Women's Affairs at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh on the afternoon of January 11, 2024.
In order to continue to promote gender equality in all areas, Samdech encouraged and provided some views for the Ministry of Women's Affairs, ministries and all stakeholders, including:
First. Encourage the Ministry of Women's Affairs and relevant ministries to continue to invest in women within the framework of national and sectoral policy through systematic budgeting, gender responsiveness, and human resource development within ministries.
Second. Relevant ministries, institutions and the private sector continue to work together to strengthen and expand measures to support women entrepreneurs leading small and medium enterprises, improve the financial environment for women, and promote women's participation in all economic and social activities.
Third. Relevant ministries and institutions need to expand the scope of the national social protection framework and health care services towards universal health coverage in order to ensure that all citizens have access to this service environmentally.
Fourth. The Ministry of Women's Affairs, in collaboration with relevant ministries and institutions, focuses on addressing the gender gap in the digital sector, in particular increasing the participation of women and girls in the digital sector, the use of digital technology and education, knowledge and skills. Science, Technology, Engineering, Creative Arts and Mathematics (STEAM) are popular fields in the digital age.
Fifth. In order to improve the balance of life and work, the Ministry of Women's Affairs must pay attention and study in collaboration with public and private partners on social benefits that recognize the value of domestic work and care for family members, as well as take necessary measures to reduce Burden the work of women and girls and give women more life choices.
7th. The Ministry of Women's Affairs and relevant ministries and institutions must continue to implement programs and measures to enhance the leadership of women and girls at all levels and in all areas to ensure that all people, both women and men, have full rights and opportunities. To have the choice and representation to contribute to the economic and social development of the environment and sustainability.
