(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Thursday, January 11, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, will close the meeting to review the work of the old year 2023 and Work direction for the new year 2024 of the Ministry of Women's Affairs. The ceremony was held at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
Please note that women's work is an interdisciplinary work that is important and covers four major aspects:
1) Diplomatic view: The expression of the Royal Government's political will on the national and international stage to protect human rights and women's rights and the vulnerability of the people, promote democracy, which contributes to the promotion of the image and honor of the nation.
2) Economic aspects: More women in leadership roles will contribute to increased economic growth (McKinsey 2015 study). At the same time, women are also a key player in contributing to the implementation of demographic policies (reproduction related to the balance of life and work).
3) Social aspects: Women have the role of mothers, the balance of the family (housework and care of family members) and intergenerational communication agencies (educating children, preserving the traditional culture).
4) Political aspects and peacekeeping: With women voters in more than 50 percent of the voting population who need to continue to think and pay attention. Promote women's participation in peacekeeping and protection (Women's Peace and Security Program).
In the Rectangular Strategy of the Royal Government, the past four stages have identified women as the backbone of the economy and society through the promotion of gender equality, investment in the promotion of rights, status, role and socio-economic status of women and families.
The Political Program of the Royal Government of the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly continues to prioritize the promotion of gender equality and the empowerment of women and girls in all areas by strengthening citizenship in a highly civilized, moral and equitable society. And the environment in which women are the core.
2023 is the last year of the implementation of the 5th Rattanak Women's Strategic Plan (2019-2023) and the Ministry of Women's Affairs has started to prepare the 6th Rattanak Women's Strategic Plan based on the spirit of the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy, including the results of the internal discussions. Two-day meeting to prepare a roadmap for the 6th Neary Rattanak Strategic Plan (2024-2028).
