* First, the Provincial Land Management Committee decided to allow the people who are actually occupying and enjoying to continue to occupy and enjoy normally.
* Second, the people have agreed to occupy, use and enjoy the community forest land only on their actual land and will not continue to encroach on the community forest land.
* Third: For the forest land that the people are cutting down, encroaching and planting fence posts without using and cultivating actual crops, the villagers have agreed to dismantle the fence posts voluntarily and hand over the land to the Land Management Committee. The state governs the provinces.
