Mr. Un Chanda continued that recently, two districts have experienced a shortage of water to irrigate dry season crops, including:
* First: Cheung Prey district has Sampong Chey commune and Pring Chrum commune, with 8 villages equal to more than 900 hectares, which face water shortage. However, this was decided by the provincial governor to open the sluice gate at the point of Thmor Da Reservoir to drop the water connected with the canal to flow into Sampong Chey and Pring Chrum communes.
* Second: Batheay district has 2 communes that face water shortage problem, in which Sandek commune has an area of more than 100 hectares, it has already been solved by using dry rice rescue pump. Separately, in Taing Krasang commune, there is more than 500 hectares of land that faces water shortage, but this work is done by the officials of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Kampong Cham province, using water pumps to provide farmers.
