US trade deficit narrows as service surplus widens
The value of imports and exports fell 1.9 percent. These figures have not yet been adjusted for inflation.
Despite a narrowing deficit in November, imports of goods continued to rise amid consumer spending volatility. US services exports rose in four months to a record $ 85.7 billion.
After adjusting for inflation, the trade deficit narrowed to $ 84.8 billion in November, the smallest volume in three months. Before the current report released, the US Federal Reserve's GDPNow forecast for Atlanta showed that trade slowed fourth-quarter economic growth by 0.23 percentage points.
The decline in imports of goods reflected a decline in the supply of industries, consumer goods and capital goods. US exports were hampered by declining exports of vehicles, industrial supplies and consumer goods. According to Bloomberg News.
