Swiss SDC vows to assist Cambodia in tourism vocational training and tourism destination management
(Phnom Penh): The Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) is committed to supporting the Ministry of Tourism in further strengthening tourism cooperation, especially in tourism vocational training and tourism management. Attractive.
This commitment was made during a working meeting between Mr. Sok Soken, Minister of Tourism, and Mr. Markus Buerli, Director of Cooperation of the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) on the afternoon of January 10, 2024 to discuss Opportunities for strengthening tourism cooperation.
On that occasion, the Minister thanked the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) for supporting the Cambodia Hospitality Training Program (HoKa) to more than 4,000 vulnerable young people in 10 target provinces and supporting the expansion of the province. For training Cambodian hospitality to two new target provinces, including Koh Kong and Kampong Chhnang from 2024 onwards.
Mr. McCarthy expressed the support of the Swiss government through the Swiss Regional Cooperation Program for 2022-2025, which will focus on supporting the Cambodian government on: (1) the participation of the people in good governance; 2) Efficient economic growth through technical and vocational training; and (3) Climate change and natural resource management.
Minister Sok Soken and the Director of Cooperation of the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) are committed to further strengthening and expanding tourism cooperation, especially on the training of tourism professionals and the management of tourism destinations in a highly competitive manner. .
Minister Sok Soken and Mr. Makass Berry also discussed further in promoting human resource development through vocational training by continuing to implement the second phase of the Skills Development Program 2024-2028, establishing a tourism vocational training mechanism in line with the Cambodian National Qualifications. Establish an online competency test system and support tourist destination management software for major tourist destinations in Cambodia.
Ministry of Mines and Energy issues press release on campaign to crack down on anarchic gold mining business in Memot district, Tbong Khmum province
According to the Ministry of Mines and Energy, on January 10, 2024, the Ministry of Mines and Energy, with the Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Mines and Energy in collaboration with the Tbong Khmum Provincial Administration under the coordination of the Tbong Khmum Provincial Prosecutor's Office, launched the operation. Settle on a large scale at a squatter gold mine in Sampov Loun village, Choam Tamao commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province.
In Sampov Loun village, Choam Tamao commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province, this is a family-owned gold mining business area since the 1990s, where local people have been digging and submerging gold by hand as a family. But in recent years, there has been a shift from hand-made and simple household items to the use of explosives and chemical equipment, with tunnels being dug in some places.
After seeing the serious challenges to safety, health and the environment, the Ministry of Mines and Energy, with the Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Mines and Energy in cooperation with local authorities, conducted several outreach and legal action against illegal mining activities in Subsequent upper areas.
In fact, between September 2021 and November 2023, Tbong Khmum Provincial Administration established a joint provincial working group to implement measures to disseminate legal aspects to the people and to close a large number of anarchic gold mines under the order of the Deputy Prosecutor. Accompanied by Tbong Khmum Provincial Court. But cracking down on anarchic mining sites in the area in the past has been like a search.
The Ministry of Mines and Energy is committed to ending anarchic mining activities and promoting legal mining that brings many national interests, including the creation of on-site and indirect job opportunities and contributing to the creation of Additional sources of national budget revenue and the elimination of serious environmental and social impacts, as well as contributing to the development of local communities through sustainable mining with the support and protection of the law.
In this regard, the Ministry of Mines and Energy would like to thank the relevant authorities for participating in the previous mechanism successfully and this time successfully, and would like to thank the relevant people for their cooperation.
Taking this opportunity, the Ministry of Mines and Energy would like to call on the people who are doing anarchic gold mining business to stop all these illegal activities and participate in preventing them by notifying the anarchic mining activities to the Ministry of Mines and Energy by calling 095. 727 727.
The production of plastic waste has caused many environmental problems, including health risks!
(Phnom Penh): The production of plastic waste has caused many environmental problems, such as: air pollution, greenhouse gas emissions by burning plastic waste, affecting human and animal health by increasing the presence of microplastics in water sources and endangering biological hazards. Diverse from a lot of plastic waste in the seas and oceans.
In addition to plastic bags, there are plastic materials used in food and beverage services, such as: plates, foam boxes, glasses, spoons, forks, knives, straws, plastic boxes, which are increasingly popular.
According to a recent study by the American Academy of Sciences, the use of plastic bottles for drinking water can be harmful to health. Experts have shown that there are thousands of plastic particles in a liter of water that are trapped in plastic bottles. Plastic particles can pose a health risk (cardiovascular and brain problems) and cause cancer.
The same goes for the use of plastic for food ports. Plastic bags and foam boxes are used for porting or packing various items, including food. Plastic or foam boxes that hold hot food can have a number of health problems, especially cancer, diabetes, heart disease, kidney disease and affect the memory system. The Office of the Prime Minister announces the results of the meeting between Samdech Hun Manet and the Ambassador of Indonesia
