Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith emphasized that through these three priority work directions, one hand is to reform the judiciary, and the other hand is to resolve disputes outside the judiciary so that there will not be too many cases in court. He added that the increasing number of cases in the court will definitely affect the quality of implementation.
In this regard, Mr. Keut Rith claimed that both justice services have been improved while quality has been reviewed. He added that through the second campaign, people who have suffered injustice or illegal abuse have an official way to complain to the Ministry of Justice for intervention.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith, the approach to leading the campaign to strengthen and improve the service of justice and the quality of justice in leading these two campaigns, the Campaign Steering Committee will adhere to two approaches: First: the noble approach of Samdech President Hun Manet for Reform and Second: Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Noble Approach for Strengthening Governance.
* Prince Hun Manet's four-point approach, which states that "no reform is easy, successful reform must be based on four main factors: 1: have a clear vision, 2: have a commitment High spirits, 3: to be honestly involved and 4: to be dedicated.
