Printing Institute of Mengli J University. Kouch publishes the book "Queen: Khmer Traditional Leadership"
Priest Kong Viel stated at the book launch that he wrote the book because he was fond of Khmer culture, and when studying Khmer history, he found that there was little writing about the leadership of the Khmer kings. Which was strong in the past. Instead, he observed that most of them were written only by the leaders of foreign powers such as Alexander the Great, Napoleon, Ong Bonaparte and Winston Churchill, for example.
"Are there any books that describe specific Khmer leadership?" "Among the many genres we see are romantic novels, children's stories, historical research books, keys to success and presence, especially in Cambodian bookstores, only books on general leadership." This is according to the content of the press release presented in the book launch program.
According to Rev. Kong Viel, this book is an ongoing research and needs to be improved through discussions and exchanges of ideas to foster a culture of courageous and virtuous leadership both at home and abroad. He thanked the current leadership for ensuring one of the longest periods of peace in Cambodia since the return of the monarchy.
The book, introduced by Duke Dr. Kouch Mengly, will be available in all bookstores in the Kingdom of Cambodia and will be published in two languages, Khmer and English. The French language is also being prepared.
