(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Hun Manet on Wednesday afternoon, January 10, 2023, received Ms. TEO Lay Cheng, Ambassador of Singapore to Cambodia for a courtesy call and discussion. At the Peace Palace. National Assembly President Khuon Sodary and Cuban Ambassador Appreciate the Participation of Women in Peace and Development
On the occasion of allowing Ms. Lyukaro Rodriguez Barrio, who is out of her diplomatic mission in Cambodia, to pay a courtesy call and say goodbye on the morning of January 10, 2024 at the National Assembly, President of the National Assembly Khuon Sodary praised and appreciated the results. The Ambassador's diplomatic mission to contribute to the strengthening of the long-standing good relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Cuba has been steadily growing.
The President of the National Assembly mentioned the activities of the Ambassador during her diplomatic mission in Cambodia to participate in all social, political and women's programs. Samdech said that due to the similar situation, Cambodian and Cuban women have stood strong and cooperated with men in all fields with courage. The National Assembly stressed that difficulties have made women strong.
At the same time, Ms. Lyukaro Rodriguez Bario also praised the active participation of Cambodian women in politics, society and economy. In particular, she mentioned the ability and talent in the leadership of the National Assembly as a model and symbol of women. The Ambassador herself has learned and learned a lot from the President of the National Assembly.
Completing a mission in Cambodia is like being away from your family. But she is pleased with the success of the diplomatic mission in Cambodia, which has received the support and encouragement of the Royal Government, the National Assembly and especially the Cambodian people. The Ambassador said that Cuba continues to support Cambodia's development, especially the provision of health scholarships to Cambodian students studying in Cuba.
In addition, National Assembly President Khuon Sodary and Ms. Lyuka Rodriguez Bario highlighted the good relations between Cambodia and Cuba, which have been nurtured by leaders at all levels of the two countries since the time of King Norodom Sihanouk and former President Fiorentina. Where Castro came from. The National Assembly stressed that Cuba is a good friend of Cambodia, which helped Cambodia in difficult times after recovering from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot in 1979.
In a press conference on the afternoon of January 9, 2024, Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith emphasized that contrary to the commutation of the punishment for those who caused traffic accidents, evading irresponsibility will be added to another type of crime, running crime. Escape.
Mr. Keut Rith stressed that those who cause traffic accidents and escape will be subject to the strictest legal measures. Therefore, traffic accident cases will be given priority.
Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith said: "I encourage the use of legal mitigation measures, not by means of escape, but will take mitigation measures if the person who caused the accident shows courage and cooperation. Resolve before the law.
He explained that a traffic accident is not punishable by life imprisonment, but if the perpetrator does not dare to face the law, he will become an outlaw for life, so if the perpetrator comes forward, the court must take action Relax and this is a guarantee of construction and justice.
Mr. Keut Rith added that when a traffic accident occurs, the first thing to consider is compensation for the victim and then determine who is wrong or who is right based on the facts, the law and the actual evidence.
It should be informed that recently, the number of traffic accidents seems to increase significantly, especially in Phnom Penh and always happens at night. In some cases, the victims lost their lives while the perpetrators tried to escape.
