National Assembly of Cambodia and Pakistan push for the establishment of a Memorandum of Understanding on deeper cooperation in all fields in the near future
The commitment to push for the establishment of Memoranda of Understanding (MOUs) between the two parliaments was made during a meeting with National Assembly President Khuon Sodary on Wednesday morning, January 10. This year 2024 at the National Assembly.
On that occasion, the Ambassador celebrated the free, fair and non-violent elections in Cambodia. He said Pakistan was one of the countries that witnessed the July general election, sending many of its key figures to observe.
The Ambassador also congratulated the National Assembly President, who was elected by the National Assembly as the President of the National Assembly for the seventh term, the first woman in Cambodia to hold this noble position in serving the people and the nation.
Zahiruddin Baba Thahim informed the National Assembly President that in February, Pakistan will hold parliamentary elections. Following the election of the new National Assembly, Pakistan will encourage the establishment of a Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation between the National Assembly of Pakistan and Cambodia in order to strengthen and expand the cooperation between the two parliaments in both fields. And multilateral.
National Assembly President Khuon Sodary supported the Ambassador's remarks and stressed that the strengthening of the two countries' National Assembly cooperation to be strong, active and comprehensive is also the desire of the National Assembly of Cambodia.
He stressed that the cooperation between the National Assembly and the two governments will not only serve the interests of peace, stability and development of Cambodia and Pakistan, but will also serve the common interests of participating in maintaining peace and stability in the region. And the whole world.
The National Assembly President praised the active participation of the Pakistani Parliament in the Inter-Parliamentary Forum on Peace and Humanitarian Affairs, especially the Pakistani Parliamentary Delegation, which is always present at the Inter-Parliamentary Forum or General Assembly hosted by the Cambodian National Assembly. Past.
National Assembly President Khuon Sodary thanked Pakistan for supporting the Cambodian elections and for always encouraging development in Cambodia.
At the same time, the National Assembly President also asked Pakistan to consider the possibility of expanding investment and trade in Cambodia, such as agro-food processing, Halal "Halal" promotes the establishment of direct flights between the two countries and connect People-to-people contacts in tourism.
In response, the Pakistani Ambassador is optimistic that once the Royal Cambodian Embassy in Pakistan is officially established, the strengthening of cooperation in all fields between the two countries will continue to grow rapidly.
Regarding trade, the Ambassador informed that the Pakistani Embassy in Phnom Penh is currently working closely with the Ministry of Commerce, Council for the Development of Cambodia, hoping that a trade agreement will be finalized soon. Coming soon.
