(Phnom Penh): Every year during the dry season from December to April, the air quality results monitored by the Ministry of Environment in Phnom Penh and provinces across the country show that the air quality situation is declining alarmingly, especially growth. Concentrations of inert particles floating in the air (PM10 and PM2.5) can exceed the standard, which poses a risk to human health and the environment.
According to the survey, the main sources and activities that cause the increase in the concentration of inert particles include: emissions from industrial vehicles, especially forest fires, burning of grass, burning of agricultural waste, burning of forest, burning of walls, burning. Solid waste in the open and fires at landfills, dumping and incineration of plastic waste, as well as dust from construction sites.
In this regard, in order to prevent and prevent air pollution in the capital-province, the Ministry of Environment has requested the 25 capital-provincial governors to promote the implementation of the Royal Government's Circular No. 01 on measures to prevent and reduce public air pollution to the municipal administration. Khan, Commune, Sangkat, People will prepare the means and take the following measures:
