(Kiev): Ukraine's power grid operator said on Tuesday (January 9) that the cold weather this winter has left more than 1,000 cities and villages without electricity in nine regions. Increased electricity consumption. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on January 9, 2024.
Electricity operators said electricity consumption was at its highest level this week as temperatures dropped to -1 degrees Celsius in many parts of the country. "Consumption levels continue to rise due to the sharp drop in temperatures across the country," the source said.
Ukraine's Ministry of Energy says 1,025 villages were without electricity on Jan. 9 as the war-torn country was hit by unusually cold waves, snow and strong winds.
"Emergency crews in the area affected by the bad weather are working tirelessly to repair the damage," the ministry said in a statement. "However, the ice makes the job harder."
The Ukrainian Meteorological Center forecast worsening weather with more snow in the south and southeast with temperatures dropping to -21 degrees Celsius at night and -12 degrees Celsius during the day.
