(Phnom Penh): Mr. Yang Saing Koma, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, confirmed the current deployment of 250 Commune / Sangkat Agriculture Officers after being selected to be deployed in 17 provinces rich in rice production.
According to Mr. Yang Saing Koma, the 250 commune agricultural officers who were newly elected at the end of 2023, the Ministry of Agriculture will start training in February for one month and will be required to work in the commune from March 2024 onwards. He said that even if the agricultural officials go to work in the commune, the Ministry will continue to provide regular training in addition to general skills, agricultural techniques, promotion and market research.
He also said that commune agriculture officials who visit the communes have a role as facilitators rather than technical experts, because the Ministry of Agriculture has organized a multi-skilled team that can go to technical training for farmers.
It should be informed that at the beginning of 2023, according to the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries deployed agricultural officers in about 10 pilot communes in Cheung Prey district, Kampong Cham province.
Chinese military tells US military that Beijing will not back down on Taiwan (Video inside) (BEIJING) Urges Washington to stop arming Taiwan, as well as to provoke trouble in the South China Sea. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, January 10, 2024.
The talks took place in Washington on Monday and Tuesday earlier this week, just days before Taiwan is set to hold a general election to elect its new leader. In a statement issued Wednesday, the Chinese Defense Ministry said that China will not compromise or withdraw from the Taiwan issue and urge the United States to stop arming Taiwan.
In addition, China has urged Washington to reduce its military deployment and stop provocative activities in the South China Sea, and to stop supporting abuses and provocations. "The United States should clearly understand the origins of insecurity, both in the air and at sea, and reduce military deployments, as well as stop inflating and exaggerating." According to the Chinese Ministry of Defense.
However, the US side, through the Pentagon, did not react significantly to the Chinese Defense Ministry's remarks, only emphasizing the importance of maintaining military-to-military contacts in order to avoid Let the rivalry between the two powers turn into war or armed conflict.
