(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, on the afternoon of January 9, 2024, spent about 3 hours to explain in detail the two campaigns that the Ministry of Justice has launched in accordance with the assignment of Samdech Moha Bovathithipat Hun The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Manet, during the first plenary session of the Council of Ministers on August 24, 2023.
The two campaigns that Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith presented at a press conference at the Ministry of Justice in front of a number of journalists were: First, a campaign to promote and expedite the settlement of cases in court and second: Campaign to monitor and resolve irregularities in court.
Both campaigns are aimed at strengthening and enhancing the service of justice and the quality of justice, which is the desire of the Prime Minister to promote "the rule of law" and "justice in society". This is considered an important political priority to be implemented as a result for the seventh legislature of the National Assembly.
He asserted that the first campaign will improve the quality and efficiency of the provision of justice services to the people quickly and easily, and the second campaign will help to find justice for the people, as well as promote transparency, integrity and fairness. In law enforcement and court proceedings.
In which, Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith explained to each campaign as follows: * Campaign to promote and expedite the settlement of cases in court: This campaign covers all types of cases, both civil and non-civil cases. Criminal cases, both commercial and other, in the courts and the prosecution at all levels.
Based on an assessment of the number of cases remaining pending across the country and based on experience in the successful implementation of past congestion-solving campaigns at provincial and municipal courts, the Ministry of Justice has assessed that The implementation of the first campaign may be completed within a maximum of 3 years from the date of the announcement of the campaign on January 9, 2024 onwards.
The implementation of the campaign to promote and expedite the settlement of cases in this court must be carried out on the basis of justice, integrity and fairness, with strict adherence to the "fast, accurate and just law-based" approach, and to avoid Absolutely "dry fish take eggs" situation by using this campaign for personal gain or to commit any corruption.
The campaign to investigate and resolve irregularities in the courts will focus on two main issues: first: review and resolve irregularities in the administration of the tribunal and the prosecution of the tribunal and second: Examine and resolve irregularities in case action and in court decisions in all types of cases. This campaign lasts for 5 years from the announcement date of the campaign on January 9, 2024 onwards.
However, Deputy Prime Minister Keut Rith claimed that the Ministry of Justice will not interfere in the work of the judiciary, that is, the judiciary is independent.
