Paul, which can be seen in the sky in the north, looks like a beautiful veil, swaying like a wave. It is a particle that carries electricity from the sun and touches the earth's magnetic field, pushing it toward the two poles.
At an altitude of 60 km to 2,000 km (usually between 100 and 140 km), these electrically charged particles affect the air molecules like the electric current in a neon lamp. Also colored. If the flux is too strong, it means that more particles from the sun can spread, so this phenomenon can sometimes be seen in France.
