At the request of both parties, the guardians of the victims and the guardians of the perpetrators decided not to file a complaint because the case of anarchy in the school of the female student did not cause physical harm and the child was a minor.
Authorities asked Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner General and Commissioner of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, and the Phnom Penh Municipal Prosecutor's Office to allow him to return home with a guarantee from his parents to continue his education.
