Samdech Hun Sen Manet: In order for the reform to be successful, four major factors are needed: a clear vision based on national interests, high commitment, sincere participation and dedication for the common good (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Moha Bhavathibati On the morning of January 9, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Hun Manet, spoke about his experience and remarks on successful reforms.
Samdech stated that in order for the reform to be successful, four major factors are needed: first, there must be a clear vision based on the national interest of the people, and second, high commitment from practitioners and leaders, and third, Loyal participation from all stakeholders, especially the people, and fourth, sacrifice for the common good.
The Prime Minister stated that the reform is not a revolution, not the cancellation of previous policies, but the strengthening and sharpening of further achievements for the benefit of the nation.
Regarding the success of this reform, Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet explained by giving practical examples of the reform of the Higher Secondary Diploma Examination (Bakdup) which started from 2014 to the present, which has shown success.
The Prime Minister made this remark during a meeting with 1691 A-level students at the OCIC Convention Center on the morning of January 9, 2024.
"Reform is not easy, but successful reform requires four main factors: First, there must be a long-term vision based on a clear national interest and the people must be the basis," he said. The second factor is the high commitment of all actors, especially the willing leaders and practitioners, the third is the participation of all parties, especially the people, and the fourth is the sacrifice for the common good. .
Samdech Prime Minister stated that through the successful reform of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports's Baccalaureate exam, which made the accuracy of the competition, Samdech believes that the overwhelming majority of people will continue to support this reform. .
