Duke Kith Meng's company launches "RGX" trading platform using Cambodia's first blockchain technology in the securities sector
"This is an important event for the country's financial landscape as we introduce a nursery that opens the door for the country to enter a new era of freedom and financial opportunity," said Duke Kith Meng. For Royal Group, RGX Nursery is not only a business platform, it is a testament to our commitment to innovation, progress and the future for Cambodian youth. ”
Duke Kith Meng added that RGX aims to be a catalyst for change, promote financial integration and empower all members of our community to access opportunities presented by the digital economy. The launch of the RGX trading platform in the FinTech regulation of the securities sector is a testament to the progress of financial technology (FinTech) in the Cambodian securities sector.
Mr. Sou Socheat said that the launch of the "RGX" trading platform in the financial technology testing environment in the securities sector is a clear sign of the progress of financial technology in the securities sector.
"This is another major step forward for us and a testament to the efforts of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia in promoting innovation, ensuring market integrity, and protecting investors, as well as protecting investors," he said. "Active participation from all parties involved, especially the private sector, which has its own Royal Group Trust."
The "RGX" trading platform is a trading platform that uses blockchain technology. This blockchain technology is considered by the world as a new technology that can help increase the efficiency, security and transparency of financial transactions, as well as create opportunities for new financial products and services, especially in the securities sector.
Features of blockchain technology create a decentralized database system that can keep track of all trading transactions that take place, as well as be verifiable by all parties involved and can not be modified. Comply with a common rule in the form of a Smart Contract.
