The North Korean leader's birthday is believed to be January 8, but the North Korean government has never officially recognized the date. The US government has designated 1984 as the year of Kim's birth, which means he has turned 40 this year.
The birthdays of his father and grandfather, Kim Jong-il and Kim Il-sung, former North Korean leaders, are national holidays across Korea. However, Kim Jong Un's premature birthday has always passed quietly, as usual, so there is no mention in the state media or on the North Korean calendar.
