Uon Silot, President of the Cambodian Cashew Association, told Fresh News on January 8, 2024 that crude grain exports may continue to decline further in 2024. This decline is not a negative thing, but a good sign for the cashew processing sector in Cambodia, which shows that local enterprises are growing and have higher processing capacity.
He pointed out that at present, some local cashew processing enterprises and companies are starting to compete with Vietnamese exporters. In the near future, he will be ready to meet with SME banks to discuss favorable lending conditions for processing enterprises so that local enterprises can compete with neighboring countries for purchase, storage and processing to international markets at the same time. The market for processed nuts has a better market.
He expects this year's cashew yield to increase by 10% if the weather is favorable and there is not much rain during the flowering and fruiting seasons, which makes cashews of high quality and good value.
