Hun Manet's questioning came after Mr. Sam Rainsy on social media yesterday, the 45th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day, attacked: Tral.
Calling Mr. Sam Rainsy "that one" at the inauguration of the bridge and talk with more than 10,000 workers in Koh Kong province on the morning of January 8, 2024, Samdech Thipdey said that when the Cambodian people. Due to the genocide of Pol Pot in Cambodia, Sam Rainsy was not present. At the same time, Samdech asked the following three questions:
First, Samdech asked whether between April 17, 1975 and January 7, 1979, the Khmer Rouge killed people in Cambodia? And how many millions died? In this question, Samdech confirmed that the people who survived the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, who survived to this day, were witnesses, and the people, young and old, all the history books recorded and confirmed that the Khmer Rouge killed the Khmer people.
Third: The President asked why to rely on Vietnam? Samdech explained that since 1978, Cambodians have only two choices: to rely on those in the West and those in the East. To the west is the United Nations and to the east is Vietnam. But at that time, why the UN did not send troops to help the Cambodian people is because the UN law does not intervene in any country without the request of the government of that country.
Samdech stated that without Vietnam, the Cambodian people at that time, with a strength of about 10,000, could not fight to defeat the Khmer Rouge. And at that time it was not possible to build hundreds of thousands of forces to fight the Khmer Rouge, as people died every day.
He called on the next generation of Cambodians to learn more about January 7 and not to use political tendencies to interpret historical factors.
