Currently, the suspect and the seized evidence have prepared a case to be sent to the Kampong Speu Provincial Court according to the procedure.
General Vong Pisen: The army must not be involved in the drug problem, if found, even the general must be expelled from the framework
(Kampong Speu): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF), has made it clear that all troops must not be involved in the use, trafficking and provision of drug production sites, if found, even at the rank of General. The Royal Cambodian Armed Forces will be legally punished.
This clear statement by General Vong Pisen was made on the occasion of the General presiding over the closing ceremony of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) Sports Competition at the Active Officers' School (Thmat Pong) on January 7, 2024 to celebrate the anniversary. 45th Anniversary of the Victory Day, January 7 (January 7, 1979 - January 7, 2024).
The Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) emphasized, "The Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) will not allow drug trafficking. "Until the fighters."
General Vong Pisen said that this order has been in place for a long time and we must take care of our own well-being. Must be expelled from the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
General Vong Pises also emphasized that for the army that uses drugs and answers that he is a victim because of drugs. For this punishment, if it is at a low level, it is to be expelled from the framework. "And recently I have seen that in recent days the navy has been expelled from the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, both colonel and lieutenant, due to drug use."
In addition, General Vong Pisen stated that as the army, it is strictly forbidden to provide private and communal land to criminals for drug production in any form. In this case, if any army dares to commit this crime, it will be punished according to the law.
It should be informed that the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Hun Sen recently issued a strict order for the Minister of Interior and the Minister of National Defense to purge all armed forces from involvement and drug use. Anyone who uses or is involved in drugs must be expelled immediately.
Samdech Hun Sen also stressed that as an armed force, law enforcement officials must be clean and free of drugs. He said that Interior Minister Sar Sokha had already announced that any police officer who tested for drugs would be expelled. Separately, within the framework of the army, there is also the practice of expelling any soldiers who find the substance since 2019.
The Prime Minister stated that any armed forces that trade in drugs must be expelled from the framework and face the law.
(Phnom Penh): Throughout 2023, Cambodia achieved a total export of nearly 8.5 million tons of agricultural products, valued at nearly 4.5 billion dollars, a decrease of 1.90%. This is according to the report on the situation of agriculture, forestry and fisheries in 2023 of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
According to the Ministry of Agriculture, in 2023, the estimated value of agricultural exports (unit price based on exporters' invoices) will be 4,306,810,688.50 US dollars.
Please be informed that the agricultural sector has actively contributed to ensuring food security, raising people's living standards, reducing poverty, increasing exports and sustaining national economic growth despite the effects of natural disasters and global crises.
(Banteay Meanchey): 132 Indian guests left Thailand for Cambodia through the Poipet International Gate to visit the Angkor Wat temples in Siem Reap and continue their tours at resorts in Cambodia.
Brigadier General E Chamroeun, Chief of the Immigration Police Station at the Poipet International Gate, told Fresh News on January 8, 2023 that 132 Indian tourists (27 females) had left Thailand. Khlong Lek Port enters Cambodia via Poipet International Port for a tour of Cambodia in the Angkor Wat area of Siem Reap Province and further tours at various Cambodian resorts.
He confirmed that Indian tourists entered through Poipet International Gate on January 6, 2024 and returned at Phnom Penh International Airport on January 9, 2024.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has sent a letter to Emmanuel Macron, President of the French Republic, in response to a recent letter from the President inviting him to pay an official visit to France on May 18-19. January 2024 is coming.
In the message, the President stated as follows:
His Excellency the President!
I would like to express my sincere respect and thank you for inviting me to pay an official visit to the French Republic on January 18-19. It is a great honor and I would like to take this opportunity with a strong commitment to discuss and strengthen our bilateral relations.
In addition, strengthening economic ties, sharing sustainable development strategies, cooperating in the field of defense, promoting our cultural heritage and promoting Francophone are pillars of our bilateral relations.
I am confident that our discussions will contribute to a deeper understanding and bring together joint initiatives that will benefit both countries. Cambodia is committed to continuing to participate in this effort, recognizing the importance of our partnership for our people and for the international community.
I look forward to meeting and discussing fruitfully with His Excellency. Please accept, Excellency, the assurances of my highest consideration. "
