Samdech Hun Sen Manet: Peace Day 29 December Celebrated for All Cambodians Who Hate War and Love Peace (Video inside) (Koh Kong) All Cambodians who hate war and love peace, and there is nothing wrong with people wanting to remember peace, keep peace.
This statement was made by the Prime Minister during the inauguration ceremony of a concrete bridge and a meeting with more than 10,000 workers in Koh Kong province on the morning of January 8, 2024.
He said that in order to end the war, there must be a clear policy, and that policy is the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who finally ended the war that lasted for about 500 years.
On January 1, 2024, the Royal Government issued a sub-decree designating December 29 as the day to celebrate Peace Day in Cambodia and a national holiday. However, there is criticism from foreign extremists that the celebration of this day is for the family, regardless of the suffering of the people who suffered in the war.
"Some people came out and criticized that the National Day on December 29 is for the Hun family," he said. I would like to say that I do not deny that the clan also welcomes peace, so Peace Day is for all Cambodians who love peace and hate war, including one clan, but not exclusively for the clan, but for all Cambodians who "Love peace and benefit from peace is our people all over the country."
The President affirmed that this Peace Day in Cambodia is for all Cambodians who love peace and hate war, because all people need to live in peace, live in development, live in peace.
It should be informed that on January 1, 2024, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet issued a sub-decree designating December 29 every year as "Peace Day in Cambodia", which is an official national holiday in the Kingdom of Cambodia. The designation of December 29 as Peace Day in Cambodia is to:
* In response to the sacred desire of the Cambodian people is to love peace and to hate war.
* A reminder of the achievement of a complete end to the war and the establishment of complete peace and national unity in the Kingdom of Cambodia by the political victory on December 29, 1998.
* It is a reminder to all generations of Cambodians, both now and in the future, to always remember the great destruction of the nation and the misery of the Cambodian people, as well as the consequences of war and national division. As well as inspiring Cambodians of all generations to hate war.
* Inspiring Cambodians of all generations, both now and in the future, to better understand the "values of peace" and to jointly promote the "culture of peace" in Cambodia, especially to participate in the protection and preservation. Absolutely "peace", which is the life of the nation and the most valuable foundation for the development of the nation and the peace of the Cambodian people in a sustainable and prosperous manner.
The same sub-decree states that this Peace Day in Cambodia is designated as a public holiday. All ministries, institutions, sub-national administrations, civil society, international organizations and the private sector must join in inspiring the Cambodian people to understand the values of peace, promote a culture of peace and jointly maintain peace in Cambodia.
