A spokesman for the Bangladesh Election Commission told AFP on Monday morning that Hasina's ruling Awami League party had won the by-elections following a reported turnout. Only 40 percent of Bangladesh's 120 million eligible voters cast their ballots.
The Bangladesh Nationalist Party (BNP) is among several other opposition parties that have decided not to run in the general election on the grounds that it is a rigged election that will not be free or fair. Opposition groups called for the people of Bangladesh not to go to the polls.
As the final results are due to be announced at a ceremony on Monday, Bangladeshi election officials say Hasina's party has won about three-quarters of the seats in parliament, or at least 220 seats. Out of a total of 300 seats. But support for other lawmakers, including those from the coalition, will pave the way for Hasina's party to control parliament by an overwhelming majority.
