Senior official in Qingdao, Shandong Province announces investment promotion in Cambodia
(China): A senior official of Qingdao, Shandong Province, China has announced that he will encourage more investment from Qingdao, Shandong Province, China to Cambodia to contribute to improving the economy and livelihood of Cambodians.
The announcement was made during a meeting between Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, and Wang Luming, chairman of the Standing Committee of the Qingdao People's Congress, on Saturday, January 6, 2024. The meeting was also attended by the presidents of several large companies in Qingdao who are looking for investment opportunities in Cambodia.
Wang Luming briefed Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol on key potentials in Qingdao, such as port and container traffic, economic and industrial activities, as well as research and development prominence.
In line with the strong friendship between Cambodia and China and the past cooperation between Cambodia and Qingdao, Wang Luming expressed his willingness to encourage investment and further cooperation to increase closeness as well as to expand employment opportunities. To the people of Cambodia.
The Deputy Prime Minister thanked the Chairman of the Standing Committee of the Qingdao People's Congress for his warm welcome to the Cambodian delegation. The Deputy Prime Minister also responded to the mention of the close friendship between Cambodia and China, which has brought a lot of cooperation and investment, and China has become the first largest investor in China. Cambodia.
The Deputy Prime Minister also highlighted that Cambodia has set a goal to become a high-income economy by 2050 to achieve this vision, which requires the participation of the private sector. The Council for the Development of Cambodia acts as an attraction, facilitator and caregiver for investors to achieve the growth of investment companies in Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol also mentioned the initiative between Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet and Chinese President Xi Jinping to set 2024 as the year of people-to-people exchanges to boost Chinese tourism. Cambodia to more and more.
It should be noted that Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol is visiting Qingdao, Shandong Province, China. The visit is aimed at mobilizing and persuading Chinese investors to invest in Cambodia, such as knocking on the door for Chinese investors to come to Cambodia.
The process of attracting Chinese investors to Cambodia was also accompanied by the leadership of the Cambodian Duke Association, with its Vice President and Board members, including Duke Leang Khun, Duke Vinh Hour, Duke Lang Kang and Duke Ty Piseth. Tbong Khmum Provincial Government Officials and Citizens Celebrate the 45th Anniversary of January 7 Victory Day
