Mr. Teang Sokun brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and Mr. Kong Sophoan, Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee in Kandal Province with the deepest condolences and sympathy.
The Branch Director continued that the Cambodian Red Cross, with Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen as its President, always thinks about the well-being of the general public at all times and even regularly advises all local officials to check. From the lives of the people, as well as visiting vulnerable people and victims of various disasters, regardless of race, religion or political affiliation.
He expressed deep regret and sympathy for the incident that we all do not want to happen to all of us.
At the same time, the branch director also encouraged and encouraged the victims, please do not be discouraged and hopeless in life, please continue to work hard to earn a living to support our family's daily life.
Please be informed that at 3:20 AM on January 4, 2024, in Kampong Chamlong village, Prek Tonleab commune, Leuk Dek district, Kandal province (the entrance to the old ferry), there was a case of fire in 3 houses, including the house Two were hit by an ant and the other was completely burnt.
Donation provided by CRC branch in Kandal province to the three affected families, each family received: 50 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 box of pure water, 1 box of fish sauce, 1 kit, in which 2 houses Accident with light received 300,000 Riels, while the completely burnt house received a rubber tent and 800,000 Riels.
