(Phnom Penh): On Sunday, January 7, 2024, Mr. Dith Tina, Chairman of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Government Working Group, presided over a meeting to commemorate the 45th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day.
Addressing the entire ceremony, Mr. Dith Tina recalled the reality of the January 7 Victory Day, when the Cambodian People's Party led the liberation of Cambodia from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot. The genocidal regime of Pol Pot, which turned Cambodia into a dark killing field for 3 years, 8 months and 20 days.
In 3 years, 8 months and 20 days, Cambodia was under the control of the genocidal regime led by Pol Pot. Family ties, lifestyles, traditions and customs of the people were completely destroyed. Under extremist ideology, 7 million Cambodians are living in hell, and nearly 3 million of them are dead.
Mr. Dith Tina emphasized that the CPP not only liberated Cambodia from the clutches of Pol Pot, but after the liberation on January 7, 1979, all the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party worked tirelessly to lead the construction. The country is recovering from empty hands to the current development.
Under the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party, the people have regained their full rights and freedoms, and the whole nation is peaceful and prosperous in all areas. At the same time, Cambodia has regained its prestige and image on the international stage.
According to Dith Tina, this historical fact, no matter how much time has passed 45 years ago, or how long it will take for young people to take turns, must remember the spirit of January 7 and be grateful for the heroic sacrifice of your hero. Liberation, especially Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party and all party leaders in the cause of the motherland of Cambodia.
Young people must take turns to be determined to avoid this bitter history from happening again on our beloved homeland of Cambodia. The youth in turn must be determined to defend the peace that the CPP has hardly seized from the clutches of Pol Pot and together as a whole push the Cambodian ship to move forward under the shadow of lasting peace.
