Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth presides over the celebration of the 45th Anniversary of January 7 Victory Day
(Kandal): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group in Kandal Province, led a meeting to celebrate the 45th anniversary of the 7 January Victory Day (January 7, 1979 - January 7). 2024) in Takhmao city, Kandal province on January 7, 2024.
The meeting was also attended by Mr. Nou Sakhorn, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth said that January 7 is an important national holiday in which all Cambodians commemorate the merits of female warriors who sacrificed their lives to liberate the country and its people from the genocidal regime. The brutal massacre of more than 3 million people is unprecedented in the history of mankind.
He affirmed that the spirit of January 7 has immortal values both for the past 45 years and in moving forward for the nation and the people of Cambodia, which we must commit to continue to unite around the Royal Government under the umbrella of the Constitution and the cool shadow of The King to continue to achieve new achievements. China to sanction five US arms manufacturers over arms sales to Taiwan
BEIJING: China will impose sanctions on five US military equipment manufacturers in response to the latest US arms sales to Taiwan, a Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman said on Sunday. According to Reuters.
US arms sales to Taiwan are a frequent source of tension between Washington and Beijing. China considers democratically ruled Taiwan its territory, but this claim has been rejected by the Taiwanese government.
The sanctions come ahead of Taiwan's January 13 presidential and parliamentary elections. The US State Department last month approved the sale of $ 300 million worth of military equipment to help maintain Taiwan's strategic information system.
A Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman was quoted by Reuters as saying in a statement that the recent arms sales "seriously undermined China's sovereignty and security interests. "To peace and stability in the Taiwan Strait seriously."
China will freeze the assets of these companies and ban any person or entity in China from engaging with them, the spokesman added.
Mr. Hun Many led the celebration of January 7 Victory Day with the people, local authorities and civil servants of the Armed Forces in Kampong Speu province
(Kampong Speu): This morning, January 7, 2024, coincides with the 45th anniversary of the Victory Day over the genocidal regime of Pol Pot at the Independence Monument in Kampong Speu province. People celebrated January 7 Victory Day.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. HUN Many, Minister of Public Works and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Kampong Speu Province, as well as the presence of Senators, National Assembly members in the Kampong Speu Provincial Assembly and Constituency, Deputy Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group, Provincial Leaders, Departments and Units. And the Armed Forces throughout the province.
The January 7 Victory Day celebration is a reminder of the sacrifices and sacrifices of brave warriors and leaders of the previous generation who sacrificed their lives to free the nation and people from the abyss of Pol Pot genocide. .
The people of Kampong Speu province with happy faces and smiles expressed their congratulations on the achievements that the province as well as the whole country has achieved in the last 45 years, which has made progress in all fields.
In his speech, the President of the Party, read by Mr. Hun Many, recalled the historical heroism and mission of the leaders, the pure patriots of the Cambodian People's Party in the national liberation and the successful quest for peace. Completely chronic internal conflicts. At the same time, Samdech reaffirmed the party's high commitment to continue to maintain peace, which is the foundation of development.
It should be noted that during the celebration of the 45th anniversary of the victory over the genocidal regime on January 7, in addition to listening to the meaningful speech of the party president and the funeral, there was also a multi-public performance by artists from the Department of Culture and Fine Arts. The province and the release of pigeons and balloons are also a symbol of respect, gratitude and thanksgiving for peace.
