(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, encouraged the Jiangsu Chinese Entrepreneurs Association in Cambodia, as well as all members, to expand investment in Cambodia and trade between Cambodia and China to contribute to economic development and development. Welfare in Cambodian society.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha supported and encouraged the Jiangsu Chinese Entrepreneurs Association in Cambodia to continue its mission to promote the expansion of relations between Cambodia and China and contribute to the economic development and welfare of Cambodian society.
Through the close relationship between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the People's Republic of China, Mr. Sar Sokha encouraged investors who are members of the Jiangsu Chinese Entrepreneurs Association in Cambodia to further expand investment in Cambodia to contribute to the strengthening of Cambodian ties. - China now and in the future.
He added that for most of the year 2023, the trade volume between Cambodia and China amounted to more than 11 billion US dollars, of which exports from Cambodia to China exceeded 1.3 billion US dollars. With an increase of 18.5 percent, imports from China to Cambodia exceeded 9.7 billion US dollars, an increase of 3.1 percent.
President Sam Ol also said that the Cambodia-China Friendship Association is ready to cooperate with the Jiangsu Chinese Entrepreneurs Association in Cambodia and other partners to provide more benefits to the people.
President of the Jiangsu Chinese Entrepreneurs Association in Cambodia, WU Jingen, stated that as a civil society organization, the Jiangsu Chinese Entrepreneurs Association in Cambodia will play an important role in the major phase of people-to-people exchanges between China and Cambodia. In particular, to deepen economic, trade, cooperation and cultural exchanges between the two countries.
The new president of the association is determined to pay more attention to coordination and close relations with the ministries and institutions of the Royal Government of Cambodia at all levels to seek more resources for the development of members of the Jiangsu Chinese Entrepreneurs Association in Cambodia. .
It should be informed that on that occasion, Mr. Abhisit Dr. Sar Sokha and other presidents also handed over the letter of appointment to the Third Mandate Council of the Jiangsu Chinese Entrepreneurs Association in Cambodia.
General Vong Pisen: Without the January 7 victory, we would not have the life and development we have today
(Kandal): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, claimed that without the January 7, 1979 victory, we would not have the life and development we have today, which is a fact of Cambodia's history. Indestructible.
This statement was made by the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) on Sunday morning, January 7, 2024, on the occasion of the closing ceremony of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) Sports Competition to celebrate the 45th anniversary of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF). January 7 Victory at the Active Officers' School (Thmat Pong).
According to a report by Lt. Gen. But Sopheap, Director of the Active Military Academy, the purpose of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) Sports Competition is to celebrate the 45th anniversary of the January 7, 1979 Victory Day and to commemorate the noble merits of the female warriors. Who made great sacrifices in the fight to overthrow the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and the revival of the Cambodian nation.
Lt. Gen. But Sopheap said that the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) sports program has seven disciplines, including: 7 km armed running, 50 kg weight training, cross-country running, AK-47 shooting and bombing. Dragging a 7-ton military vehicle 700 meters, 200 meters swimming, and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces martial arts with the participation of 14 institutions.
General Vong Pisen praised and appreciated the efforts of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) Activities Committee, Sports Organizing Committee, relevant units, working groups, coaches and all sports teams that co-organized and participated in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) sports celebrations. 45th Anniversary of the historic day of the January 7, 1979 victory.
On that occasion, General Vong Pisen stated that 45 years after the victory of January 7, 1979, Cambodia has gone through many political and economic turning points and changed its face in all fields, ending the long civil war and bringing peace. National unity, territorial unity and development under the wise and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The Commander-in-Chief continued that the sport has been rehabilitated and developed step by step until now. The Cambodian people will always remember, "Without the victory of January 7, 1979, we would not have the life and development in all areas as we do today."
He added that the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, led by Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, is continuing to lead the Cambodian navy and ensure national sustainability, peace and stability, which is the foundation for the nation's development in all areas.
