Dr. Thong Khon confirmed that the celebration, while the Cambodian People's Party throughout the country has been celebrating this event, especially the big event in Phnom Penh under the high presidency of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo. Hun Sen, Chairman of the Supreme Council of the King and President of the Cambodian People's Party, and Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Honorary President of the Cambodian People's Party.
According to Dr. Thong Khon, the purpose of organizing the January 7 Victory Day is to:
First, to make party members and the public better understand the history and the most precious meaning of the January 7 victory for the nation and the people of Cambodia. On that basis, always remember the great merits of heroes, warriors, women and patriots, as well as friends who have sacrificed the most courage in the fight to overthrow the genocidal regime and protect the revival of the Cambodian people.
Second, to raise people's awareness of the great achievements of the nation's history, which have been achieved over the past 45 years under the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party, as well as the lessons of the nation's precious experience, and are committed to maintaining Strengthen and expand these achievements to be stable, stable and grow further.
Third, to make it clear to the national and international public that Cambodia is firmly moving forward on the path of democracy and the rule of law and adherence to an independent foreign policy based on the absolute protection of national sovereignty.
Fourth, Strengthen the Great Solidarity under the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia to maintain peace, promote the implementation of the first phase of the pentagonal political program and strategy of the Royal Government, the seventh legislature of the National Assembly to achieve success and eliminate all forms of extremist politics. From Cambodia.
It should be noted that at the end of the ceremony, Dr. Thong Khon, on behalf of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Kampong Thom Provincial Party Working Group, also distributed gifts to 70 retirees in Kampong Thom.
Business Awareness: Businesses that adjusting product scanning policies and procedures contribute to reducing costs and enhancing competitiveness.
(Phnom Penh): Traders say that adjusting the principles and procedures for identifying export-import goods will make it easier to export goods to international markets, saving both budget and time, especially contributing to the cut. Lower the cost of goods, which will make it easier to compete on price.
Recently, the Ministry of Economy and Finance issued a Prakas on the revision of the principles and procedures for identifying export-import goods and transit goods in containers that must pass through the scanner inspection system implemented from the first day. January 2024 onwards.
B. Other export goods to be inspected by the scanner can be inspected by the scanner at the Customs Office and the Dry Port Authority or at the export port at the request of the owner or as determined by the Customs Administration.
Oknha Lim Heng, vice president of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, told Fresh News that on behalf of the private sector, congratulations on the revision of the principles and procedures. This is a focus of the Royal Government and an encouragement to the private sector to do business.
He stressed that the revision of export policies and procedures will make the cost of goods lower, easier to compete with goods from other countries, as well as make the price of goods in the market more affordable.
According to Tycoon Lim Heng, in the past, all goods stored in a container cost $ 10 per scan for a 20-foot container, while a 40-foot container costs $ 16 per scan.
He added: "The exemption of this scan for companies that do not have the risk of regular entry and exit and companies with a good history is reducing costs, which is a good thing for both carriers from Cambodia and into Cambodia is valuable. More appropriate. ”Mr. Thong Khon: 45th Anniversary of January 7 Victory Day Cambodia has achieved many great achievements in all fields.
