Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that the anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day this year was celebrated in a situation where the Kingdom of Cambodia has achieved new great achievements in all fields after Cambodia won the battle of the 19-crisis Kovid crisis. Let us re-open the country since the end of 2021 and have been moving forward with confidence on the path of peace, democracy, rule of law and development.
Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Occasion of the 45th Anniversary of January 7 Victory Day
The following are the main contents of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech during the gathering to celebrate the 45th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that January 7, 2024 is the 45th anniversary of the historic victory of the Cambodian people over the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, which revived the Cambodian nation in time. Free from the most heinous torture and murder.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day this year was celebrated in a situation where the Kingdom of Cambodia has achieved new great achievements in all fields after Cambodia won the battle of the 19-crisis Kovid crisis. Let us re-open the country since the end of 2021 and have been moving forward with confidence on the path of peace, democracy, rule of law and development.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the Cambodian National Salvation United Front, which has the support of the people throughout the country and has received large-scale and timely support from the Vietnamese Volunteer Army, as well as the support of forces, love, peace and justice. The world overthrew the genocidal regime and achieved a historic victory on January 7, 1979, which the Cambodian people dubbed "its second birthday".
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that in order to fully achieve the process of seeking peace and national unity in Cambodia, Samdech has successfully launched and led the implementation of a win-win policy that has brought complete peace and national unity and territorial unity. At the end of 1998. The victories of the victorious politics put an end to the wars, national divisions and territorial divisions that Cambodia went through over the last 500 years of its history.
