According to the launch, the Ministry of Environment, the seventh mandate, under the leadership of Dr. Eang Sophalleth, has officially launched the "Environmental Chakra Strategy 2023-2028" with three main angles: clean, sustainable and green.
The Environmental Chakra Strategy 2023-2028 is designed to turn the potential of the environmental sector into real benefits for the nation and the people of Cambodia of all generations. The environmental chakra strategy focuses on three major driving forces: first: policy, second: digital administration, and third: outreach, which is the driving force behind Cambodia's ships towards achieving Cambodia's vision of 2050: clean, green. And sustainability.
The Environmental Chakra Strategy 2023-2028 will be used as a roadmap to implement the priority goals, provide public services to meet the needs of the public and turn the potential of the environmental sector into the best interests to serve all generations of Cambodians and contribute. Respond to global climate change.
By launching this chakra strategy, it will further promote a cleaner Cambodia for all generations, no plastic, advanced cities, people with a high level of concern for the environment, especially Cambodia has joined the international community for greater environmental work.
