The Cambodian People's Party, together with the Cambodian people throughout the country, considered January 7, 1979, the day of the historic victory of the Cambodian people who overthrew the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, ending the darkest period in Cambodia. And killed nearly 3 million Cambodians. January 7, 1979 marked the reopening of a new era of independence, freedom, democracy and social progress.
The leader of the Cambodian People's Party, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, a man who sacrificed everything for the motherland of Cambodia, has always emphasized that the celebration of the January 7 Victory Day is an expression of the memory of the great merits of the heroic cadres and fighters of the Front. The Kampuchean National Salvation Unity and the Vietnamese Volunteer Army, who made great sacrifices in the fight to overthrow the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and defend the Cambodian revival.
People all over the country, especially in Phnom Penh, expect that the liberation of the country from General Lon Nol by the Khmer Rouge will end the war, bring peace and development to the country. Expectations were dashed after the new regime introduced a policy of evicting Cambodians from Phnom Penh and other towns to live and farm in areas in the Sre Chamkar district.
People are forced to live and work in groups, in rural cooperatives and forced to eat and sleep together, as well as forced to work overtime and malnourished. Nearly 3 million Cambodians have died. A large number of them were killed on charges of being traitors.
The suffering of the people in the black shirt regime ended after the patriotic forces of the Cambodian brave fighters united to form the United Front for National Salvation on December 2, 1978, with the support of the Vietnamese army. Completely occupied the country from Pol Pot on January 7, 1979.
Starting from this victory, Cambodia had the opportunity to move and step forward until the beginning of peace talks between Samdech Preah Mok Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Through negotiations under the auspices of Indonesia and France, a peace agreement was reached between all Cambodians in conflict (the Cambodian state government and the Tripartite Army Movement) on October 23, 1991.
After the end of the war, Cambodia fully developed the country and made progress. Currently, under the shadow of peace, Cambodia has gained more trade and foreign investment. Prior to the Kovid 19 pandemic, Cambodia maintained an economic growth rate of around 7%. In addition, many national achievements are highlighted with joy and pride.
