The garbage pit is 80 meters wide, 170 meters long and 2 meters deep, which is 1.36 hectares. According to the plan, the pit will be filled to a height of 10 meters from the mouth of the pit can hold about 97,886 cubic meters of garbage and is scheduled to be used for 20 years for about 36,478 people in the area. Including Kampong Thom province.
Chinese authorities launch probe into EU wine imports
SHANGHING (Reuters) - China on Friday launched an anti-dumping investigation into brandy imported from the European Union, a move seen as aimed primarily at France. Will increase the tension with this block. According to Reuters.
The investigation, announced by China's Ministry of Commerce, will focus on brandy stocked in less than 200 liters imported from the European Union.
Reuters reports that the Chinese Ministry of Commerce has launched an investigation into a complaint by the Chinese Alcohol Association as a local brandy.
China will import 1.57 billion US dollars worth of Spirits wine by 2023 as of November, with France accounting for the most part, according to data released by the Chinese Customs. 99.8% of all European brandy exports
Trade tensions between China and Europe have been rising over the past year, with both sides accusing each other of unfair competition and creating protectionism. The European Union (EU) said in December that it would launch an anti-dumping investigation into biodiesel imports from China.
He said Beijing's actions against European brands were "counter-counter" in response to what he described as a European attack on China's electric car sector.
Fearing that Caesar's influence would increase, the Senate ordered Caesar to lay down his arms. But Caesar disobeyed the Senate, and he was well aware of the consequences of his disobedience. He knew very well that a civil war would break out between him and Rome, led by the strongest enemy and his former ally. If he chooses to cross the Rubik's Cone, it will be irreversible.
After winning this civil war, Caesar came to power and began the Roman Empire.
Crossing the Rubikone River by Caesar became a theory for use in warfare and international relations. Rubikon's theory is one of the few theories used by the US military. This theory is incorporated into military science, taught at universities, and incorporated into military regulations.
The purpose of studying this theory is to better understand the intentions of the enemy and to avoid any provocative actions without triggering a response that leads to irreversibility.
Action phase
Scholars have analyzed the form of action of Rubikon's theory, trying to answer the following questions:
1. Pre-planning potential outcomes that are positive and negative on desires and action choices (pre-decision stages).
2: The stage of planning a clear strategy to reach the goals achieved at the end of the decision-making phase (the stage before the action or after the decision).
3: The stage of adopting the prepared strategy (action phase).
4: And finally is the stage of evaluating the results of activities (stages after activities).
I. Stages before decision making
Finally, one has to weigh one's desires and possibilities over many of them. The purpose of this initial stage is to decide which of its aspirations to capture based on the possible categories (i.e. the hope of the outcome of the desired action is successful) and Satisfaction (meaning the value of the result of the expected action).
The process of this project increases the commitment to a specific goal in the Rubikon crossing between desire and goal. The transition from desire to specific goal creates a strong sense of commitment to translate the goal into action.
II. Stage before action or after decision
The word "will" here indicates that the motivation for the design of the objective, the potential action (desire) is determined by going through the Rubikon and that the individual is committed to achieving the goal achieved. Select. Therefore, at this stage, it is no longer a matter of choosing a satisfactory and possible goal, but it is a stage that determines how to achieve the chosen goal.
In short, the stage before the action, everyone thinks of the best way to proceed to the goal they have achieved in the end before the decision. They choose strategies and create plans that can achieve the desired goals.
IV. Stages after activities
At this stage, the individual evaluates the outcome of the action achieved. If satisfied with the results achieved, the set goals are kept at the end of the stage before the decision is made. And if he is not satisfied with the result, he will lower the expectation level and keep the goal the same, or keep the expectation level and increase the effort to achieve the desired goal.
The case of the journey to the National Rescue on January 7, 1979 in accordance with the definition
An analysis of events linked to theory is taken from the documentary Journey to National Salvation, January 7, 1979.
The pre-decision stage, according to the Rubikon's model of time, in this early stage is determined by the planning that arises from the desire, the motivation.
What are the motivating factors that make the journey towards national salvation?
The most important motivation is to see the massacre of the people and the brutal atrocities of the Communist Party of Kampuchea on the people themselves, if not die from the purge, die of starvation, overwork.
In 1977, seeing the country in danger, Hun Sen had the first choice to stand up to fight the uprising against Pol Pot. But if they stand up to attack Memot and Snuol districts with a force of about 2,000 men to take the base, such a struggle will not last more than a month, which will die in a pool of blood due to the Pol Pot crackdown.
Many questions have been raised as to whether Hun Sen was killed by a landmine while crossing the border, or by Vietnamese border guards, and whether Vietnam will deport him back to Cambodia.
With only one good option, on June 20, 1977, Samdech Hun Sen decided to cross the border (across the Rubikon) into Vietnam, using his life as a capital in the national liberation struggle to save the Cambodian people.
Stage before action or after decision
After the interrogation, Hun Sen met with the Vietnamese leader to explain the situation in Cambodia and ask for help (plan). But the first proposal was rejected by Vietnam because it thought it would interfere in Cambodia's internal affairs.
The Khmer Rouge's attack on Vietnam changed Vietnam's position in providing aid to Hun Sen. Which, of course, made the video an overnight sensation.
