In November 2023, Chinese officials launched an investigation into suspected "illegal" crimes against the company, following reports that ZEG had declared bankruptcy.
The troubled company reportedly told its investors in a letter in November that its debt of up to $ 64 billion was more than the company's estimated assets. About $ 38 billion.
"ZEG's assets are insufficient to repay all its debts and it is clear that the company lacks capacity," a Beijing court reported on Friday in a statement on WeChat. In full repayment of debt.
Informal lending has always existed in China's economy, but shadow banking only began to emerge after the global financial crisis in 2008, when credit was scarce.
China's shadow banking industry is worth about $ 3 trillion. The industry often finances China's once-booming real estate sector, which has now been hit hard by the credit crunch, with some large real estate companies now on the brink of collapse due to a lack of finance.
According to the BBC, at the height of its growth, asset management companies under ZEG owned more than one trillion yuan ($ 139 billion) in assets.
