(Iran) - Iranian mourners on Friday shouted and shed tears over the coffins of the victims of two deadly bombings in Iran on Wednesday, the interior minister said. A number of suspects have been arrested in connection with attacks claimed by Islamic State. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on January 5, 2024.
Crowds chanted "Revenge, Revenge" in a state television video of a funeral in Kerman, the scene of Wednesday's deadliest attack in Iran since the 1979 Islamic Revolution.
The attack comes amid regional tensions as Israel's war against Hamas in the Gaza Strip nears three months.
Interior Minister Ahmad Vahidi told Iranian state television that some suspects had been arrested. "Our country's competent intelligence agencies have found good clues regarding the elements involved in the Kerman bombings and some of the people involved in the incident have been identified," he said without elaborating. Arrested.
