(Phnom Penh): Dr. Neth Savoeun, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, on the afternoon of January 5, 2024, instructed the inter-ministerial working group to control drugs and chemical compounds to prepare SOP standards. (Standard operating procedures) To control the import of all kinds of chemicals, especially substances that can be processed into drugs.
Ket Sophan, spokesman for the National Authority for Combating Drugs, told reporters at the end of the meeting that Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun's instructions to the inter-ministerial working group were aimed at strengthening drug control mechanisms. All of those chemicals are being smuggled into Cambodia by criminals.
He added that during the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun emphasized that the preparation of the SOP standard should be simple and effective to manage, but not to complicate the companies that import chemicals to bring. Serve their needs, especially in industry, health, mining and other related fields.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun, the relevant ministries and institutions must also set up mechanisms for their internal use, in order to effectively control the use of chemicals and prevent The chemical falls into the hands of criminals, who create an environment for them to steal and process drugs.
He added that the working group is responsible for the National Authority for Combating Drugs on the control of drugs and chemicals used in legal activities in the fields of health, industry, agriculture, mining and energy to prevent and avoid. Theft of this chemical to be used in illegal activities.
Meanwhile, a spokesman for the National Authority for Combating Drugs said that the meeting, chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun, outlined a number of key inputs for the SOP standard. The meeting also agreed that the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs will compile a list of chemicals that can be processed into drugs and send them to the relevant ministries and institutions.
Please be informed that according to the decision of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia on December 15, 2023 on the establishment of the Inter-Ministerial Working Group on Drug and Drug Control, this working group has a senior minister. Sokha, Permanent Vice President of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, chaired by 6 Vice-Chairmen and 10 members.
