Subsequent storms in recent weeks have brought prolonged rains to saturated soils and caused swollen rivers and waterways to erupt across shores across England and Wales. The storm has also caused flooding in other parts of Europe in recent days.
The Trent River in central England has flooded, prompting local authorities to declare a major incident. The London Fire Brigade said it had taken about 50 people to safety Thursday evening after a canal in the eastern part of the capital overflowed.
