(Phnom Penh): Dr. Neth Savoeun, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, chaired a meeting on January 5, 2024 to disseminate and announce the composition of the inter-ministerial working group on drug and substance control. Chemicals, drugs. The meeting was held at the Friendship Building of the Office of the Council of Ministers.
Pursuant to the decision of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on December 15, 2023 on the establishment of the Inter-Ministerial Working Group on Drug and Narcotics Control, it was determined that this working group consists of Senior Minister Prum Sokha, Deputy Chairman. The National Anti-Drug Authority is chaired by 6 Vice-Chairmen and 10 members.
This inter-ministerial working group has the following responsibilities:
Collect information related to the import, export, transportation, storage, consumption and inventory of substances used in the sector as stated in Article 2 of this Decision.
* Control the trafficking, storage, storage of drugs, chemicals and chemicals related to the production of illegal drugs to prevent the illegal use and diversion from the legal trade to the production of illegal drugs.
