The Philippines remains open to diplomatic talks with China and believes the two countries can reach a solution to the dispute in the South China Sea, the Philippine National Security Adviser said on Friday. Period of peaceful conversation. This was released by Reuters on Friday, January 5, 2023.
The comments by Philippine National Security Adviser Eduardo Ano came after the Chinese Foreign Ministry on Thursday condemned a joint US-Philippine joint patrol operation in the South China Sea. Provocative and irresponsible.
Responding to Chinese criticism, Ano said: "Patrol operations with the United States and possible future actions with our other allies demonstrate our shared commitment to security and order. "International law and aims to promote peace as well as stability in the region as a whole."
"The Philippines still welcomes diplomatic talks with China and is committed to building good relations with all countries," he said. "We believe that through peaceful dialogue and respect for international law, we will be able to achieve solutions that best serve the interests of all parties involved in the region."
