Social Analysts: The close relationship between the Ministry of Labor and unions of all perspectives is a sign of harmonization of the labor sector in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Analysts see the closeness between the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and local unions as a sign of working together to address labor issues rather than attacking each other through reports. And activities that indirectly and directly affect employment harmonization in Cambodia.
The remarks came after it was seen that the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training held frequent meetings with unions of all walks of life in Cambodia to discuss work and put issues on the table for a common solution.
This is why Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the rapprochement between the unions and the Royal Government is a good sign because there is nothing better than putting issues on the table and discussing. Find a solution, especially if both parties aim to protect the rights and interests of workers alike.
Dr. added: "This should be done from the beginning, but it is too late, it is important now we should have such a mechanism to solve problems and protect the rights of Cambodians. "Putting microphones on, using violence, issuing excessive reports is not a good solution."
In particular, Dr. Yong Pov urged that both unions and the government, which are all protectors of the interests of the same workers, can work together smoothly and establish a mechanism to work together instead of using other platforms to attack each other. All have negative effects and results on the work sector, speaking separately and society as a whole.
In particular, Dr. Chheng Kimlong, President of the Asian Vision Institute, said that the close relationship between unions and the Royal Government is a good thing for the sustainability of the labor sector in Cambodia, which unions and the Royal Government have always been in conflict with each other in the past. .
He added that this is the right thing to do and there is a mechanism to solve common problems, rather than acting against each other, which leads to damage to the overall national interest, especially affecting workers who are working in industrial plants, which is Pillar income for their families.
"Especially in a situation where the economy is in trouble like now, the issuance of union reports to the outside world needs to be done with caution, which could hurt the national economy and investors," he said. In this sense, our nation is damaged and we all lose.
This is because he has seen that some unions in Cambodia often make critical reports about the situation of workers in Cambodia, which does not reflect the real situation. According to Dr., unions should implement the spirit of the Union Law, which stipulates that unions promote harmony in industrial relations and contribute to the development of decent work, increase productivity and further investment in the protection of workers' rights.
"If you are not careful, it will hit the big pot and affect the investment," he said. "In this situation, foreign countries are more orderly than we are. Business people are fleeing to those countries because those countries have a stable control over workers and they are safer."
