Today is the 48th anniversary of the marriage of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, organized by the Khmer Rouge
A wedding under a black shirt regime is a lavish wedding, no traditional dress, no Bai Khon Chong Chai music, no Preah Thong music, no veil, no relatives and no friends. In other words, the wedding dress is only black and only the organization is a witness of this wedding.
After the wedding, there is no honeymoon or a trip to a resort like the couple today. After the wedding, there were no gatherings to eat and celebrate. About 28 hours after the wedding, the couple had dinner prepared by the people.
The honeymoon of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit took place on a house provided by the organization. In the dormitory house organized by the organization, two pairs are to sleep, the 12th and the 13th, which are Samdech and Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
Many Cambodian couples were organized and matched by the Khmer Rouge even though they did not love each other. After the Khmer Rouge regime broke up on January 7, 1979, some couples asked to be separated.
Separately, the love of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, which was born from the heart and has a lot of bitter history, is still immortal. Marriage during the war, the two princes had six children, one of whom died shortly after leaving the womb, "Hun Komsat."
Inheritance of this sincere love, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit now have 5 children (3 boys, 2 girls) and 22 grandchildren (12 boys, 10 girls). The 22nd grandson was born on January 3, 2021. The 22nd grandson is the daughter of Lt. Gen. Dy Vichea and Ms. Hun Mana, Director General of Bayon Radio and Television.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has emphasized that no matter how sad the marriage is, as long as the marriage is maintained, it will be stable and happy forever.
I received the news in the morning, in the afternoon I met Brother Sok Saroeun, my commander insisted that he take me to Krouch Chhmar district that evening. Understanding the low-ranking officer who helped him a lot on the job, and perhaps he was also finding the heart and relatives of a woman he loved, Sok Saroeun decided immediately and left immediately, which he and I initially thought Will be back all night.
That night, I became a liar by telling my commander that our motorcycles, engines, and batteries were not working properly, and that traveling all night could damage the road. Sometimes it was almost ten o'clock at night, and my commander agreed, asking the director of the hospital for an overnight stay.
The sky is not clear yet, I hear the sound of rice hitting, I try to see Rany and his friend Khemara is threshing rice. My commander told me to get my motorbike ready to leave early in the morning. I only wished for the broken motorcycle to talk to Rany, but it was not our intention, just kicked the motorcycle on fire immediately.
The fact that I love Rany is real and whether Rany loves me or not is a matter to be solved. Falling in love with a girl for the first time in my life, however, I have not forgotten my role and responsibilities.
April 13, 1974 is the Khmer New Year. I took the time to visit Krouch Chhmar district in order to visit Rany under the pretext of visiting the soldiers who were being treated at the hospital. When he arrived at the hospital, he did not see Rany and did not dare to ask. I rode the motorcycle out of the hospital, all hope. We had to continue our journey to Roka Khnor commune to bring a friend of mine to visit his parents in his hometown.
When I was traveling for about 2 km, I met Rany riding a bicycle alone on the road, I stopped my motorcycle, Rany stopped the bike. We greeted each other with polite words for about three minutes and then said goodbye to our respective routes. Neither Rany nor I did show any signs that were different from what we had known before.
In August 1974, I had to get to know both of my leaders on both sides of Rany, as I proposed to Rany. The answer I received from my commander was yes, but I have to wait for the country to be liberated from the Lon Nol regime. The answer from Rany is according to his spokesperson that it is up to the parents. These two answers are very encouraging for me. 98% of Cambodian women who answer that it is up to their parents or elders means yes.
From then until I became disabled, I never met Rany again, despite the opportunity. On January 1, 1975, I suffered my fourth shoulder injury. At that time, I thought that Rany would take care of my wounds. On the contrary, the front battle hospital prepared to remove the shrapnel and continue treatment at the hospital located in Boeung Proul commune, Peam Chi Liang district.
On the morning of April 16, 1975, I was seriously injured and fainted until April 21, when I regained consciousness. When I woke up, my left eye was blind and my right eye was only about 10 meters long. At that time, I also learned that Phnom Penh and the country as a whole were liberated from the American occupation. The words love and care are like lenses for me, I can no longer speak because I have already lost my lenses.
I have to try again for Rany and me and Rany's parents, there are no obstacles. But the organization is the real obstacle. At that time, Rany was forced by the organization to marry another man, but she flatly refused. As for me, I was also reunited with other women, but I also refused. I have to propose to Rany again to the regional military chief. At that time, the local military chief wrote a letter for me to take to the Krouch Chhmar district committee.
During October 1975, both the region and the district, Rany, who was their spouse, agreed and only waited for the wedding day. Both before and while waiting, Rany and I had a difficult time. Refusing to marry according to the organization's arrangements can be life threatening. As for me, in addition to treating injuries, my main job is to organize secret forces to attack organizations that have been killing people, even though it was not serious at the time.
On the evening of January 4, 1976, I had to leave with a group from the regional department in Tambor district to Chrap village in Tbong Khmum district, where I was to get married. On January 5, 1976, the 4th day of the 4th lunar month, the year of Rong, the Buddhist era 2519, the day my wife and I married 12 other couples, of which my wife and I were the 13th. At around 8:00 am, the ceremony started with one presidency and one organizing committee.
The program began after reading the resume, to the program where the presidency asked the bride and groom questions to answer one by one, asking the bride first and then the groom. 12 pairs finished my turn, I was the 13th pair, Rany answered both questions well. Out of the previous 12 pairs, only one question is up to Rany 2 questions. As for me, I have up to 3 questions.
After questioning the 26 stakeholders, the presidency asked the invited elders, who were called witnesses. Two elders spoke, including Brother Chum Hul, my former commander, using the appropriate words and wishing us well. (Mr. Chum Hul after 1979 as Governor of Sihanoukville until 1993, then retired and died in 2014).
At around 4:00 pm, we ate together, the couple and guests, sitting on the skin. Rany has officially become my wife, but I still do not dare to talk to her. When Bai Rany cooked rice for me and helped cook rice for another disabled soldier because his wife was shy.
I waited for my wife but could not find her because she was still talking to the landlord where she was staying last night. I took a shower first and prepared a place to rest. Now I have taken off my black clothes and put on my army uniform. Please note that during the ceremony, the groom is required to wear black pants and a long-sleeved shirt, while the bride is required to wear a black skirt and a long-sleeved shirt.
Today's actions of the organization are also another important part that motivates me to struggle to overthrow this non-traditional and secular regime. Today it's talking about clearing the internal siren embedded, it's right, because I am the master of this embedded. Speaking of my wife, I feel sorry for her, she should not have to work with a disabled person like me, get married without her parents and relatives.
Compassion made me understand more clearly that she accepted me wholeheartedly and did not discriminate against people with disabilities. After a good night's sleep on January 5, 1976, in the morning, the local military department took a tuk-tuk to take us back to the unit.
The section of National Road 7 at that time was almost completely damaged and could not travel fast. We left the market less than 10 kilometers, the wheel or the left side of the truck leaked, but we can still inflate the air to travel. Initially, one compressor can travel about 1 km in a row, the compressor no longer enters.
At night, the owner arranged for us to sleep, male by male, female by female, I asked the landlord to sleep with my wife, and heam with his wife, but the landlord responded with an apology for fear of nephews kidnapping, not husband and wife. Exactly. We had no choice but to accept the landlord's arrangements so that he would not be bothered by us.
