Deputy Prime Minister Hang Chuon Naron: The Khmer Law Trial Forum is an open forum discussion focusing on the tradition of discussing the law.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, stated that the forum on Khmer legal tradition is an opportunity for presentation and discussion in an open framework, focusing on traditions, methods and practices. There have been changes in the past, and there have been changes in the way the church is judged.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron said this on January 4, 2024, on the occasion of closing the forum on Khmer legal tradition held at the Royal School of Administration with the participation of Mr. Youk Bunna, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Public Works and Director of the Royal School of Administration, Mr. Hel Chamroeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, including expert speakers, students, senior officials and officials of the Royal School of Administration.
According to Youk Bunna, the Khmer Law Tribunal was organized to achieve two main objectives: to present the existence of legal identity and the concept of ancient Khmer law, and to link the evolution of customary law to modern law. French law since the drafting of the first Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia in 1947.
Mr. Youk Bunna stated that this forum on Khmer Law Tribunal is a forum for presentation and discussion in an open framework with the participation of inter-ministerial and relevant institutions based on the one-player system approach aimed at building and strengthening The culture of the rule of law upholds four core values, including legal values, cultural values, historical values and educational values.
Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Inspects Field Team Officials and Accelerates Systematic Land Registration for Citizens
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on the morning of January 4, 2024, led the officials of the relevant units to inspect the field team to expedite the systematic land registration for the people in Stung Trang district.
The provincial governor said that the systematic land registration for the people of Kampong Cham province is committed to be completed by the middle of 2024 to become a model province, the first of the 25 provinces to complete this work. - Province.
The provincial governor stated that despite some challenges in the systematic land registration process, our field team officials have made a joint commitment to achieve the plan planned by Kampong Cham province. The total number to be registered is about 920,000 plots.
But so far, professional officers have completed about 810,000 plots, so there are only about 110,000 plots left, which our officials have to work to complete this work by mid-2024.
In addition to speeding up the land registration process, the provincial governor has instructed the local authorities to facilitate the preparation of relevant documents for the people. For the people, please help spread the word to prepare enough documents and clear demarcation for our officials to measure quickly.
