Speaking on that occasion, Lt. Gen. Lor Soleng fully agreed and supported the report of the General Department of Internal Audit, which reported on the audit process and results of the General Commission of the National Police to the ceremony.
He thanked the Internal Audit Team and the Heads of Departments, Departments under the General Commission of the National Police, who were the subject of the audit, for their close and active participation in facilitating mutual assistance in order to find positive and negative points. Which may occur during the performance of duties in maintaining the security and social order of the General Commission of the National Police.
Lt. Gen. Lor Soleng further stated that the management of the force and some immediate tasks require flexible, lively and authoritative leadership on the eventual event, which causes these shortcomings. And the challenge of justification and self-determination in commanding forces. All of these points can cause some gaps for the specialized department.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Nguon Sreng commended the heads of departments, units and departments in each field for their good cooperation in providing documents and providing time for successful audits. He said that in the report, there are some points that are not enough and exaggerated by some points, so the director of the department can complain to improve in the coming years.
