The Ministry of National Defense is determined not to allow soldiers to use drugs, the case will be severely punished and removed from the framework
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia has decided not to allow any soldiers in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to use drugs. This was confirmed by a spokesman for the Ministry of National Defense.
This commitment was made at a meeting to review the work results for 2023 and set the direction for 2024 of the Anti-Drug Committee of the Ministry of National Defense, chaired by Mr. Chai Saing Yun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense and Chairman of the Committee Anti-drug of the Ministry of National Defense this morning, January 4, 2024.
According to General Chhum Socheat, the meeting reviewed the report on past activities, including: education, dissemination of the law on drug control, regular crime suppression work of units under the Ministry of National Defense, especially the Gendarmerie, rehabilitation treatment. Rehabilitation, drug testing, including vocational training and so on.
On that occasion, the Chairman of the Meeting disseminated the Instruction No. 007 of the Ministry of National Defense on Drug Prevention Measures in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, emphasizing the three strict measures of Mr. Tea Seiha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense on December 29, 2023, which are as follows:
1: Develop an action plan to prevent officers, deputies and soldiers from being involved in the cultivation, production, trafficking, trafficking in drugs and chemicals as prescribed by law and to prevent law enforcement from committing crimes. Drugs, even relatives.
2. Develop an action plan to mainstream education to raise awareness of the problems and effects of drugs to officers, deputies and soldiers of all units in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
3. Regularly inspect drugs in all units of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. In the event that officers, deputies and soldiers are found to have used or been involved in drugs, their names shall be removed from the framework of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
This instruction of the Ministry of National Defense is strictly in accordance with the high recommendation of His Majesty the King Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia in the closing ceremony of the 2023 work review meeting and the 2024 work direction of the Ministry of Environment on December 21, 2023 ago.
