The governor said that Kampot is a province with many potentials that serve the interests of the people in the province, especially tourism, which currently has nearly 40 tourist sites, so we must jointly promote and jointly create, process and develop. The Minister of Inspection, Mr. Huot Hak, pointed out the differences between the National Audit Authority, the Anti-Corruption Unit and the Ministry of Inspection.
(Phnom Penh): Due to the misunderstanding that the National Audit Authority, the Anti-Corruption Unit and the Ministry of Inspection have overlapping jurisdiction, Mr. Huot Hak, Minister of Inspection, pointed out the different jurisdictions between the above three units / institutions in order to prevent the public from There is more confusion.
The Minister made a presentation on the differences between the three units / institutions by the Minister on the morning of January 4, 2024, while the Club of Cambodian Journalists (CCJ) in collaboration with the Ministry of Inspection organized a discussion forum at the Ministry's office. "Inspection in the context of reform" with the participation of Mr. Puy Kea, President of the Club, Ministry officials, as well as many journalists.
The differences that Mr. Huot Hak mentioned include:
* The National Audit Authority is an independent institution.
The Anti-Corruption Unit has the right to summon and arrest anyone found guilty. The Anti-Corruption Unit also has the right to release you if you are arrested but not found guilty.
* The Ministry of Inspection has the authority to inspect and research at institutions, both good and bad. If the institution is found to be good, the Ministry will help to disseminate it as a model, but if the inspection is wrong, the Ministry of Inspection will continue the procedure. If the procedure is minor, the institution will be instructed, educated and corrected, but if it is serious, it must be thoroughly researched and reported to the Prime Minister to take action.
However, according to Huot Hak, the National Audit Authority, the Anti-Corruption Unit and the Ministry of Inspection have a common mission: to jointly prevent and take measures to combat corruption, abuse of power and inactivity.
"This work is to contribute to the Royal Government in the successful implementation of the Royal Government's political program, as well as the Pentagon strategy." This is the additional confirmation of the Minister.
Please be informed that on October 5, 2023, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, issued a Royal Kram promulgating the Law on the Establishment of the "Ministry of Inspection", which was renamed from the Ministry of National Assembly Relations. The Senate and the inspection are after the Royal Government of the 7th mandate. Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Information Department instructs officials to increase work efficiency and jointly improve the information sector
