(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on Wednesday night, January 3, 2024 issued a statement stating that Cambodia does not yet have an agreement on sending workers from Cambodia to work in Israel. The announcement comes after the illegal recruitment of workers to Israel via telegram.
"To prevent fraud by the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, we are honored to inform the public that Cambodia does not yet have an SPIP agreement to send workers from Cambodia to work," the ministry said in a statement. "In Israel, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training is currently working with the Israeli side to discuss a draft memorandum of understanding on recruitment and deployment."
According to the same letter, the Ministry has announced that it will take legal action in case any citizen sees or advertises the recruitment of workers to work in Israel in any form.
For the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, the illegal recruitment and sending of workers abroad is a crime of human trafficking.
However, the Ministry of Labor will notify the public in the event of an official agreement to send workers to work in Israel in the near future. Former member of the Board of Directors of the former CNRP proposes to join the political life with the Cambodian People's Party
