Russian state-owned Alrosa, which owns more than 90 percent of Russia's diamond production, provides the Kremlin a valuable source of revenue.
The European Union (EU) said on Wednesday that Alrosa and its executives had been placed on a list of individuals and entities sanctioned for "acts that undermine or threaten Ukraine's territorial integrity, sovereignty and independence." "Companies are an important part of the economy and provide a lot of revenue to the Russian government," the report added.
Since Russia sent troops to Ukraine in February 2022, about 1,950 Russian companies and individuals have been subject to EU sanctions, according to Reuters. Amid Economic Concerns and Conflicts in the Red Sea
SINGAPORE: Oil prices stabilized in Asian markets on Wednesday morning after falling sharply earlier this week as markets weighed on concerns over the US economy and supply disruptions caused by tense tensions. Continuing in the Red Sea. According to Reuters.
Crude prices rose about $ 2 earlier this week after attacks on ships in the Red Sea by Houthi rebels last weekend and the arrival of an Iranian warship on Monday. Escalating conflicts could close the Red Sea, a major waterway for oil transportation, and disrupt trade flows.
However, crude oil markets fell in the previous trading session as market optimism about US interest rate cuts came ahead of the release of the US Federal Reserve and US jobs data. .
Analysts from ING wrote in a note to clients: "The energy market can not escape the greater pressure that is expected to occur on risky assets, while the stock market. Fall in price. "The fall in oil prices comes despite rising tensions in the Middle East."
Vietnamese Ambassador wants to see Cambodians invest in Vietnam
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Nguyen Huy Taing, Vietnamese Ambassador to Cambodia, expressed his desire to see Cambodian investors invest in Vietnam.
This intention was expressed on the occasion of the Ambassador's courtesy call and discussion with Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia on the afternoon of January 3, 2024.
During the meeting, the two sides discussed the purpose of promoting investment and trade, as well as discussing arrangements for Cambodian and Vietnamese investors to meet to discuss work and explore potential for investment in the two countries.
The Vietnamese Ambassador congratulated Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol on his appointment as First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia. The ambassador expressed hope that the two countries would be able to further boost investment and trade between them. The ambassador also expressed the desire for Cambodian investors to invest in Vietnam.
Ta Prohm villagers in Prek Eang commune urge Chbar Ampov district authorities to dismantle illegal rooster farms, causing noise and foul smell in violation of the authorities' decision
(Phnom Penh): Residents of Ta Prohm Village, Sangkat Prek Eang, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh, have urged the Chbar Ampov District Authority to close and dismantle an unlicensed rooster farm that still causes noise and stench to the surrounding residents. According to the decision of the authorities after 30 days from November 21, 2023 to dismantle, but the owner of the farm did not comply.
The people's representative told Fresh News on January 3, 2024 that after the people filed a complaint and inspected the farm location of the authorities, on November 21, 2023, the authorities decided to set a time. 30 days for the owner of this illegal rooster farm to completely dismantle it. In case of exceeding this limit, the district administration will take action to dismantle without any loss or damage.
