(Kampong Speu): Kampong Speu Provincial Administration has submitted a plan to civil servants under the auspices of the Royal Government to participate in the implementation of various reform programs of the Royal Government, especially the three core reform programs: public administration reform, public financial management reform and decentralization reform. Decentralization.
This emphasis was made at the opening of the meeting to review the work of 2023 and work direction 2024 of Kampong Speu Provincial Administration for 2 days on the morning of January 4, 2024, chaired by Mr. Yim Sokhom, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Vy. Samnang, the governor of Kampong Speu province, as well as more than 600 units around the provincial administration.
Mr. Vy Samnang said that the provincial administration focuses on attracting local and foreign investors to invest in the province to create jobs for people in the province to have high-income jobs and decent living conditions, strengthen public service delivery. Citizens to be more efficient and timely.
The provincial governor emphasized the support for public administration reform, and the provincial administration has made efforts to strengthen and continuously improve the quality and efficiency of public services, including the provision of administrative services to the people, and support for the reform of civil servants. Appointment, promotion, management, presence and performance of officials at all levels in each department.
In addition, support for the roles and responsibilities in the structure of the municipal administration after the integration of specialized offices around the municipality / district to the municipal / district administration to improve and strengthen the work efficiency in the institution.
In addition, the provincial administration held a forum to disseminate and consult with the provincial council in the third mandate throughout the nine cities / districts, collecting challenges and concerns of local people to solve in a timely manner.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Aphisandit Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, has issued a proclamation to determine the mandate of the Chief and Deputy Chief of Police of the International Border Gate and the International Gate of the General Department of Immigration.
* Chief and Deputy Chief of Police, International Border Gate and International Gate, served for 4 (four) years
* The officers and deputy chiefs of the gate police station who have completed their term shall be appointed to a new position or appointed as the chief or deputy chief of another gate police station for the next term.
The same proclamation states that the number of deputy police chiefs at international border checkpoints and international checkpoints that exceed the limit set forth in the above two articles shall be retained.
In the event that the position is vacant due to retirement or transfer or other reasons, it shall not be replenished until the number is below the limit as stated in Article 2 of this Prakas.
