(Pursat): Pursat Provincial Administration on January 3, 2024 issued a directive on the suspension of rice cultivation in the second dry season, while the cultivation of our farmers has increased to 46,341 hectares. Exceeded water consumption plan by 26,341 hectares.
In this regard, the provincial administration would like to recommend to all farmers in the province who are growing rice in the dry season 2024 as follows:
All farmers are asked to suspend the cultivation of rice for the second time after the harvest is completed during January to May 2024.
2. People throughout the province must be prepared to store water in ponds, wells and canals that can store water for daily use and livestock.
3. In case the farmers still do not accept the instructions of the provincial administration, the provincial administration is not responsible for the lack of water to irrigate rice crops in the dry season.
4- If our farmers continue to grow rice in the dry season for the second time, you will be able to face the lack of water for daily use, lack of water for livestock and the loss of farmers' budget.
