Minister Tho Chetha Inspects the Progress of Irrigation Project in Svay Rieng Province
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, on January 3, 2024, inspected the progress of irrigation construction project in Svay Rieng province.
The Minister, together with Mr. Peng Pursa, Governor of Svay Rieng Province, and technical officers of the Ministry and the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Svay Rieng Province inspected the Daun Toay Irrigation System in Sangkat Prey Angkunh, Bavet City and Prey Koki Commune, Chantrea District, Svay Rieng Province.
Please be informed that Dauntoy Irrigation System was repaired and restored in 2011 by the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology with a volume of 17 million cubic meters, with a total irrigated area of 7,239 hectares, including 6049 hectares of wet paddy and 1,190 hectares of dry paddy. Hectares.
On the same day, the Minister together with the technical leaders of the Ministry and the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Svay Rieng Province also inspected the progress of the project to develop the Vaiko Irrigation System Phase 2 (Kampong Chrey Reservoir) in Svay Chrum District, Svay Rieng Province.
Please note that the construction work to be carried out in this second step includes: 1) Digging 2 canals with a total length of 14.6 km 2) Construction of 4 main canals with a total length of 59.5 km 3) Construction 41.5 km of delta dams; 4) construction of 1 spillway construction site, 6 dams and 8 drainage facilities, and 5) construction of 4 pumping stations and 32 drainage structures.
At the same time, the Minister expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the progress made and further instructed the Director of the Department and the Technical Working Group to continue good cooperation with local authorities and all stakeholders. To make this project successful, high quality and durable to serve the lives of local people.
