Minister of Women's Affairs: Ariana is a hospital created by Cambodian children but has international standards that will help reduce the number of people seeking treatment abroad (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): From now on, the leadership and all government officials Of the Ministry of Women's Affairs will not only receive quality health services, but will also receive affordable prices from Ariana International Hospital.
This announcement was made at the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding between Arinda International Hospital and the Ministry of Women's Affairs, which was presided over by Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, and Ms. Oknha Koun Thida, Chairman of the Board of Directors of International Hospital. Learn on the afternoon of January 2, 2024.
On that occasion, Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi praised Arinda International Hospital for its spacious, clean and international standard. She also revealed that she had referred many patients to the first branch of Arinda International Hospital and found that they were satisfied.
She also praised Ariana International Hospital for its good hygiene, ethical doctors and encouraged the leaders and families of officials of the Ministry of Women's Affairs to choose Arinda International Hospital to deal with any health problems. Going abroad costs a lot of money. She also added that every year, Cambodians spend tens of millions of dollars to seek health services abroad.
"I believe that Arinda International Hospital will help change the minds of Cambodians to seek health care locally." This is according to the Minister.
With the goal of contributing to the strengthening of the local health sector to reduce outpatient treatment of Cambodians, Arinda International Hospital has carefully considered its reasonable price, adhering to the principle of "domestic price, quality, international standard". In order for the general population at all levels of living standards to have access to health services from Ariana International Hospital.
As for the vision of Arinda International Hospital, Ms. Oknha Kuon Thida showed that she is also a Cambodian citizen who sees that Cambodians have a hard time when they have health problems, they have to go abroad, that is why she set up the department. This modern and international standard doctor. At the same time, Ms. Oknha also wants to contribute to the Royal Government in improving the health sector.
Duke Kuon Thida stated: "We would like to commend Ms. Kittibandit who has taken into account the well-being and health of the leaders and civil servants of the Ministry of Women's Affairs by signing a memorandum of understanding with our hospital. This is so that the leaders and civil servants of the entire ministry can receive quality and affordable health services.
