The following is a decision by the Ministry of Economy: Thailand approves measures to reduce taxes on alcohol and nightclubs to boost tourism (Video inside) (Bangkok): A Thai government spokesman said on Tuesday that the cabinet Thailand has approved measures to reduce taxes on alcoholic beverages and entertainment venues to boost tourism. According to Reuters.
The announcement comes after Thai authorities in November 2023 extended the opening hours for entertainment venues by two hours, which will run until 4 a.m. for nightlife and tourists.
Tourism is a major driver for the Thai economy, the second largest economy in Southeast Asia. Last year, Thailand achieved 28 million tourist destinations, generating 1.2 trillion baht in revenue, according to Thai government data.
The move also partly reflects China's economic challenges, leading policymakers to formulate a series of stimulus measures last year. However, this month-long data does not provide clear evidence of a long-term change in business model.
China remains South Korea's largest trading partner due to Seoul's imports from China, the world's second-largest economy.
Although South Korea's exports to the United States increased for the fifth consecutive month from the same period in 2022, South Korea said exports to China continued. Increase as well. Meanwhile, South Korea's total imports fell 10.8 percent year on year in 2022, bringing the trade surplus to $ 4.5 billion. According to Bloomberg News.
