Stong District Governor Calls on Stong Market Traders to Cooperate with Authorities to Develop a Safe Market
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Say Kim Lam, Governor of Stong District, called on the traders of Serey Stong Market to cooperate with the authorities to develop a safe market.
He said this during the inspection of Serey Stong market in Kampong Kdei village, Kampong Chen Tbong commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province on January 2, 2024.
He appealed to all traders in the market and people living around Serey Stong Market to cooperate with the authorities and development partners to improve the quality of the market to be aesthetically pleasing and environmentally friendly, as well as to participate in improving the image of Stoung and its district. .
The Governor of Stong District instructed Koy Kimsay Company, which manages the collection of taxes and the development of Serey Stong Market, to strive to develop the market with good infrastructure, drainage system, concrete roads, quality, technical standards to ensure drainage without Congestion and so on.
Mr. Stong District Governor appealed to help preserve the beauty of the market, especially to keep garbage well, do not put in the sewer system, which causes congestion and bad smell, which leads to disturb the beauty, health and environment. Also.
At the same time, Mr. Say Kimlam advised the garbage collection company Carabao Stong to collect garbage in time to avoid congestion, which causes rot and bad smell, affecting the beauty. And the environment in the market as well as the entire Stoung district town base.
The full text of President Macron's official letter in French reads as follows:
Dear Prime Minister, Dear Friend
As the King's visit to Paris last month reaffirmed the power of friendship between our two countries and our people, I am honored to invite you to pay an official visit to France on January 18-19. Face.
This first visit to France since His Excellency took office as Prime Minister will pave the way for a number of key areas that are fundamental to the relationship between our two countries, including economics, military development, heritage and Francophonie.
I wish this visit opens up the possibility of deepening and diversifying cooperation between our two countries to jointly address the global issues we are facing, especially in the field of energy transition. This visit will allow us to examine the means by which we can work together to strengthen the rule of law in order to ensure the full sovereignty and independence of all states.
Please accept, Excellency, the assurances of my highest consideration.
On Friday, South Africa asked the International Court of Justice (ICJ) to issue an emergency order declaring that Israel was violating its obligations under the 1948 Genocide Convention in its military campaign against Hamas.
"The state of Israel will appear before the International Court of Justice in The Hague to eliminate South Africa's ridiculous insults," spokesman Elon Levy said in an online press conference. "We assure the leaders of South Africa that history will judge you and it will judge you mercilessly," he added.
The International Court of Justice (ICJ), sometimes called the World Court, is the venue of the United Nations to resolve disputes between states. The Israeli Foreign Ministry called South Africa's allegations "baseless".
