Kampong Thom Cross Branch Donates to 3 Families Affected by Fire in Sandan District
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Chea Van Chan, Deputy Governor and Secretary of the Kampong Thom Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross; Three families were affected by fire.
The fire occurred on the night of January 1, 2024, caused by a stove fire in Khmer village, Ngon commune, Sandan district, Kampong Thom province on the afternoon of January 2, 2024.
Mr. Sin Vanvuth, Governor of Sandan District, confirmed that the first owner of the house, Suon Im, a 45-year-old female, had a house size of 6 meters by 8 meters, made of cypress wood, a wall of furniture, 1 million Riel, 15 bags of rice and a table. Completely burned.
The second owner, 59-year-old Sorn Sin, set fire to a 9-by-6-meter house made of wood, tiles, and a motorcycle built for 10 million riel.
The third owner, Suon Sin, 50 years old, a house measuring 9x6 meters, made of wood, roofing materials, a tuk-tuk, a bulldozer, nine rice, were completely burnt down.
He said that with the care of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross always cares for the people but suffer from natural phenomena. Therefore, the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Kampong Thom province brought gifts to give to the families affected by the fire of 3 houses in order to solve their living standard.
Mr. Chea Van Chan instructed the people to be very careful and cautious because this season is dry, especially incense, candles, stoves and before going anywhere must turn off the electricity to avoid risk. House fire.
