If we want the people of the world to have a better life, we must first have a peaceful and peaceful environment. From the release of "China's position on a political solution to the Ukraine crisis" and "China's position on resolving the Palestinian-Israeli conflict" to the deployment of several officials to coordinate the efforts of China is widely recognized by the international community.
Development is the key to solving all problems. Over the past year, the global economy has recovered from weak forces, the food crisis, the energy crisis and rising commodity prices have put the people of many countries under great pressure. Among the world's major economic entities, in the first three quarters of 2023, China's economy grew by 5.2 percent compared to the same period in 2022. China remains the largest engine of the global economy. .
This year marks the 75th anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China. China will continue to demonstrate the responsibility of major countries to uphold global equality and justice, expand high-level openness and promote global economic recovery. China is willing to work with the international community to meet challenges and promote common prosperity.
