600 fighters trained in artillery to strengthen national defense and territorial integrity
(Phnom Penh): About 600 brave Cambodian fighters have been trained in artillery to participate in national defense and territorial integrity. These 600 fighters have successfully graduated with excellent results and are highly committed to using their knowledge and skills to serve the motherland without hesitation when the nation needs it.
In this spirit, the Artillery Command has opened a series of training courses for the troops under the command. On January 1, 2023, the General Artillery Command held a training course for the 6th generation artillery lieutenants. This training course has a total of 600 participants and lasts for 9 months.
During the ceremony, General Nop Ratana reminded all participants to continue their self-study on artillery skills and to cooperate well during the operation. For General Nop Ratana, the use of artillery without a collective can not achieve better results.
Pech Visal has been serving in the Army at the Artillery Command for one year. Visal joined the army because he wanted to contribute to national defense and territorial integrity. On the other hand, having a father who is a veteran is also a motivating factor for Visal to join the army.
Pech Visal has successfully completed his artillery training skills. Visal claimed that during the training, they received highly attentive training from the teachers. Visal claims that the skills they have learned for about nine months can be used at any time when the nation needs them.
In addition, Visal has bravely determined to use his knowledge and skills to serve the motherland without hesitation when the nation needs it.
It should also be noted that in the closing ceremony of the above training course, General Prof. Dr. Nop Ratana prepared a solidarity meal for the graduates as well as congratulations on the occasion of the Global New Year to the troops of the General Artillery Command. Happy command.
