This Overseas Caterpillar Processing Handicraft is located in O'Sandan Chas Village, Teuk Hot Commune, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province. Then, according to the season, there are many worms.
Deu Pov, 56 years old, the owner of the above worm processing handicraft, described to Fresh News on December 30, 2023 that the opening of the above worm processing handicraft has just started more than a year. . Initially, his family transported fresh worms to be sold to fishermen along the banks of the Phsar Krom River, a business he has been doing for many years.
Later, after seeing the fresh worm processing handicrafts that were opened locally, he stole the experience and technique to open a fresh worm processing craft by himself. Initially, starting little by little until today, there are many workers in the craft of the brothers as well.
He added that for his handicraft processing worms, during the rainy season, which is rich in worms, people can sell worms to him up to 10 tons per day for the price of fresh worms. The rainy season, which is rich in earthworms, he buys from people from 3,000 to 3,500 riel per kilogram for the season rich in earthworms is 5 to 6 months per year.
