The following is a proclamation of the Ministry of Education: Mr. Hun Many presided over the dissemination of the decision of the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hun Many, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, presided over the dissemination ceremony of the decision of the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Party on the afternoon of December 29, 2023. December 10, 2023 to more than 600 CPP members at the CPP office in Phnom Penh.
On this special occasion, the ceremony congratulated His Excellency Hun Manet on his election as Vice President of the Party and congratulated Mr. Hun Many on his election as a Permanent Member of the Party Central Committee. Cambodian people.
After reading the decision of the General Assembly and the announcement of the elected members, Mr. Hun Many recalled the historical journey that Cambodia went through many stages, from independence to the passing of the Sangkum era. The pro-war, Khmer Rouge genocidal regime and the stage of the struggle to liberate the country from the Khmer Rouge regime led to the pursuit of complete peace for the nation and the people by the CPP.
Linking the above points, Mr. HUN Many also provided ideas around the world order, geopolitical competition, the context of the Kovid 19 crisis, climate change and war issues that have been affecting the global economy and politics and Cambodia.
However, he stressed that Cambodia has maintained its resilience by maintaining peace, political stability, economic growth, and social progress, as well as fulfilling Cambodia's obligations in international affairs and within the ASEAN framework. At the same time, he also briefed the members on Cambodia's progress towards achieving its ambition to become a high-middle-income country.
Mr. HUN Many advised all members to strengthen their leadership and institutional capacity in all fields in accordance with the political direction of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia to join forces in national development, defense of the Constitution, peace, democracy. Sovereignty, national interests and people ensure macroeconomic growth and stability, as well as proper foreign policy.
