Disability Foundation of the Ministry of Social Affairs Donates a House to People with Disabilities in Mondulkiri Province
(Mondulkiri): The Disability Fund of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation handed over a house to the disabled in Mondulkiri province on December 29, 2023.
A house of the Foundation for the Disabled, 4 x 6 meters in size, made of galvanized stone, was handed over to a disabled person named Bun Sok Nhim, female, 35 years old, a person with a congenital right leg, who currently has 6 family members Lives in O'Am village, Sre Khtom commune, Keo Seima district, Mondulkiri province.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Huth Ponleu, Deputy Director of the Disability Fund, represented by HE Khom Phal Loeun, Royal Government of Cambodia Representative in charge of the Disability Fund, Director of the Provincial Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, Sre Khtom Commune Council, O'Am Village Representative. Social Welfare, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and local authorities.
Speaking at the event, Mr. HOT Ponleu stated that this house uses a budget of 20,000,000 Riels, part of which was built from the donation box of the Charitable Foundation for the Disabled, which is placed in public places and the contribution of the Royal Government. Cambodia. On behalf of His Excellency the Director of the Foundation for the Disabled, he urged the families of people with disabilities to live in this house to prosper and take care of their health to avoid various diseases.
In this ceremony, the Disability Foundation also brought a package of donations, including: 25 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 stick of soy sauce, 2 sticks of canned fish, 2 bags of salt, 100,000 Riels to the host family to facilitate Livelihood.
Senior official of the Ministry of Interior: Peace, political stability, security and public order are the keys to favoring the process of economic, social and other development.
(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Phan Chanthul, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, opened a meeting to review the results of the implementation of the policy to 2023 villages, communes and sangkats.
The meeting was held on the evening of December 28, 2023 with the participation of Mr. Blake Vary, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey, Deputy Governor, Major General Sithy Loh, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, Military Officer, District Governor. City, commune chief, commune chief, post chief and many other relevant officials.
Mr. Oum Rath gave some recommendations to the District Governor, Commune Chief, Sangkat Chief, Post Chief in order to consider and implement the work more effectively, continue to strengthen and promote the spirit of vigilance, responsibility and national interest. Good cooperation with local authorities, relevant professional institutions in the protection of security, order and public order for local people to get better results.
The provincial governor stated that districts, municipalities, commune chiefs, commune chiefs, and post chiefs must work to improve security and public order throughout the province by promoting the dissemination of safe village-commune policies through the mobilization of all civil servants. Private, civil society organizations, the public to participate in the implementation and cooperation widely and vigorously throughout the province.
He said that the police force, which is law enforcement officers, must strive to improve the capacity, skills and professional ethics with cleanliness, as well as strive to serve the people honestly and fairly.
Mr. Oum Rath added that districts, municipalities, commune chiefs, commune chiefs, and post chiefs must participate in implementing the orders of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Interior, relevant ministries and institutions to prevent and suppress various crimes, such as criminal offenses, human trafficking, gangs, traffic production, consumption and storage. All kinds of drugs, gambling and so on.
In that, the provincial governor urged districts, municipalities, commune chiefs, commune chiefs, post chiefs to continue to provide public services to the people quickly, transparently, effectively, such as providing family books, residence books, continue to promote activities in making and issuing Khmer identity cards to people who Remaining and expiring everyone to avoid any inactive actions that cause resentment from the local people.
Mr. Phan Chanthul stated that peace, political stability, security, public order are the key factors that favor the process of economic, social and other development in line with the policies and strategies of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
He stressed that these are the duties of the police force, which is the core force in maintaining security, order, public order for the well-being of the people, and as a force to intervene in disasters and other social activities such as helping to put out fires. Floods, hurricanes and other activities. Families of car crash victims die for nearly 3 months in Yeak Laom commune, Banlung city, leaving two young children to seek justice
