Youth groups, civil society organizations: Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win politics is a history that Cambodian children must always remember and be grateful for
(Phnom Penh): When it comes to peace and development, the Cambodian people miss the heroism of Samdech first! Heng Samnang stated that December 29 is the historic day of the 25th anniversary of the end of the Cambodian Civil War. A history that Cambodian children, especially students, intellectuals must follow their history.
"What we want to focus on is that as a country, a region with social security problems or a war, of course, our country cannot develop," he said. As a result of leading Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy and integration, Samdech has made efforts to lead the country to increase understanding of history, patriotism and continue to maintain stability, peace and stability. Motherland development.
What we want to see as young people is to follow history as well as value doing something for our motherland. The celebration of the 25th anniversary of the end of the Cambodian Civil War coincides with the 5th anniversary of the construction of the Victory Monument, as well as the commemoration of the gratitude and initiative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the founder and General Guide for Peace.
As the next generation of civil society youth, I would like to express my deepest gratitude to the leaders of the 6th and 7th legislatures under the leadership of His Excellency Hun Manet, who is continuing to lead the Cambodian navy to grow and develop human resources, develop economic resources. Cambodia is sustainable. Phnom Penh Municipal Court Detains 4 Offenders Involved in Killing Victims in Kandal and Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Theam Chanpiseth, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, has ordered the detention of four perpetrators in connection with the use of swords and axes to kill victims in Kandal and Phnom Penh.
Case 1: committed at the riverside, Tonle Sap Road, Group 7, Village 1, Sangkat Chroy Changva, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh on December 22, 2023. The victim was 19-year-old Phal Chanvis.
The four perpetrators are: Hoeun Bunleap, 18 years old, Hun Visal, 18 years old, Thima Hao La, 18 years old, and Nou Sopanha, 17 years old. . Cambodia asks Thailand to expand study tours to boost land tourism movement
(Bangkok): The Cambodian side requested the Thai side to expand study visits to more tourist destinations, especially to Siem Reap and the eastern and northeastern provinces of Cambodia to promote land tourism between the two countries. Be more active.
On that occasion, Ms. Chhay Sivalin expressed her congratulations to Ms. Soda Vanvieng Sopheakkosal, who was entrusted by the Royal Government of Thailand to hold the position of Minister of Tourism and Sports and also committed to continue cooperation in tourism with The Thai side as a player in the tourism industry of Cambodia.
The President of CATA requested the Minister of Tourism of Thailand to facilitate and promote the exchange of Thai public and private sector visits to tourist destinations in Cambodia so that the two countries' tourism and tourism industries can have better cooperation. Together.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin asked Minister Soda Van to continue to instruct the Thai Tourism Authority to continue to facilitate this coordination so that tourists passing through the two countries are more comfortable and Easy.
At the same time, the Cambodian side also requested that the documents be processed faster because in the past, all tourists from Cambodia to Thailand had to wait a little longer, so Ms. Chhay Sivalin. Ask the Thai Ministry of Tourism to make it easier to keep tourists entertained.
Not only that, Ms. Chhay Sivlin also continued to ask the Minister of Tourism of Thailand when the Thai side promotes the Chao Phraya (Chao Preah Ponhea) River tourism destination, please increase the promotion of Cambodia's Tonle Sap Lake tourist destination to increase production. More tourism for foreign tourists.
In response, Ms. Sodavann, Minister of Tourism and Sports of Thailand, accepted all requests from the Cambodian side and promised to coordinate and promote these activities in order to further enhance the cooperation in the field of tourism between Cambodia and Thailand and to promote the tourism movement. Pass through both countries with warmth, convenience and get a good experience from their trip.
Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet advised to continue research on the process of finding peace and ending the war in Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Continue research on the process of finding peace and ending the war in Cambodia.
This introduction was made on the occasion that Samdech Hun Sen presided over the celebration of the 25th anniversary of the end of the Cambodian Civil War and the successful implementation of the win-win politics and the 5th anniversary of the construction of the Victory Monument. In the morning of December 29, 2023.
"We encourage the continued research and documentation of win-win politics and the process of seeking peace and ending the war in Cambodia," he said.
In addition, Samdech President Hun Manet advised to continue to disseminate the content of the win-win policy through seminars, forums, as well as to integrate the historical content related to the win-win policy into the curriculum so that students have a deeper understanding. And know the value of win-win politics.
Samdech Hun Manet also advised to continue researching and organizing win-win monuments in key areas, as well as some important military historical sites with historical value for historical evidence and for study visits.
At the same time, Samdech President Hun Manet advised to pay attention to mobilize and find partners to build and maintain a win-win monument, a symbol of peace in Cambodia. Samdech President Hun Manet appealed to all philanthropists and people to continue to support this work.
