This statement was made on December 29, 2023, when he presided over the celebration of the 25th anniversary of the end of the Cambodian Civil War and the successful implementation of the win-win politics and the 5th anniversary of the construction of the Victory Monument. Win. On that occasion, Samdech President Hun Manet praised all the armed forces who strongly supported the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Celebrating the 25th Anniversary of the End of the Cambodian Civil War and the Successful Implementation of Win-Win Politics in Remembrance of the Complete End of the Civil War in Cambodia Brings Peace and Full National Unity and National Development To this day.
This event coincides with the 5th anniversary of the construction of the Win-Win Monument, a historic building to commemorate the heroism and values of the win-win politics, initiated by Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, the founder and A guide for peace and to raise awareness of national history and patriotism in maintaining stability, security and national development.
Samdech President Hun Manet stated that the Victory Monument was built not to glorify anyone or any group, but the Victory Monument was built as a historical evidence for the younger generation to understand history.
This statement by Samdech Hun Sen was made on the occasion of celebrating the 25th anniversary of the end of the Cambodian Civil War under Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy and the successful implementation of the win-win policy and the 5th anniversary. Years of building a win-win monument.
Samdech Hun Sen said that the construction site of the Victory Monument is a favorable location, but the achievements we have seen today are not in the ordinary shape, both in terms of location and land, in terms of negotiations and fundraising. Meaningful planning and construction requires careful thought and effort.
"Without high commitment here, it would not be possible to build here, and I am a personal witness to Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh's commitment to how to build this historic monument from the beginning." This is the additional emphasis of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet.
Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet also thanked Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh for his efforts to lead the team to build this Victory Monument successfully as planned. Also, I would like to thank General Nem Sovath and all relevant working groups for their attention to the historical aspects to connect at various locations in the Victory Monument in order to fully understand the meaning of the historical monuments that describe the history of Cambodia.
Samdech President Hun Manet added that the Victory Monument was built as a symbol of all Cambodians, built as a symbol of peace, built for all Cambodians, not to glorify Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
President Hun Manet emphasized that, of course, Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the founder of the guiding principle in formulating a win-win political strategy and guiding the execution wisely, but the win-win policy of the one-sided guide cannot be achieved if No involvement in the operation to ensure the continuity of this end-of-war policy.
According to President Hun Manet, war is very likely to happen without thousands or tens of thousands of people, that is, with only one group forming a separatist zone. Extinguishing the flames of war requires the participation of all parties, from commanders to soldiers.
In particular, the benefits of ending the war through win-win politics are shared by all those who criticize, those who do not trust, those who do not believe in win-win politics and skeptics, but those who are benefiting from Peace and Prosperity by Win-Win Politics This is according to the emphasis of Samdech President Hun Manet.
At the same time, Samdech President Hun Manet claimed that the construction of the Victory Monument was made to be a symbol for all Cambodians and a symbol of peace, because every Cambodian is a desire for peace, no one wants peace. This construction is also a celebration of the achievements that all Cambodians have achieved together, as well as a reminder of history so that the next generation of Cambodians will remember the value of peace.
It should be informed that under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Founder and Leader of Win-Win Politics, as well as the active participation of the operators in the spirit of implementing with confidence, seeking peace, national unity and values. High on the right to life, freedom and dignity of the Cambodian people, Cambodia has the peace and full national unity that has never been in the history of 500 years ago.
