(Rattanakiri): After successfully breeding elephants, the President of the Airawatta Association, Ms. Khay Chenda, stated that she will continue to turn Lumphat District into an attractive resort with the potential to earn income for the association and Families of people living nearby.
This statement was made at a time when the Ai Rao Association was organizing a three-year birthday celebration for a baby elephant named Noel Tevy on December 26, 2023, with many guests in attendance at Ka Teang village, Lbang 2 commune. Lumphat District, Rattanakiri Province.
The president of the Irawata Association, Ms. Khay Chenda, said that in 2024, our association is 10 years old, starting from her love and want to preserve the Khmer elephants in Ratanakkiri, she spent time and resources. He bought more than 6 hectares of land and bought three elephants, one female, but unfortunately in 2020, one male elephant, Bak Mai, died.
Despite some problems, the process of breeding elephants continues to go remarkably smoothly. On December 26, 2021, a lovely baby elephant named Noel Devi was born. With the support of the relevant ministries, departments and institutions, the Ka Teang waterfall community also lent the land nearby, which is nearly 100 hectares to be an easy shelter for raising and breeding elephants.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of December 29, 2023, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration closed a meeting to summarize the work results for 2023 and set the work direction for 2024 under the chairmanship of Mr. Prak Sam Oeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, on behalf of Mr. Abhisit Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister. Interior.
On that occasion, Mr. Prak Sam Oeun stated that in 2024, this is the first year of the implementation of the first phase of the Royal Government of Cambodia's strategy, in which the core of the first phase of the Pentagon strategy is focused on reform, strengthening governance and implementation. Modernize state institutions to become modern public administration with high capacity, intelligence and cleanliness.
To maintain internal security stability, ensure the regularity of national institutions, ensure the safety of senior national and international dignitaries, as well as national, regional and international political events held in Cambodia, especially the election process of the fifth mandate senators and council elections. Capital, province, city, district, Khan, 4th mandate in 2024 in the future.
In addition, Mr. Prak Sam Oeun reminded to prevent the formation of illegal armed forces or the establishment of separatist zones, as well as to oppose any tactics of attempting to overthrow the legitimate government. Measures and measures must be taken to prevent and extinguish fires, especially in high-rise buildings, factories, enterprises, markets and people's homes.
Based on the Decade of Strategic Road Safety, the Secretary of State urged the traffic police force to strictly enforce the road traffic law. Continue to strengthen the quality and efficiency of public service delivery by strengthening and improving public institutions at all levels to become modern, competent and clean administration.
Mr. Prak Sam Oeun requested that the leadership of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration to strengthen the examination of civil servants, the management and administration of civil servants, the promotion and appointment of officials must be transparent and accountable, non-partisan and family-oriented. Encourage officials who work hard, have the ability to work and promote skills training and capacity building for civil servants in line with the evolution of work and digital technology.
At present, the provision of public services to the people through the one-stop-shop mechanism has gone smoothly and has the support of the people. In fact, in 2023, the Phnom Penh OWSO has provided a total of 65,698 public services, which means that on average, people come to the Phnom Penh administration for 180 services per day and receive state budget revenue. Nearly 27 billion riels or about 6.58 million US dollars.
In order to ensure the regular and permanent implementation of the national program and to continue to support the lives of poor families and vulnerable family members, the meeting focused on departments, units, local authorities at all levels and program operators to Pay attention to practice with transparency, integrity and high responsibility.
The meeting encouraged and provided full support to the 14 Khan administrations, with the Khan Office of Education, Youth and Sports as its staff, to strive to improve the provision of education services within the jurisdiction through good cooperation with the armed forces. Armed to eradicate gangsters, big and small, and drug problems in schools.
