(Phnom Penh): On the night of Thursday, December 28, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Chairman of the King's Personal Advisory Council, posted a short video clip showing the activities of the tourists of the Western Dam dancing before they board the ship. Cambodia.
With the posting of this video, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded of his decision to allow the ship to dock in Cambodia more than three years ago, on February 13, 2020, after many countries did not allow the ship to enter. Parked for fear of an outbreak of Kovid 19.
Samdech Techo stated that he wanted this question from those who claim to be the Father of Human Rights and Democracy to answer this question.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned his views and strong position that from the beginning to the end, the right to life is the most important point, because if he dies, what are the rights and democracy?
Recall that in February 2020, the Western Dam cruise ship with a total of more than 2,000 tourists and crew sailed on the ocean for about two weeks after the port in the country up to 5 not allowed. Have the ship docked after it is suspected that the passengers on the ship contracted Kovid 19 disease.
The US Embassy in Cambodia, through Mr. Sun Chanthol, who was then Senior Minister, sought permission from Samdech Techo Hun Sen to allow the ship to dock in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen did not hesitate after receiving the request, Samdech Techo allowed the ship to dock on February 13. Not only allowed to dock, on February 14, one day after the ship docked, Samdech Techo went to pick up passengers directly from the ship, accompanied by roses and scarves.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's decision at that time led to great admiration and admiration on the international stage. But for the opposition in Cambodia at the time, they did not welcome Samdech Techo Hun Sen's decision, and they even criticized Samdech Techo's decision.
At that time, all the passengers on the ship were not found to have 19 cases of Kovid. Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced at that time that not to mention that there were no 19 cases of Kovid. Samdech Techo's humane gestures led to the nickname Cambodia as a small country with a big heart, a heart full of emotions and love for humanity in the world.
