(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Chairman of the Local Government Working Group on Banteay Meanchey Province, this morning, December 28, 2023, presided over the ceremony to announce the composition of the Royal Government Working Group. 112 people in Banteay Meanchey province at the administrative hall of Banteay Meanchey provincial hall.
The Minister paid a courtesy call on His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and the Royal Government's efforts to implement the party's policies and the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy, as well as the establishment of a grassroots working group. Serve the interests of the people and participate in promoting the national economy as well.
At the same time, Minister Dith Tina also announced the composition of 122 national grassroots working groups, which have a total of 3,659 members to assist communes, sangkats, cities and districts. Through the working group that was divided and instructed the working group to prepare additional components to reach all village bases throughout Banteay Meanchey province in accordance with the instructions from the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
