(Pursat): The Cambodia-Japan Water Treatment Plant in Pursat City was officially inaugurated on December 28, 2023, increasing the water production capacity of Pursat Water Supply Authority almost twice.
The inauguration ceremony was presided over by Mr. Hem Vandy, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, High Representative of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Mr. UENO ATSUSHI, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia. Joint efforts between Cambodia and Japan to address the growing demand for clean water in the province.
The event was also attended by representatives of relevant ministries and institutions, the Embassy of Japan in the Kingdom of Cambodia, JICA, Kitakyushu Municipality, Pursat Provincial Administration, local authorities, technical advisors, construction companies and a total of 650 people.
Mr. Hem Vandy thanked the Government and people of Japan for their continued support for Cambodia's development, especially in the field of clean water.
He said: "This is the third water treatment plant under the financial assistance of the Government of Japan, which was inaugurated in 2023 after the new water treatment plant in Siem Reap and Stung Sen II. In Kampong Thom province. "As we celebrate the 70th anniversary of the strong and vibrant diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Japan in 2023, we also highlight the many achievements of this relationship."
Along with the socio-economic development and physical infrastructure in recent years, the demand for clean water in Pursat has been steadily increasing. Pursat Water Supply Authority, the provincial body in charge of water supply in the province, has responded to this growing demand by increasing its water production capacity through the inauguration of the new water treatment plant.
Under a grant from the Government of Japan through JICA totaling 2,405 million yen (approximately 22.2 million US dollars), the project will take 24 months to complete from August 2021 to August 2023. Including a water treatment plant and an administrative building that will contribute to the improvement of water infrastructure in Pursat province as a whole.
The Cambodia-Japan Water Purification Plant in Pursat City with a capacity of 6,600 m3 / day will boost the water production capacity of Pursat Water Supply Authority to 13,860 m3 / day. With a 247-kilometer water distribution network, Pursat Water Supply Authority will be able to distribute clean, safe, sustainable and affordable water to more than 15,000 families in Pursat City and parts of Bakan and Kandieng districts.
This significant achievement not only addresses the community's urgent need for clean water, but also supports Cambodia's 2030 Sustainable Development Goals. With this achievement, Pursat will also be better able to attract more investment, which contributes to the economic development and well-being of the people in the province.
