Mr. Ny Buntha, the family member of the body, denied and clarified that as a son-in-law was with his father-in-law, he was well aware of his father-in-law's condition.
Sources said that before arriving at Khieng Sokunthea Hospital, he also went to other doctors, but other doctors did not receive treatment. In particular, when his father arrived at the hospital, Khieng Sokunthea also asked the doctor to help treat his father, but the hospital did not want to receive treatment, but because his family begged too much, the hospital agreed to receive treatment. And made the right contract.
He said that when he arrived at the Provincial Referral Hospital, the provincial doctor continued to send his father-in-law to Phnom Penh, but he did not want to go, but due to his illness, his father-in-law had to be sent to Phnom Penh while being sent halfway across the Prek Bridge. I was a little sick, my father's condition worsened, causing him to die on the way.
Please note that in the contract, the patient's family agreed to allow the doctor to perform a technical emergency, regardless of any complications or obstacles that may eventually occur in this treatment. If during the emergency or after the doctor's emergency, but the patient still can not save, the patient's family has promised not to file a complaint or seek compensation from the medical team and the hospital.
In connection with this case, according to the doctor of Khieng Sokunthea Hospital, the patient who came to his hospital was named Chin Phat, 62 years old, living in Ta Leuk Village, Angkor Tret Commune, Svay Antor District. Prey Veng has been suffering from severe chronic diseases for many years, with high blood pressure, heart disease and chronic pneumonia.
