Turkish Parliamentary Foreign Affairs Committee approves Sweden's NATO application
Sweden and Finland have abandoned their decades-long policy of neutrality and sought membership in the US-led military following Russia's invasion of Ukraine in February 2022.
Their proposal was immediately approved by all NATO members except Turkey and Hungary, as the decision was unanimous. Both countries eventually repented, and Finland was recognized as the 31st member of NATO in April. Sweden, on the other hand, 19 months after applying for membership, has not yet been approved.
However, on Tuesday this week, the Turkish Parliament's Foreign Affairs Committee approved the measure.
