(Kampong Speu): The community of Eight Forests has claimed that wild animals such as deer, elk, wild boar, peacock and many other species that remain in the forest are facing serious attacks in 2023 could face extinction if the authorities Relevant professional authorities do not have strict preventive measures.
Soeun Lay, President of the Eight Mum Forest Community, said on December 27, 2023 that traps had been deployed throughout the forest and doubled, posing a serious threat to the lives of rare wild boar. Peacocks and other animals.
He said that in 2022, the community found only 444 traps, but in 2023, as of December, the community found nearly 900 traps, which number seems to have doubled.
The eight-community forest chief added that the traps were found by community forces and deployed in densely forested areas and sugarcane fields with water sources.
"Moreover, the most vulnerable animals are when they leave the community forest to get drinking water, because there are always hunters deploying traps to hunt and catch these rare animals," he said. "Seeing this challenge, the community decided to ask the authorities to dig a pond in the community forest to save water for these rare animals to drink and avoid harassment by active hunters, trappers."
Regarding the request of the Eight Mum Forest Community, Mr. Sim Rattanak, Deputy Governor of Kampong Speu Province, decided to accept the request and also announced to find a private partner who can afford to dig, in which the private company can use the land as needed. Only ponds for the community for the animals to drink.
It should be noted that the community of Pram Bei Mom has an area of about 1221 hectares located in Thnal Keng village and Trapeang Kreun village, Pram Bei Mom commune, Srong Thpong, Kampong Speu province.
