(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on December 27, 2023 disseminated and officially launched the Mental Health Strategic Plan 2023-2032 under the chairmanship of Professor Chheang Ra, Minister of Health.
"Mental health is an important component of our health," he said. There is no health without mental health. Body and mind are always in contact, interacting with each other and inseparable. Therefore, mental health is the responsibility of all of us and is also an important element in ensuring quality human resources.
Therefore, on the occasion of the official launch of the Mental Health Strategic Plan 2023-2032, the Minister also made some additional recommendations, including:
* Encourage cooperation with relevant institutions to promote mental health and prevent mental illness.
* Health training institutions need to develop training programs specializing in mental illness, medical skills, mental health and the science of new behaviors to meet the needs of the population, and to include public mental health in relevant training and Public health to increase knowledge on public health in all aspects.
* National and sub-national health services need to expand mental health care and treatment services, both psychiatric counseling and psychiatric treatment services, and more options for people to reach coverage. Global Health.
At the same time, the Minister also called on all stakeholders, including the people, to work together to improve mental health and stop stigmatizing or discriminating against mentally ill people.
In addition, Minister Chheang Ra called on all relevant bilateral and multilateral development partners to support additional resources to make the implementation of this strategic plan more effective in accordance with the framework contained in the strategic plan. Because mental health is a priority that has been emerging in the health sector as well.
