On the occasion of co-chairing with the Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia at the inauguration ceremony of the sewage system in Phnom Penh, Samdech Hun Sen highlighted that the good relations between Cambodia and Japan are important achievements. Many were built as a result of the contribution of the Royal Government and the people of Japan to Cambodia.
His Excellency Hun Manet claims that according to the historical record, Cambodia-Japan is not only connected for 70 years, but more than 400 years ago, during the Odong period, there was a Japanese village in the capital. Odong at once. But relations were severed when Cambodia fell into the flames of war and were reconnected.
According to the Prime Minister, in 2023, this is the 70th anniversary of the establishment of relations between Cambodia and Japan, with only four days left to reach the 71st anniversary of the Royal Government and the people of the country. The two need to strengthen their relationship even better. In this regard, Prince Hun Manet thanked the Royal Government and the people of Japan for always providing support to the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia.
The Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia emphasized that in the past 70 years, despite some problems, but after Cambodia achieved peace in the early 1990s, Japan has played an important role in helping Cambodia. In the negotiation phase, the war ended.
In addition to the 70th anniversary of the relationship between Cambodia and Japan, this year the two governments have also decided to upgrade this relationship to a comprehensive strategic partnership. This is according to what Prince Hun Manet emphasized.
It should be informed that His Excellency Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, last week recently paid an official visit to Japan to attend the meeting to commemorate the 50th anniversary of ASEAN-Japan relations.
Starting from good relations and also being upgraded to a comprehensive strategic partnership, Japan has supported Cambodia in maintaining peace, supporting recovery after the end of the civil war, which has a program of assistance. Support the development of democracy, socio-economic development.
Apparently, the Chroy Changvar bridge was repaired after being blown up during the civil war. As well as the construction of major bridges, roads, infrastructure, health facilities, schools and many other irrigation systems to improve the lives of Cambodians.
In terms of economic cooperation between Cambodia and Japan, it was 1.6 billion yen in 1981, now it has increased to more than 200 times by 2022. For the Japanese group in Cambodia, there is also a high growth and Japanese companies have been significantly involved in investing in Cambodia.
