Koh Kong Deputy Commissioner Comes Out After Allegations That He Took Land at Sre Ambel District Police Station to Build His Own House
(Koh Kong): Mr. Hourn Nonn, Deputy Commissioner of Koh Kong Provincial Police, came out to clarify after he was accused that he took the land of the police station to build a house in Sre Ambel commune, Sre Ambel district, Koh Kong province.
Deputy provincial commissioner Huon Nonn told Fresh News on December 25 that the public's accusation that he had used the unit's post office land to build a house was not on the land on which he was building the house. It does not involve the land, headquarters or post of any unit or individual, and the construction of his house is legally permitted by the local authority.
Mr. Houn Nonn said that during 2021, as the Inspector of Sre Ambel District, he asked the Sre Ambel Commune Chief to find a small plot of land to build a temporary police station so that police officers could have a suitable place to work. Come to the Sre Ambel Administrative Police Station, there is no good place to work yet. In the past, the station was under the roof of Sre Ambel commune hall for decades.
Later, the Sre Ambel commune hall requested to change the location of the post so that the commune hall could rebuild the commune's resource building, and then, as the district inspector, discussed with the commune chief and also informed the district governor about the change and Construction of a temporary administrative police station, the Sre Ambel Administrative Police Station. He added that the discussion also had the permission and approval of the Sre Ambel district governor.
Later, the commune chief, the group leader, inspected the location of the state land that was left from the clearing of a vacant deep water, which was also owned by the state and commune authorities. Later, he saw a villager set up a post to encroach on the land as private property, but did not throw it all away, leaving only one plot of land more than 10 meters, which can build a temporary police station.
He filled in the rubble and built a temporary post measuring 6.20 meters x 15 meters with a total area of 190 square meters. For the construction of this administrative post, he contributed his family's own budget.
After the construction was completed, he wrote a letter of respect to the Major General to ask for his policy to change the location of the old administrative post to work at the new administrative post, he and his family are the builders, and with the approval of the Commissioner on December 19, 2023 as well.
The house he is building is not related to the land of the administrative post or any other person. The Sre Ambel commune chief gave him an empty 6.7-meter plot of land adjacent to the administrative post, and he asked for an additional 5 meters of neighboring land to build a house. He confirmed that the reserve land for the construction of the administrative post was behind the Sre Ambel market, but the market was full of rubbish.
Keo Sok, chief of Sre Ambel commune, said that the land that Huon Non was building was given to him without any involvement with the administrative post because he was looking at Huon Non's house 50 km away from his work site. He also had a lot of work to do and spent his own money to build an administrative post.
He said that in the past, the administrative post was behind a small commune hall in the form of dilapidated timber, and this old post was requested by the commune inspector to temporarily rebuild the commune's resource building, so he found the remaining land of the commune. The post has been built and the construction is done, he has the right permission in accordance with the law.
Mr. Chea Chankanha, Governor of Sre Ambel District, said that Mr. Huon Nonn had the right to build a building because he had the approval of the local committee to properly inspect and the consent of the people who bordered the border. Without objection, it can be built if any party objectes or without permission can not build. An explosion occurred near the Israeli embassy in India, but no one was injured.
