(Siem Reap): The APSARA Authority on December 27, 2023 issued a statement on the dissemination of false information about the activities to prevent illegal construction in Sandan village, Sangkat Teuk Vil, Siem Reap city, Siem Reap province.
APSARA Authority said that on the morning of December 26, 2023, there was a post on Facebook about the illegal demolition activities of the APSARA Authority's law enforcement team in Sandan Village, Sangkat Teuk Vil Krong. Siem Reap.
The APSARA Authority states that these advertisements are contrary to the facts and create misunderstanding by the public about the APSARA Authority.
In this regard, APSARA Authority would like to inform the public about this case as follows:
1. The building that was the subject of the demolition is an illegal type of construction that has been built without permission since May 2023.
2. As a precautionary measure, the working group handed over a letter of notification requiring the owner to dismantle it himself, with a three-day period from May 25-27, 2023. This work was heard by Sandan village chief.
3. Later, at the request of the above illegal construction owners to dismantle these structures by themselves, the team to prevent illegal construction asked the owners to sign a voluntary demolition contract with 3 days from the 10th. November 12, 2023
4. Through this, the APSARA Authority has set aside a reasonable time for the builders to dismantle themselves for many months.
5. The person who cried in the social media is not the host above.
