Taiwan will hold general elections to elect its new leader on January 13, 2024, with the current leader, Sai Yingluck, out of office. Issued by Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun for Kampong Cham Provincial Administration for 2024
(Kampong Cham): At the Closing Ceremony of the Conference to Summarize 2023 Work Results and Raise Work Directions for 2024, Dr. Neth Savoeun, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group for Kampong Cham Province, set out three priority work directions to The provincial administration uses it as a beacon to further the implementation of the goals set by the province.
In the afternoon ceremony on December 26, 2023, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun started from the first big point is to strengthen stability, security, social order, increase harmony for the people under the cold shadow of peace of the Royal Government of Cambodia. Out of a legitimate election and born out of the real will of the people.
To strengthen security and order, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun stressed that extremist groups who have plotted to overthrow the government have not given up their ideas, and especially the locomotives abroad, so vigilance must continue to increase vigilance. While crime, drugs, order and traffic safety must be strengthened to create conditions for people to work without worries.
In this regard, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun advised to strengthen the capacity of the competent authorities at all levels by increasing the capacity, increasing the responsibility to ensure the response to the crime group for the comfort of the people. In addition, it is necessary to mobilize the people to participate and promote education to the people so that the owners can participate with the competent authorities to protect and report when there is a suspicion or crime.
He also urged the provincial administration to draw up a clear plan to build and develop localities, provinces and districts, and to be aware of the geography, potential and potential to attract more investors to develop in Kampong Cham province. There is more growth and aims to attract jobs to the people as well as increase the income of each family.
With the above guidance, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun expressed his strong hope that the Kampong Cham Provincial Administration, with Mr. Un Chanda as the Provincial Governor, will make every effort to be more successful in 2024. .
According to the report of Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, in 2023, local authorities at all levels and the three competent forces will continue to work to protect peace, security and public order at the local level, especially continue to implement Regulations and guidelines of the Royal Government, especially the Ministry of Interior, to ensure and maintain effective social security and safety.
(Phnom Penh): In the morning of Wednesday, March 15, 2023, which is on December 27, 2023, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the sewage system. In Phnom Penh.
Wastewater generated in Phnom Penh has increased rapidly due to population growth as well as building infrastructure. Wastewater in Phnom Penh flows through the toilets of each family home and business building. Fluid from the floating basin is discharged into the lake through sewers and canals and is purified naturally but to a lesser extent.
In view of the above, the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) has studied the project to improve the drainage and sewage system in Phnom Penh from 2014 to 2016 in response to the request of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The project aims to build a wastewater treatment plant, sewer and sewerage pumping facility based on a short-term program to be implemented in stages in the master project.
The above project was started on February 22, 2022 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Construction in the inaugural project includes:
1: Construction and pumping of wastewater to Choeung Ek wastewater treatment plant with a pumping capacity of 7 cubic meters per minute.
2: Road for maintenance of canals and for digging and laying sewer pipes, drainage water to Choeung Ek wastewater treatment station, about 1,700 meters long, 10 meters wide, paved with AC rubber.
3. A 0.3-meter-long steel sewer pipe, approximately 1,840 meters long, to drain wastewater from the interception and pumping water to the Choeung Ek Wastewater Treatment Plant.
4: Choeung Ek wastewater treatment plant with a capacity of 5,000 cubic meters of wastewater per day.
