National University of Battambang Celebrates 4th Anniversary of Confucius Institute
(Battambang): The National University of Battambang on the morning of December 26, 2023 celebrated the 4th anniversary of the establishment of the Confucius Institute.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Education, Youth and Sports.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron said that Cambodia and China are long-standing neighbors, strategic partners in all aspects of cooperation between the two countries, and have an inseparable steel relationship. As Cambodia-China relations have improved and deepened, cooperation between the two countries in all fields has continued to increase in both scope and depth.
The Minister emphasized that Cambodia has actively responded to the "Belt and Road Initiative" by participating in several construction projects. China has continued to be the largest source of investors and the largest source of tourists to Cambodia, which has driven the Cambodian economy to continue to develop at a high level, as well as significantly increased the demand for Chinese language learning. Personally, I am also learning Chinese in my spare time.
These activities have become a bridge between international Chinese language education in northwestern Cambodia and China through cultural exchanges between China and Cambodia and the promotion of friendship between our two nations. All these activities are covered in national and international media. In particular, the Confucius Institute at the National University of Battambang has won some outstanding awards in some well-known Chinese newspapers.
She urged all stakeholders to continue to support the Confucius Institute at the National University of Battambang for growth and prestige in the Northwest Zone.
