(Phnom Penh): Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport is a leading public higher education institution that trains human resources in the field of public works and transportation with quality, innovation, professional ethics and national and international recognition.
To meet the shortage of technicians in the field of public works and transportation in Cambodia, the Institute has been recruiting 300 undergraduate and Bachelor + 1 (Engineering) students in the academic year 2023-2024, including the Institute Scholarship 100% 50 places and 50% (women) many places in accordance with the requirements of the Institute.
Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport provides undergraduate and graduate +1 (engineering) training on the following academic skills:
* Road, highway, bridge, railway and port construction skills * Wastewater treatment system skills * Economics and land transport management skills * Logistics and supply chain management skills * Ship driving skills * Ship engine skills
Separately, for the subjects of the 4th generation student selection exam, it depends on the selected skills as follows:
First: Road, Expressway, Bridge, Railway and Port Construction Skills Second: Wastewater Treatment System Skills * Required to pass the exam in Mathematics, Physics and English
Third: Economic and land transport management skills Fourth: Logistics and supply chain management skills Fifth: Shipbuilding skills Sixth: Ship engine skills
* Requirements to pass the exam on subjects: Mathematics, General Culture and English
Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport has started to open and accept applications for the 4th generation of students - Date: From November 30, 2023 onwards - Time: 8:00 am - Location: Office of Education Ground floor of Akka Institute - Application deadline: January 08, 2024 at 5:00 pm.
For more details, please contact on the selection of 300 4th generation students to study for Bachelor's and Bachelor's Degree + 1 + 2023-2024 academic year.
Minister of Information urges the media to participate in maintaining peace, stability and social order through the dissemination of factual information
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Information has encouraged the media to participate in maintaining peace, stability and social order through the dissemination of accurate, accurate and ethical information to enhance the value of the media and the value of journalists. Good order.
This was stated by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information during a meeting with the Global Peace Journalists Association led by Mr. Hun Makara, President of the Association on the morning of December 26, 2023 at the Ministry of Information.
The Minister of Information considered the Media Association as an important partner to walk together, consult with each other, the Ministry can not be separated from the Media Association, but to meet to grasp the main goals and challenges. In order to make the media and audio-visual sector in Cambodia move forward vigorously.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that what he wanted to see was that the media sector in Cambodia was not only strong enough to stand firm within the framework of professional ethics and quality, but also to stand out in the regional and global framework because of the direction of In the future, the Ministry of Information must become the government's public relations institution, and within the framework of the press must be the voice of Cambodia.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that in the seventh mandate, the Ministry of Information has been making the media sector a priority, playing an important role as the voice of Cambodia, meaning that all media have a role in helping to spread the word about Cambodia to the people. People to the world. The Ministry also focuses on institutional modernization, building facilities for day-to-day operations, and modernizing the capacity of officials and reporters in line with social change and evolution.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra continued that this modernization is not only within the framework of the Ministry of Information, but also for the journalists as a whole, also needs to be modernized by reopening the Media Training Center and Crisis to help strengthen the capacity of journalists. Strong foundation in producing and writing quality news articles.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra continued that the level of knowledge and human resources of Cambodia has improved, so all media need to strengthen the production of quality information to serve their readers and to contribute to strengthening the quality of Cambodia's human resources through the provision Real, fast and quality information.
The occasion was also accompanied by Lt. Gen. Sok Thoeun, Deputy Director of the Central Border Police Department, and Lt. Gen. Sim Sam Ath, Director of the Land Border Police Department.
