(Siem Reap): 200 needy families in Sangkat Kork Chak, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province received food donations from the Life Saving Association of Singapore.
The donation was made by Mr. Bun Tha Rith, Member of Parliament for Siem Reap Constituency, at the Kork Chak Temple in the presence of monks and Mr. Bun Tha Rith, Member of Parliament for Siem Reap Constituency, Mr. Goh Tung Hong, President of Life-Saving Association. Of Singapore and colleagues, municipal authorities, commune councils, as well as philanthropists.
Each family received 10 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 bottle of cooking oil and 2 bottles of soy sauce, in which Mr. Bun Tha Rith and philanthropists donated 15,000 Riels per family.
The President of the Life-Saving Association stated that the purpose of the Life-Saving Delegation Association is an association that does not serve any politics, only serves the humanitarian movement in the world. He added that this is a small gift to help solve and alleviate the needs of the people for a while. His association will continue to help Cambodians in need in other local areas as well.
Mr. Buntharith thanked the Life-Saving Association of Singapore for its generosity to the Cambodian people in joining the Royal Government of Cambodia in the aftermath of the Kovid-19 crisis. This gesture of generosity will make it an opportunity to strengthen the bonds of solidarity and strengthen the good cooperation between the two nations and peoples.
He also requested the Life-Saving Association to continue its activities in Cambodia to participate in the development with the Royal Government of Cambodia, such as the construction of school buildings, health centers, roads, water wells and toilets, environment. And drug-related workers must be fired and dealt with according to the law without tolerance
