Mr. Samleang Try warned all staff and workers, especially at the construction site, if they are involved in drug problems, they should be fired and take legal action without exception.
(Kampong Thom): Mrs. Lum Kuntheary, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province, Deputy Director of the Department around the three forces, many government officials and students on December 26, 2023, celebrated the 12th National Day Against Human Trafficking. December under the theme: Technology as a means for national development, not for human trafficking in Kampong Thom Provincial Hall.
Colonel Kang Koy, Deputy Commissioner of the Provincial Police and Deputy Director of the CPPCC Secretariat, said that the efforts to combat human trafficking in the province, which has six working groups, are structured at the district level. Up to the provincial level, including partner organizations in the province in order to prevent, fight, fight against human trafficking and destroy the honor, dignity, interests and even the lives of the victims.
The Deputy Commissioner of the Provincial Police said that although human trafficking has not yet ended, the mission is not over and will continue to work harder, which requires greater support and cooperation to prevent it. Eliminate human trafficking successfully.
Ms. Lum Kuntheary said that the National Anti-Human Trafficking Day program on December 12, the Royal Government of Cambodia is strongly committed to safeguarding national peace, social security, political stability, sustainable economic growth by strengthening broader national-international cooperation and Development of human resources with energy and potential.
The Royal Government of Cambodia remains committed to resolutely oppose all forms of human trafficking and other crimes that have been seriously disturbing the society, harming the honor, dignity and interests of the people. As well as seriously undermining security, social order and the national economy.
Technology is also being used by criminals to lure people into all kinds of crime, including human trafficking and all forms of exploitation. The Royal Government of Cambodia strives to find all means, resources and techniques to actively investigate the perpetrators and destroy the criminal efficiency of criminals and rescue those who are vulnerable and vulnerable.
