This statement was made by Samdech President Hun Manet on the occasion of the announcement of the national report on the final results of the Cambodian Economic Census 2022 this morning, December 26, 2023.
"In 2022, not only good data but also the ability of the Cambodian people, our officials have the ability to self-research, of course, we have technical assistance from friends, partners, but the ability of officials," he said. We in ourselves do this is something we should be proud of. "This capacity building is to ensure that we want to turn on the lights whenever we turn off the lights, light up the walkway, this is an important task."
At the same time, the Prime Minister of Cambodia reminded that the first time we did in 2011 when the data situation, the technical situation was difficult, but most importantly, when human resources are still limited, we rely entirely on technical support.
Samdech Mani praised the efforts of the National Institute of Statistics of the Ministry of Planning, the National Economic Census Committee in the Kingdom of Cambodia, the Economic Census Technical Committee, the Economic Census Propaganda Committee, the Economic Census Committee in the Capital and Provinces, and the team. All the technical core work to achieve the success of the 2022 Economic Census in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The census has already been conducted twice, the 2011 census and the 2022 census.
On the occasion of presiding over the dissemination of the National Report on the Final Results of the Cambodian Economic Census 2022, His Excellency Hun Manet made seven recommendations to help orient the work of the Ministry of Planning as follows:
First, we request the Ministry of Planning to translate this census data into comprehensive and scientific information through the use of appropriate methods of statistical science as a strong input for all ministries and institutions to use in their respective work. Especially for policy making based on this evidence and information. Samdech encourages the dissemination of these results widely to all relevant ministries and institutions.
Second, the Ministry of Planning, with the National Institute of Statistics as its staff, must continue to improve the economic census and other relevant surveys, ensuring the collection of data that is truly representative of the issues it wants to study for its benefit. And inputs for national socio-economic development. To ensure good representation, the sample must be well prepared in a statistical manner using the appropriate sampling method.
Third, the relevant ministries and institutions must cooperate with the Ministry of Planning in conducting the necessary censuses and surveys, as the Ministry of Planning is a state institution with high technical skills in charge of data collection, in order to improve the census. Socio-economic as a whole, and in other words, to be an input for all ministries and institutions to carry out their respective work.
Fourth, the Ministry of Planning must continue to increase the capacity of its officials on a regular basis for the necessary surveys and censuses, as well as the work of translating data into sufficient information for the Royal Government to use in a timely manner.
Fifth, the Ministry of Planning must develop a strategic plan for attracting and mobilizing highly talented human resources in statistics and statistical analysis, both domestically and abroad, for the important work of the Ministry. At the same time, the redistribution of existing human resources to or near specialization will help increase efficiency and productivity.
Seventh, request the Ministry of Economy and Finance to examine the possibility of allocating budget resources for investment in human resource training and increase human capital as indicated in the Pentagon Strategy - Phase 1 and for the provision of appropriate technological equipment for the Ministry of Planning. To increase the efficiency of performance in the field of statistics to be highly efficient, good quality and fast.
