(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, March 14, 2023, which falls on December 26, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, presided over the dissemination of a national report on the results. The latest of the Cambodian economic census 2022.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Mani Hun Manet's opportunity to publish the national report on the final results of the Cambodian Economic Census 2022:
* Samdech Hun Manet praised and commended the efforts of the National Institute of Statistics of the Ministry of Planning, the National Committee for Economic Census in the Kingdom of Cambodia, the Economic Census Technical Committee, the Economic Census Propaganda Committee, the Economic Census Committee in the Capital and Provinces, and All technical core teams for the successful completion of the 2022 Economic Census in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
* President Hun Manet thanked the World Bank for providing technical assistance for the census.
* Hun Manet stated that quality and reliable statistical data is indispensable evidence that policy makers need for policy formulation, strategy, and short-term socio-economic development planning. Medium and long.
* President Hun Manet stated that the census data is very important, helping policy makers gain insight into the structure, livelihoods, and achievements of an economy.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that the data helps to analyze the work clearly and without risk.
* President Hun Manet stated that it is a matter of pride that Cambodia was able to conduct the 2022 national economic census on its own, which is a demonstration of the ability of officials.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that the 2022 National Economic Census is a very important basis for Cambodia to move forward and achieve national plans.
* President Hun Manet stated that the 2022 National Economic Census shows that the Royal Government does what is based on clarity, not imagination.
* Samdech Thipdey Hun Manet instructed the relevant ministries and institutions to cooperate with the Ministry of Planning in conducting the census and the necessary surveys, as the Ministry of Planning is a state institution with high technical skills in charge of data collection to improve the census. Socio-economic as a whole, and on the other hand to be an input for all ministries and institutions to carry out their respective work.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet advised the Ministry of Planning to continue to increase the capacity of its officials on a regular basis for the necessary surveys and censuses, as well as to turn the data into sufficient information for the Royal Government to use in a timely manner.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet stated that this era needs science, not fortune tellers.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet instructed the Ministry of Planning to develop a strategic plan for attracting and mobilizing highly talented human resources in statistics and statistical analysis, both domestically and abroad, for the ministry's important work. At the same time, the redistribution of existing human resources to the skills or near specialization will help increase efficiency and productivity.
* Samdech Hun Manet Requests the Ministry of Economy and Finance to Examine the Feasibility of Allocating Budget Resources for Investment in Human Resource Training and Increasing Human Capital Indicated in the Pentagon Strategy - Phase I and for the Appropriate Technology Equipment for the Ministry of Planning To increase the efficiency of performance in the field of statistics to be highly efficient, good quality and fast.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet recommended 7 points to help orient the work of the Ministry of Planning as follows:
First. Please request the Ministry of Planning to turn this economic census data into comprehensive and scientific information through the use of appropriate methods of statistical science to be a solid input for all ministries-institutions used in their respective work, especially for Policy making based on this evidence and information, Samdech encourages the dissemination of these results widely to all relevant ministries and institutions.
Second. The Ministry of Planning, under the auspices of the National Institute of Statistics, must continue to improve the economic census and other relevant surveys, ensuring the collection of data that is truly representative of the issues to be studied, explored for the benefit and input. For socio-economic development. To ensure good representation, the sample must be well prepared in a statistical manner using the appropriate sampling method.
Third. Relevant ministries and institutions must cooperate with the Ministry of Planning in conducting the necessary censuses and surveys, as the Ministry of Planning is a state institution with high technical expertise in charge of data collection, in order to improve the socio-economic census. Overall, in other words, to be an input for all ministries and institutions to carry out their respective work.
Fourth. The Ministry of Planning must continue to increase the capacity of its officials on a regular basis for the necessary surveys and censuses, as well as the work of translating data into sufficient information for the Royal Government to use in a timely manner.
Fifth. The Ministry of Planning must develop a strategic plan for attracting and mobilizing highly talented human resources in statistics and statistical analysis, both domestically and abroad, for the ministry's important work. At the same time, the redistribution of existing human resources to or near specialization will help increase efficiency and productivity.
7th. Request the Ministry of Economy and Finance to examine the feasibility of allocating budget resources for investment in human resource training and human capital increase as indicated in the Pentagon Strategy - Phase I and for the development of appropriate technological equipment for the Ministry of Planning to increase efficiency. Of performing work in the field of statistics in a highly efficient, high-quality and timely manner.
