Samdech Hun Sen Presides Over the 4th Mekong-Lan Chang Cooperation Summit on Video
(Phnom Penh): On Monday afternoon, December 25, 2023, Prime Minister Hun Manet attended the 4th Mekong-Lan Chang Cooperation Summit via video.
This afternoon's meeting was co-chaired by General Min Aung Lan, Chairman of the Myanmar Administrative Council, and Chinese Premier Li Chiang.
The 4th Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation was held under the theme "Participate in building a common destiny and modernization among the Mekong-Lanchang countries".
Under the above theme, the leaders of the Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation will review the progress made under the cooperation and set future directions for the expansion of the cooperation area and boost mutual trust. As well as strengthening partnerships among the Mekong-Lanchang countries to contribute to socio-economic development and improve the well-being of the people in the Mekong-Lanchang subregion.
The 4th Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation Summit will be an important event for Mekong-Lanchang member countries to achieve common goals in promoting peace, stability and prosperity in the sub-region and promoting Mekong-Lanchang cooperation goes further through the implementation of the five-year action plan on Mekong-Lanchang cooperation.
It should be noted that the Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation is a cooperation between five countries along the Mekong River, including Myanmar, Thailand, Laos, Cambodia and Vietnam, and the Lanchang River, China. The cooperation was initiated by Li Keqiang at the 17th China-ASEAN Summit on November 13, 2014 in Myanmar, following the Thai Initiative for Sustainable Development of the Subregion. Mekong-Lanchang in 2012.
Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation has set up several meetings divided into four levels. The working group meeting is held once or twice a year and as necessary, the meeting of senior officials is held once a year and as necessary, the meeting of foreign ministers is held once a year. The summit is held every two years.
The Mekong-Lanchang meeting is to be held with China as the permanent co-chair, and the Mekong countries to take turns chairing in alphabetical order.
The second Mekong-Lanchang Summit in 2018 was held in Cambodia with Cambodia and China as co-chairs.
Mekong-Lanchang cooperation is established in accordance with the principles of consensus, openness, integration, equality, consultation and mutual coordination, volunteering, contribution and common interests, and respect for the UN Charter. And international law.
Mekong-Lan Chang Cooperation Established with the aim of promoting cooperation in all fields, building a community of peaceful and prosperous future, maintaining peace, stability and promoting regional development, accelerating the "Economic Belt and the Silk Road" 21st Century Silk Road, also known as "One Road - One Belt".
It should be noted that the Mekong-Lanchang River has a total river area of approximately 4,880 km, passing through six countries: China, Myanmar, Thailand, Laos, Cambodia and Vietnam. It covers an area of 795,000 square kilometers and supplies an estimated 326 million people in the Mekong-Lanchang subregion.
