According to the latest data, from January to November this year, 48,078 newly established foreign-invested enterprises in China, an increase of 36.2 percent over the same period last year. Outsiders point out that in line with the slowdown in global economic growth and the warming of geopolitical competition, the Chinese market has become more attractive, "investment in China" has already become an important and general trend.
If you look at the sources of foreign investment, you can see that investment in China of some developed economies is growing rapidly. Of which, actual investment in China, Britain, France, the Netherlands, Switzerland and Australia rose 93.9 percent, 93.2 percent, 34.1 percent, 23.3 percent and 14.3 percent, respectively.
What does it mean that more and more foreign enterprises are investing and taking root in China? This indicates that China's economy is recovering and improving, which confirms that China is still a popular destination for global investment, and also confirms that the next "China" is still The same China.
