Land cover crops in Battambang province not only contribute to improving the quality of fertile soil, but also improve people's livelihood.
(Battambang): Many types of ground cover crops that people in Battambang province cultivate not only contribute to improving the quality of the soil to be fertile, it also helps to improve the livelihood of the people through the cultivation of these crops. According to agricultural experts.
He said that when the land loses its livelihood, it loses its yield, which in turn encourages him to use pesticides, which increase costs from year to year. In addition, it affects health and changes the environment.
He said that because of the impact, the General Department of Agricultural Land Management, in collaboration with the Center for Research and International, has started to carry out conservation work, which is to make the soil more fertile through the use of cover crops. There are many types.
According to the technical expert, when planting cover crops can help improve soil quality as a fertilizer. This type of crop not only helps to improve the quality of the soil, it also helps agriculture to earn more income.
At the same time, Mr. Sor Veng also said that ground cover crops also contribute to the environment by helping to capture household gases into the soil. In addition, this type of crop helps the economic benefits, people get money. Immediately too.
According to Mr. Sar Veng, there is currently a strong market for ground cover crops in the country and also exported to foreign countries. He added that this cover crop is not only needed in our country, but globally, they also use this type of crop to improve the quality of their soil.
Regarding the price, Mr. Sar Veng added that for the cultivation of this type of crop, the price is also negotiated with the buyer company when the farmers plant, because this type of crop is difficult to grow without a buyer.
At the same time, Mr. Lim Sokhom, a farmer living in Reaksmey Sanghar village, Reaksmey Sanghar commune, Rattanak Mondul district, Battambang province, said that today he grows crops such as corn, beans, potatoes, while growing cover crops such as monkeys, monkeys, small leaves, large leaves. Original.
According to the farmer, he grows 10 hectares of land with a household income, for example, he can get between 7 and 8 tons per hectare.
"For this crop, we can get money to support the family, that is, can continue to cultivate," he said.
Please be informed that the ground cover crops are: small-leaved monkeys, millet, cantoel, soybeans, rice, large-leaved monkeys, etc.
