Articles and pictures by Cambodia-China Friendship Radio This year at the Victory Monument there will be fireworks, exhibitions of products and programs to celebrate the 25th anniversary of the end of the war in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): 2023 is the 25th anniversary of the end of the Cambodian Civil War through the successful implementation of win-win politics, bringing peace and national reconciliation to the motherland of Cambodia to the present.
The 25th anniversary of the end of the Cambodian war will be marked by a series of events to celebrate a historic day in Cambodian society. The event will run for three days, from December 29, 30 and 31, 2023, accompanied by fireworks, product exhibitions and more.
To mark the 25th anniversary of the end of the civil war in Cambodia and the successful implementation of win-win politics and the 5th anniversary of the Victory Monument, General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Lead a meeting to review the work of organizing this celebration at the Victory Monument.
General Ith Sarath said that for December 29, 2023, there will be a gathering with 6,604 people, including more than 500 national and international guests. There are 5 military forces, 2 national police forces, 1 bokator plan, 1 unit of the USSR plan, scouts, Red Cross plan, Royal Government officials and many people.
General Ith Sarath continued: "The ceremony on December 29 will be presided over by Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. In addition to the event, we also organize exhibitions with a number of ministries, institutions and units, which ministries and institutions organize exhibitions of 25 achievements of 25 years, and in addition to these 50 exhibitions, we also organize exhibitions of products and Our food.
According to General Ith Sarath, to celebrate the 25th anniversary of the end of the civil war in Cambodia and the successful implementation of the win-win policy and the 5th anniversary of the Victory Monument, the Ministry of Tourism has set up a product exhibition booth. 250 Khmer food stalls and 250 Khmer food stalls.
General Ith Sarath confirmed that in addition to performing arts, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts will also hold a number of exhibitions featuring about 300 artists.
General Ith Sarath continued that the celebration of the 25th anniversary of the end of the civil war in Cambodia and the successful implementation of the win-win policy is a demonstration of the achievements of 25 years of peace to the people of Cambodia. All over the country, it is clear that peace is very valuable for the nation.
