(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise on December 25, 2023, confirmed that the Royal Government is preparing to adjust some conditions to allow the import of frozen meat. To improve the quality of the meat and avoid it, anyone can apply to import frozen meat.
This statement was made by Dr. Kun Nhem at a press conference after the forum to promote trade facilitation measures under customs jurisdiction. This conference was held on December 25, 2023 at the National Customs School.
Dr. Kun Nhem stated, "For the next step, the General Department of Customs and Cambodia will continue to work to crack down on the importation of damaged and illegal meat We propose to the Royal Government to determine who "To be able to import frozen meat, you have to have a cold storage, a clear business to avoid anyone can apply to import frozen meat."
The Director General said that in recent times, there have been many activities on social media related to the inspection of frozen meat warehouses.
He said that the current sub-decree 17, which is still in force, does not require a permit from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. Sub-Decree 17 clearly states that imported frozen meat is required to have an animal health certificate issued by the exporting country. Therefore, in the future, importers of frozen meat must have a permit issued by the Ministry of Agriculture, and international ports for importing frozen meat must also be clearly defined.
Regarding the import of frozen meat, Dr. Kun Nhim explained that meat farmers think about his business, but the Royal Government thinks not only about meat but also about the meat eater. If there is not enough livestock, it must be imported to fill the market so that meat or meat prices do not rise.
Dr. emphasized that international trade is within the rules set out in the World Trade Organization, so meat importers, if compliant, have the right to import and distribute.
(Sihanoukville): The Department of Welfare for the Disabled held a meeting to review the annual results of the Disability Identification Program based on social norms and fundamental rights and policies for poor people with disabilities in the community.
This annual review meeting was held for the purpose of disseminating the results of the disability identification program and the policy regime for persons with disabilities in 2024 and the plan for 2024, strengthening the implementation of the disability identification program, planning the use of the population database. Disability to promote access to vocational and technical training (TVET) for people with disabilities.
