(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia on the morning of December 25, 2023 organized a "Forum to promote trade facilitation measures under the jurisdiction of the Customs to the private sector" with the participation of officials of the General Department of Customs and Excise. Cambodia and the private sector as well.
Fourteen measures were presented at the 19th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum on November 13, 2023, chaired by His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to address the challenges and concerns of the private sector in relation to Cambodia. And promote economic growth.
This package of trade facilitation measures covers three main areas: reduction of public administration fees by the Customs Administration, import control and protection of public health, and digitalization of customs procedures and trade facilitation, and these measures will be implemented. From January 1, 2024 onwards.
Speaking on the occasion, Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, stated that through these 14 measures to be implemented, it provides good benefits for the private sector by reducing costs and streamlining procedures. Export-import, and this measure will make some customs revenue also lost.
"Overall, the government has made sacrifices to reduce costs in the form of related fees, willing to lose, but to ease the burden of the private sector," he said. "Profits from fee adjustments and deductions go to the private sector."
