(Battambang): Aid devices for natural disaster warning systems have been installed on the roof of Sangkat Slaket, Battambang City, Battambang Province to alert people living along the Sangke River in advance of natural disasters.
The city's early warning system is a new information channel to broadcast emergency messages to residents about floods and other hazards.
The city's early warning system is a good communication mechanism during emergencies such as floods and other natural disasters. The introduction of this information system is very important to be able to provide information that people understand and be prepared to respond to climate change such as floods.
The commune chief said the city's early warning system had an automatic microphone that could receive information from the provincial disaster management committee. This pre-announcement message can be sent to people in the community within a distance of about 500 square meters of the installed location.
After receiving the message, the microphone's automated control system sends the voicemail to the microphone's electronic beep, and people in the target area automatically hear the microphone announcement. An advance message can be sent to people in the community within 50 square meters of the installed location.
She confirmed that so far, in addition to being implemented in Slaket, there are three other locations in Battambang that are equipped with an early warning system to prevent natural disasters.
