Dr. Soeur Socheata, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, reported on the activities and good cooperation with the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs in organizing this anti-drug library to facilitate public education to understand the drug problem.
According to Zhang Chheang, China continues to implement the principle of mutual assistance and support in the fight against drugs as a comprehensive friendship between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Chinese government in the form of a diamond friendship.
On that occasion, Mr. Chuon Chivin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, on behalf of Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister, praised and thanked all stakeholders, especially the Government of the People's Republic of China, for implementing the principle of comprehensive friendship between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government. China in the form of diamond friendship really makes Cambodia-China shining like diamonds and precious.
He claimed that this anti-drug library is really a nursery to strengthen knowledge, participate in prevention and reduction of drug-related problems, protect human resources for national development in line with the national development goals of Cambodia. Deputy Director of Kampong Speu Provincial Prison. Clarify the case of Li Meiing's demolition before the contract after the misunderstanding on social media
(Kampong Speu): Mrs. To Sokly, Deputy Director of Kampong Speu Provincial Prison, came out to clarify the case of the demolition of Ly Mey Eng Company in Phum Nhor, Sangkat Kandol Doum, Chbar Morn City, Kampong Speu Province, which caused confusion on social media when the company That did not work.
"After the company was operating for a while, I saw that my company was not doing well and I decided to suspend the company for a while," the statement said. Before deciding to dismantle the company, I informed Hean Phanna but could not contact him and I went to his house but did not see him at any house at work and did not see him come to work without knowing "Where did he go to live?"
(Battambang): Mr. Seng Chheng, former advisor to the Executive Committee of the Battambang Provincial CNRP, decided to join the political life with the Cambodian People's Party. The decision comes after Seng Chheng despaired of leading an opposition party that lacked unity and deepened internal divisions.
In a video message asking Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party to participate in political life, Mr. Seng Chheng highlighted that only the Cambodian People's Party has a good unity and has built many achievements for the nation.
